INSERT INTO s505_cards VALUES
(57915, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 17, 4, $n$Or wherein did Moses suffer loss in that he lived only one hundred and twenty years, and, inasmuch as he was subject to Him who formed him, brought the law to the seed of Jacob, and lighted a lamp for the nation of Yashar'el (Israel)?'$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 6, 23, $n$Prov 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the commandment itself the lamp Moses lit.$n$, $n$Proverbs 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the commandment itself the lamp Moses lit.$n$, 14098, $n$Prov 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the commandment itself the lamp Moses lit.$n$, $n$Proverbs 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the commandment itself the lamp Moses lit.$n$),
(57916, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 17, 4, $n$Or wherein did Moses suffer loss in that he lived only one hundred and twenty years, and, inasmuch as he was subject to Him who formed him, brought the law to the seed of Jacob, and lighted a lamp for the nation of Yashar'el (Israel)?'$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 119, 105, $n$Ps 119:105 — *Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path* — the law as the lamp Baruch says Moses lighted for Israel.$n$, $n$Psalm 119:105 — *Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path* — the law as the lamp Baruch says Moses lighted for Israel.$n$, 14098, $n$Ps 119:105 — *Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path* — the law as the lamp Baruch says Moses lighted for Israel.$n$, $n$Psalm 119:105 — *Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path* — the law as the lamp Baruch says Moses lighted for Israel.$n$),
(57917, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 17, 3, $n$Therefore the multitude of time that he lived did not profit him, but brought death and cut off the years of those who were born from him.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 5, 14, $n$Rom 5:14 — *Nevertheless death reigned from Adam to Moses, even over them that had not sinned after the similitude of Adam's transgression* — death reigning over Adam's seed, as Baruch says his years were cut off.$n$, $n$Romans 5:14 — *Nevertheless death reigned from Adam to Moses, even over them that had not sinned after the similitude of Adam's transgression* — death reigning over Adam's seed, as Baruch says his years were cut off.$n$, 14097, $n$Rom 5:14 — *Nevertheless death reigned from Adam to Moses, even over them that had not sinned after the similitude of Adam's transgression* — death reigning over Adam's seed, as Baruch says his years were cut off.$n$, $n$Romans 5:14 — *Nevertheless death reigned from Adam to Moses, even over them that had not sinned after the similitude of Adam's transgression* — death reigning over Adam's seed, as Baruch says his years were cut off.$n$),
(57918, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 17, 2, $n$For what did it profit Adam that he lived nine hundred and thirty years, and transgressed that which he was commanded?$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 5, 12, $n$Rom 5:12 — *Wherefore, as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned* — death entering by the one man's transgression, the same root Baruch names.$n$, $n$Romans 5:12 — *Wherefore, as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned* — death entering by the one man's transgression, the same root Baruch names.$n$, 14097, $n$Rom 5:12 — *Wherefore, as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned* — death entering by the one man's transgression, the same root Baruch names.$n$, $n$Romans 5:12 — *Wherefore, as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned* — death entering by the one man's transgression, the same root Baruch names.$n$),
(57921, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 18, 1, $n$And I answered and said: 'He that lighted has taken from the light, and there are but few that have imitated him.$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 6, 23, $n$Prov 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the lamp of the law that few imitate.$n$, $n$Proverbs 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the lamp of the law that few imitate.$n$, 14099, $n$Prov 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the lamp of the law that few imitate.$n$, $n$Proverbs 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the lamp of the law that few imitate.$n$),
(57922, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 19, 5, $n$For now it is the consummation of time that should be considered, whether of business, or of prosperity, or of shame, and not the beginning thereof.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 32, 29, $n$Deut 32:29 — *O that they were wise, that they understood this, that they would consider their latter end!* — the very weighing of the end, not the beginning, that Baruch is told to make.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:29 — *O that they were wise, that they understood this, that they would consider their latter end!* — the very weighing of the end, not the beginning, that Baruch is told to make.$n$, 14101, $n$Deut 32:29 — *O that they were wise, that they understood this, that they would consider their latter end!* — the very weighing of the end, not the beginning, that Baruch is told to make.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:29 — *O that they were wise, that they understood this, that they would consider their latter end!* — the very weighing of the end, not the beginning, that Baruch is told to make.$n$),
(57923, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 19, 3, $n$But after his death they sinned and transgressed, Though they knew that they had the law reproving (them), And the light in which nothing could err, Also the spheres which testify, and Me.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 32, 1, $n$Deut 32:1 — *Give ear, O ye heavens, and I will speak; and hear, O earth, the words of my mouth* — the abiding heaven-and-earth witness that, Baruch says, testifies against those who transgressed.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:1 — *Give ear, O ye heavens, and I will speak; and hear, O earth, the words of my mouth* — the abiding heaven-and-earth witness that, Baruch says, testifies against those who transgressed.$n$, 14100, $n$Deut 32:1 — *Give ear, O ye heavens, and I will speak; and hear, O earth, the words of my mouth* — the abiding heaven-and-earth witness that, Baruch says, testifies against those who transgressed.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:1 — *Give ear, O ye heavens, and I will speak; and hear, O earth, the words of my mouth* — the abiding heaven-and-earth witness that, Baruch says, testifies against those who transgressed.$n$),
(57924, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 19, 1, $n$And He answered and said unto me: 'Wherefore at that time he appointed for them a covenant and said: "Behold I have placed before you life and death," And he called heaven and earth to witness against them.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 15, $n$Deut 30:15 — *See, I have set before thee this day life and good, and death and evil* — the choice set before the nation that Baruch repeats.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:15 — *See, I have set before thee this day life and good, and death and evil* — the choice set before the nation that Baruch repeats.$n$, 14100, $n$Deut 30:15 — *See, I have set before thee this day life and good, and death and evil* — the choice set before the nation that Baruch repeats.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:15 — *See, I have set before thee this day life and good, and death and evil* — the choice set before the nation that Baruch repeats.$n$),
(57925, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 19, 1, $n$And He answered and said unto me: 'Wherefore at that time he appointed for them a covenant and said: "Behold I have placed before you life and death," And he called heaven and earth to witness against them.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 19, $n$Deut 30:19 — *I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life* — the exact covenant words and witnesses Baruch ascribes to Moses.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:19 — *I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life* — the exact covenant words and witnesses Baruch ascribes to Moses.$n$, 14100, $n$Deut 30:19 — *I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life* — the exact covenant words and witnesses Baruch ascribes to Moses.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:19 — *I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life* — the exact covenant words and witnesses Baruch ascribes to Moses.$n$),
(57926, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 20, 3, $n$Now therefore hold fast in thy heart everything that I command thee, And seal it in the recesses of thy mind.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 14, $n$Deut 30:14 — *But the word is very nigh unto thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart, that thou mayest do it* — the word sealed in the heart that Baruch is told to hold fast.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:14 — *But the word is very nigh unto thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart, that thou mayest do it* — the word sealed in the heart that Baruch is told to hold fast.$n$, 14103, $n$Deut 30:14 — *But the word is very nigh unto thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart, that thou mayest do it* — the word sealed in the heart that Baruch is told to hold fast.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:14 — *But the word is very nigh unto thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart, that thou mayest do it* — the word sealed in the heart that Baruch is told to hold fast.$n$),
(57930, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 21, 24, $n$For there have been many years like those that are desolate from the days of Abraham and Isaac and Jacob, and of all those who are like them, who sleep in the earth, on whose account Thou didst say that Thou hadst created the world.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 4, 17, $n$Rom 4:17 — *Elohim, who quickeneth the dead* — the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob who quickens those who sleep in the earth, as Baruch pleads.$n$, $n$Romans 4:17 — *Elohim, who quickeneth the dead* — the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob who quickens those who sleep in the earth, as Baruch pleads.$n$, 14106, $n$Rom 4:17 — *Elohim, who quickeneth the dead* — the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob who quickens those who sleep in the earth, as Baruch pleads.$n$, $n$Romans 4:17 — *Elohim, who quickeneth the dead* — the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob who quickens those who sleep in the earth, as Baruch pleads.$n$),
(57933, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 21, 6, $n$Thou that rulest with great thought the hosts that stand before Thee: also the countless holy beings, which Thou didst make from the beginning, of flame and fire, which stand around Thy throne$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 40, 26, $n$Isa 40:26 — *behold who hath created these things, that bringeth out their host by number: he calleth them all by names* — the host made and ruled by Him whom Baruch addresses.$n$, $n$Isaiah 40:26 — *behold who hath created these things, that bringeth out their host by number: he calleth them all by names* — the host made and ruled by Him whom Baruch addresses.$n$, 14105, $n$Isa 40:26 — *behold who hath created these things, that bringeth out their host by number: he calleth them all by names* — the host made and ruled by Him whom Baruch addresses.$n$, $n$Isaiah 40:26 — *behold who hath created these things, that bringeth out their host by number: he calleth them all by names* — the host made and ruled by Him whom Baruch addresses.$n$),
(57934, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 21, 6, $n$Thou that rulest with great thought the hosts that stand before Thee: also the countless holy beings, which Thou didst make from the beginning, of flame and fire, which stand around Thy throne$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 7, 10, $n$Dan 7:10 — *thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him* — the countless hosts of fire that stand before the throne, as Baruch beholds them.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:10 — *thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him* — the countless hosts of fire that stand before the throne, as Baruch beholds them.$n$, 14105, $n$Dan 7:10 — *thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him* — the countless hosts of fire that stand before the throne, as Baruch beholds them.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:10 — *thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him* — the countless hosts of fire that stand before the throne, as Baruch beholds them.$n$),
(57935, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 21, 4, $n$'O Thou that hast made the earth, hear me, that hast fixed the firmament by the word, and hast made firm the height of the heaven by the spirit, that hast called from the beginning of the world that which did not yet exist, and they obey Thee.$n$, 'canon', 'hebrews', 11, 3, $n$Heb 11:3 — *the worlds were framed by the word of Elohim, so that things which are seen were not made of things which do appear* — the firmament fixed by the word, as Baruch prays.$n$, $n$Hebrews 11:3 — *the worlds were framed by the word of Elohim, so that things which are seen were not made of things which do appear* — the firmament fixed by the word, as Baruch prays.$n$, 14104, $n$Heb 11:3 — *the worlds were framed by the word of Elohim, so that things which are seen were not made of things which do appear* — the firmament fixed by the word, as Baruch prays.$n$, $n$Hebrews 11:3 — *the worlds were framed by the word of Elohim, so that things which are seen were not made of things which do appear* — the firmament fixed by the word, as Baruch prays.$n$),
(57936, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 21, 4, $n$'O Thou that hast made the earth, hear me, that hast fixed the firmament by the word, and hast made firm the height of the heaven by the spirit, that hast called from the beginning of the world that which did not yet exist, and they obey Thee.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 4, 17, $n$Rom 4:17 — *even Elohim, who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were* — the very God who calls the non-existent into being whom Baruch invokes.$n$, $n$Romans 4:17 — *even Elohim, who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were* — the very God who calls the non-existent into being whom Baruch invokes.$n$, 14104, $n$Rom 4:17 — *even Elohim, who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were* — the very God who calls the non-existent into being whom Baruch invokes.$n$, $n$Romans 4:17 — *even Elohim, who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were* — the very God who calls the non-existent into being whom Baruch invokes.$n$),
(57940, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 23, 4, $n$Before therefore the number aforesaid is fulfilled, the creature will not live again [for My spirit is the creator of life], and Sheol will receive the dead.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 6, 11, $n$Rev 6:11 — *they should rest yet for a little season, until their fellowservants also and their brethren... should be fulfilled* — the appointed number that must first be completed before the end, as Baruch says the creature will not live again till the number is fulfilled.$n$, $n$Revelation 6:11 — *they should rest yet for a little season, until their fellowservants also and their brethren... should be fulfilled* — the appointed number that must first be completed before the end, as Baruch says the creature will not live again till the number is fulfilled.$n$, 14109, $n$Rev 6:11 — *they should rest yet for a little season, until their fellowservants also and their brethren... should be fulfilled* — the appointed number that must first be completed before the end, as Baruch says the creature will not live again till the number is fulfilled.$n$, $n$Revelation 6:11 — *they should rest yet for a little season, until their fellowservants also and their brethren... should be fulfilled* — the appointed number that must first be completed before the end, as Baruch says the creature will not live again till the number is fulfilled.$n$),
(57941, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 23, 3, $n$Because when Adam sinned and death was decreed against those who should be born, then the multitude of those who should be born was numbered, and for that number a place was prepared where the living might dwell and the dead might be guarded.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 5, 12, $n$Rom 5:12 — *as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men* — the decree of death at Adam's sin that Baruch names as the start of the numbering.$n$, $n$Romans 5:12 — *as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men* — the decree of death at Adam's sin that Baruch names as the start of the numbering.$n$, 14109, $n$Rom 5:12 — *as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men* — the decree of death at Adam's sin that Baruch names as the start of the numbering.$n$, $n$Romans 5:12 — *as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men* — the decree of death at Adam's sin that Baruch names as the start of the numbering.$n$),
(57943, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 24, 1, $n$'For behold! the days come and the books shall be opened in which are written the sins of all those who have sinned, and again also the treasuries in which the righteousness of all those who have been righteous in creation is gathered.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 32, 34, $n$Deut 32:34 — *Is not this laid up in store with me, and sealed up among my treasures?* — the treasuries where the record is laid up against the day, as Baruch's treasuries of righteousness.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:34 — *Is not this laid up in store with me, and sealed up among my treasures?* — the treasuries where the record is laid up against the day, as Baruch's treasuries of righteousness.$n$, 14111, $n$Deut 32:34 — *Is not this laid up in store with me, and sealed up among my treasures?* — the treasuries where the record is laid up against the day, as Baruch's treasuries of righteousness.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:34 — *Is not this laid up in store with me, and sealed up among my treasures?* — the treasuries where the record is laid up against the day, as Baruch's treasuries of righteousness.$n$),
(57944, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 24, 1, $n$'For behold! the days come and the books shall be opened in which are written the sins of all those who have sinned, and again also the treasuries in which the righteousness of all those who have been righteous in creation is gathered.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 20, 12, $n$Rev 20:12 — *and the books were opened... and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works* — the books of sins and the gathered righteousness Baruch names.$n$, $n$Revelation 20:12 — *and the books were opened... and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works* — the books of sins and the gathered righteousness Baruch names.$n$, 14111, $n$Rev 20:12 — *and the books were opened... and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works* — the books of sins and the gathered righteousness Baruch names.$n$, $n$Revelation 20:12 — *and the books were opened... and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works* — the books of sins and the gathered righteousness Baruch names.$n$),
(57945, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 24, 1, $n$'For behold! the days come and the books shall be opened in which are written the sins of all those who have sinned, and again also the treasuries in which the righteousness of all those who have been righteous in creation is gathered.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 7, 10, $n$Dan 7:10 — *the judgment was set, and the books were opened* — the very opening of the books at the consummation that Baruch foretells.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:10 — *the judgment was set, and the books were opened* — the very opening of the books at the consummation that Baruch foretells.$n$, 14111, $n$Dan 7:10 — *the judgment was set, and the books were opened* — the very opening of the books at the consummation that Baruch foretells.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:10 — *the judgment was set, and the books were opened* — the very opening of the books at the consummation that Baruch foretells.$n$),
(58016, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 39, 7, $n$And it will come to pass when the time of its consummation that it should fall has approached, then the principate of My Messiah will be revealed, which is like the fountain and the vine, and when it is revealed it will root out the multitude of its host.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 2, 6, $n$Ps 2:6 — *Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion* — the Anointed installed by the Father, the principate revealed that Baruch names My Messiah.$n$, $n$Psalm 2:6 — *Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion* — the Anointed installed by the Father, the principate revealed that Baruch names My Messiah.$n$, 14142, $n$Ps 2:6 — *Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion* — the Anointed installed by the Father, the principate revealed that Baruch names My Messiah.$n$, $n$Psalm 2:6 — *Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion* — the Anointed installed by the Father, the principate revealed that Baruch names My Messiah.$n$),
(58017, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 39, 7, $n$And it will come to pass when the time of its consummation that it should fall has approached, then the principate of My Messiah will be revealed, which is like the fountain and the vine, and when it is revealed it will root out the multitude of its host.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 1, $n$Isa 11:1 — *And there shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots* — the shoot of David's hope, the vine and fountain Baruch sees rise as the Messiah's principate.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:1 — *And there shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots* — the shoot of David's hope, the vine and fountain Baruch sees rise as the Messiah's principate.$n$, 14142, $n$Isa 11:1 — *And there shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots* — the shoot of David's hope, the vine and fountain Baruch sees rise as the Messiah's principate.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:1 — *And there shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots* — the shoot of David's hope, the vine and fountain Baruch sees rise as the Messiah's principate.$n$),
(58018, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 39, 7, $n$And it will come to pass when the time of its consummation that it should fall has approached, then the principate of My Messiah will be revealed, which is like the fountain and the vine, and when it is revealed it will root out the multitude of its host.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 2, 44, $n$Dan 2:44 — *And in the days of these kings shall the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed... it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand for ever* — the kingdom revealed at the empires' end, Baruch's principate of the Messiah.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:44 — *And in the days of these kings shall the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed... it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand for ever* — the kingdom revealed at the empires' end, Baruch's principate of the Messiah.$n$, 14142, $n$Dan 2:44 — *And in the days of these kings shall the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed... it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand for ever* — the kingdom revealed at the empires' end, Baruch's principate of the Messiah.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:44 — *And in the days of these kings shall the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed... it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand for ever* — the kingdom revealed at the empires' end, Baruch's principate of the Messiah.$n$),
(58019, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 39, 7, $n$And it will come to pass when the time of its consummation that it should fall has approached, then the principate of My Messiah will be revealed, which is like the fountain and the vine, and when it is revealed it will root out the multitude of its host.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 2, 34, $n$Dan 2:34 — *Thou sawest till that a stone was cut out without hands, which smote the image upon his feet that were of iron and clay, and brake them to pieces* — the stone that smites the last kingdom at its hour, as the Messiah roots out the fourth kingdom's host.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:34 — *Thou sawest till that a stone was cut out without hands, which smote the image upon his feet that were of iron and clay, and brake them to pieces* — the stone that smites the last kingdom at its hour, as the Messiah roots out the fourth kingdom's host.$n$, 14142, $n$Dan 2:34 — *Thou sawest till that a stone was cut out without hands, which smote the image upon his feet that were of iron and clay, and brake them to pieces* — the stone that smites the last kingdom at its hour, as the Messiah roots out the fourth kingdom's host.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:34 — *Thou sawest till that a stone was cut out without hands, which smote the image upon his feet that were of iron and clay, and brake them to pieces* — the stone that smites the last kingdom at its hour, as the Messiah roots out the fourth kingdom's host.$n$),
(58020, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 39, 3, $n$Behold! the days come, and this kingdom will be destroyed which once destroyed Zion, and it will be subjected to that which comes after it.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 7, 17, $n$Dan 7:17 — *These great beasts, which are four, are four kings, which shall arise out of the earth* — four kingdoms arising in succession, the frame Baruch's angel interprets.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:17 — *These great beasts, which are four, are four kings, which shall arise out of the earth* — four kingdoms arising in succession, the frame Baruch's angel interprets.$n$, 14141, $n$Dan 7:17 — *These great beasts, which are four, are four kings, which shall arise out of the earth* — four kingdoms arising in succession, the frame Baruch's angel interprets.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:17 — *These great beasts, which are four, are four kings, which shall arise out of the earth* — four kingdoms arising in succession, the frame Baruch's angel interprets.$n$),
(58021, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 39, 5, $n$And after these things a fourth kingdom will arise, whose power will be harsh and evil far beyond those which were before it, and it will rule many times as the forests on the plain, and it will hold fast for times, and will exalt itself more than the cedars of Lebanon.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 7, 7, $n$Dan 7:7 — *behold a fourth beast, dreadful and terrible, and strong exceedingly... it devoured and brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with the feet of it: and it was diverse from all the beasts that were before it* — the fourth beast more evil than all before it, Baruch's fourth kingdom in Daniel's other vision.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:7 — *behold a fourth beast, dreadful and terrible, and strong exceedingly... it devoured and brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with the feet of it: and it was diverse from all the beasts that were before it* — the fourth beast more evil than all before it, Baruch's fourth kingdom in Daniel's other vision.$n$, 14141, $n$Dan 7:7 — *behold a fourth beast, dreadful and terrible, and strong exceedingly... it devoured and brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with the feet of it: and it was diverse from all the beasts that were before it* — the fourth beast more evil than all before it, Baruch's fourth kingdom in Daniel's other vision.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:7 — *behold a fourth beast, dreadful and terrible, and strong exceedingly... it devoured and brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with the feet of it: and it was diverse from all the beasts that were before it* — the fourth beast more evil than all before it, Baruch's fourth kingdom in Daniel's other vision.$n$),
(58022, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 39, 5, $n$And after these things a fourth kingdom will arise, whose power will be harsh and evil far beyond those which were before it, and it will rule many times as the forests on the plain, and it will hold fast for times, and will exalt itself more than the cedars of Lebanon.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 2, 40, $n$Dan 2:40 — *And the fourth kingdom shall be strong as iron: forasmuch as iron breaketh in pieces and subdueth all things... shall it break in pieces and bruise* — the harsh fourth kingdom far beyond the rest, the same Baruch names.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:40 — *And the fourth kingdom shall be strong as iron: forasmuch as iron breaketh in pieces and subdueth all things... shall it break in pieces and bruise* — the harsh fourth kingdom far beyond the rest, the same Baruch names.$n$, 14141, $n$Dan 2:40 — *And the fourth kingdom shall be strong as iron: forasmuch as iron breaketh in pieces and subdueth all things... shall it break in pieces and bruise* — the harsh fourth kingdom far beyond the rest, the same Baruch names.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:40 — *And the fourth kingdom shall be strong as iron: forasmuch as iron breaketh in pieces and subdueth all things... shall it break in pieces and bruise* — the harsh fourth kingdom far beyond the rest, the same Baruch names.$n$),
(58023, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 39, 4, $n$Moreover, that also again after a time will be destroyed, and another, a third, will arise, and that also will have dominion for its time, and will be destroyed.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 2, 39, $n$Dan 2:39 — *And after thee shall arise another kingdom inferior to thee, and another third kingdom of brass, which shall bear rule over all the earth* — the second and third kingdoms succeeding, as Baruch's vision counts them off.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:39 — *And after thee shall arise another kingdom inferior to thee, and another third kingdom of brass, which shall bear rule over all the earth* — the second and third kingdoms succeeding, as Baruch's vision counts them off.$n$, 14141, $n$Dan 2:39 — *And after thee shall arise another kingdom inferior to thee, and another third kingdom of brass, which shall bear rule over all the earth* — the second and third kingdoms succeeding, as Baruch's vision counts them off.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:39 — *And after thee shall arise another kingdom inferior to thee, and another third kingdom of brass, which shall bear rule over all the earth* — the second and third kingdoms succeeding, as Baruch's vision counts them off.$n$),
(58024, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 40, 3, $n$And his principate will stand for ever, until the world of corruption is at an end, and until the times aforesaid are fulfilled.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 2, 44, $n$Dan 2:44 — *shall the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed... and it shall stand for ever* — the kingdom that stands for ever, the very promise Baruch makes of the Messiah's principate.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:44 — *shall the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed... and it shall stand for ever* — the kingdom that stands for ever, the very promise Baruch makes of the Messiah's principate.$n$, 14144, $n$Dan 2:44 — *shall the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed... and it shall stand for ever* — the kingdom that stands for ever, the very promise Baruch makes of the Messiah's principate.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:44 — *shall the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed... and it shall stand for ever* — the kingdom that stands for ever, the very promise Baruch makes of the Messiah's principate.$n$),
(58025, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 40, 3, $n$And his principate will stand for ever, until the world of corruption is at an end, and until the times aforesaid are fulfilled.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 7, 27, $n$Dan 7:27 — *whose kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and all dominions shall serve and obey him* — the enduring kingdom given to the saints under their King, the dominion Baruch says will stand for ever.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:27 — *whose kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and all dominions shall serve and obey him* — the enduring kingdom given to the saints under their King, the dominion Baruch says will stand for ever.$n$, 14144, $n$Dan 7:27 — *whose kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and all dominions shall serve and obey him* — the enduring kingdom given to the saints under their King, the dominion Baruch says will stand for ever.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:27 — *whose kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and all dominions shall serve and obey him* — the enduring kingdom given to the saints under their King, the dominion Baruch says will stand for ever.$n$),
(58026, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 40, 3, $n$And his principate will stand for ever, until the world of corruption is at an end, and until the times aforesaid are fulfilled.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 7, 14, $n$Dan 7:14 — *And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom... his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed* — the principate that stands for ever, Baruch's word for the Messiah's reign.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:14 — *And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom... his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed* — the principate that stands for ever, Baruch's word for the Messiah's reign.$n$, 14144, $n$Dan 7:14 — *And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom... his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed* — the principate that stands for ever, Baruch's word for the Messiah's reign.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:14 — *And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom... his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed* — the principate that stands for ever, Baruch's word for the Messiah's reign.$n$),
(58027, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 40, 1, $n$'The last leader of that time will be left alive, when the multitude of his hosts will be put to the sword, and he will be bound, and they will take him up to Mount Zion, and My Messiah will convict him of all his impieties, and will gather and set before him all the works of his hosts.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 19, 20, $n$Rev 19:20 — *And the beast was taken, and with him the false prophet... These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone* — the last leader taken and his host destroyed, as Baruch's vision ends.$n$, $n$Revelation 19:20 — *And the beast was taken, and with him the false prophet... These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone* — the last leader taken and his host destroyed, as Baruch's vision ends.$n$, 14143, $n$Rev 19:20 — *And the beast was taken, and with him the false prophet... These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone* — the last leader taken and his host destroyed, as Baruch's vision ends.$n$, $n$Revelation 19:20 — *And the beast was taken, and with him the false prophet... These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone* — the last leader taken and his host destroyed, as Baruch's vision ends.$n$),
(58028, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 40, 1, $n$'The last leader of that time will be left alive, when the multitude of his hosts will be put to the sword, and he will be bound, and they will take him up to Mount Zion, and My Messiah will convict him of all his impieties, and will gather and set before him all the works of his hosts.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 7, 11, $n$Dan 7:11 — *I beheld even till the beast was slain, and his body destroyed, and given to the burning flame* — the last ruler convicted and put to death, Baruch's leader taken up to Zion and slain.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:11 — *I beheld even till the beast was slain, and his body destroyed, and given to the burning flame* — the last ruler convicted and put to death, Baruch's leader taken up to Zion and slain.$n$, 14143, $n$Dan 7:11 — *I beheld even till the beast was slain, and his body destroyed, and given to the burning flame* — the last ruler convicted and put to death, Baruch's leader taken up to Zion and slain.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:11 — *I beheld even till the beast was slain, and his body destroyed, and given to the burning flame* — the last ruler convicted and put to death, Baruch's leader taken up to Zion and slain.$n$),
(58030, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 40, 2, $n$And afterwards he will put him to death, and protect the rest of My people which shall be found in the place which I have chosen.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 4, $n$Isa 11:4 — *he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Anointed putting the impious ruler to death, exactly the deed Baruch's Messiah does on Zion.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:4 — *he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Anointed putting the impious ruler to death, exactly the deed Baruch's Messiah does on Zion.$n$, 14143, $n$Isa 11:4 — *he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Anointed putting the impious ruler to death, exactly the deed Baruch's Messiah does on Zion.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:4 — *he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Anointed putting the impious ruler to death, exactly the deed Baruch's Messiah does on Zion.$n$),
(58032, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 41, 4, $n$But others again I have seen who have forsaken their vanity, and fled for refuge beneath Thy wings.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 56, 6, $n$Isa 56:6 — *Also the sons of the stranger, that join themselves to Yahuah (LORD), to serve him... that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and taketh hold of my covenant* — the stranger who takes up the covenant, the ones Baruch sees fled for refuge.$n$, $n$Isaiah 56:6 — *Also the sons of the stranger, that join themselves to Yahuah (LORD), to serve him... that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and taketh hold of my covenant* — the stranger who takes up the covenant, the ones Baruch sees fled for refuge.$n$, 14145, $n$Isa 56:6 — *Also the sons of the stranger, that join themselves to Yahuah (LORD), to serve him... that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and taketh hold of my covenant* — the stranger who takes up the covenant, the ones Baruch sees fled for refuge.$n$, $n$Isaiah 56:6 — *Also the sons of the stranger, that join themselves to Yahuah (LORD), to serve him... that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and taketh hold of my covenant* — the stranger who takes up the covenant, the ones Baruch sees fled for refuge.$n$),
(58033, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 41, 4, $n$But others again I have seen who have forsaken their vanity, and fled for refuge beneath Thy wings.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 11, 17, $n$Rom 11:17 — *And if some of the branches be broken off, and thou, being a wild olive tree, wert graffed in among them, and with them partakest of the root and fatness of the olive tree* — the stranger grafted in, Baruch's refugees fled beneath the wings.$n$, $n$Romans 11:17 — *And if some of the branches be broken off, and thou, being a wild olive tree, wert graffed in among them, and with them partakest of the root and fatness of the olive tree* — the stranger grafted in, Baruch's refugees fled beneath the wings.$n$, 14145, $n$Rom 11:17 — *And if some of the branches be broken off, and thou, being a wild olive tree, wert graffed in among them, and with them partakest of the root and fatness of the olive tree* — the stranger grafted in, Baruch's refugees fled beneath the wings.$n$, $n$Romans 11:17 — *And if some of the branches be broken off, and thou, being a wild olive tree, wert graffed in among them, and with them partakest of the root and fatness of the olive tree* — the stranger grafted in, Baruch's refugees fled beneath the wings.$n$),
(58034, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 41, 3, $n$For lo! I see many of Thy people who have withdrawn from Thy covenant, and cast from them the yoke of Thy law.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 11, 20, $n$Rom 11:20 — *because of unbelief they were broken off, and thou standest by faith. Be not highminded, but fear* — the natural branches broken off, Baruch's people who cast off the yoke of the law.$n$, $n$Romans 11:20 — *because of unbelief they were broken off, and thou standest by faith. Be not highminded, but fear* — the natural branches broken off, Baruch's people who cast off the yoke of the law.$n$, 14145, $n$Rom 11:20 — *because of unbelief they were broken off, and thou standest by faith. Be not highminded, but fear* — the natural branches broken off, Baruch's people who cast off the yoke of the law.$n$, $n$Romans 11:20 — *because of unbelief they were broken off, and thou standest by faith. Be not highminded, but fear* — the natural branches broken off, Baruch's people who cast off the yoke of the law.$n$),
(58035, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 42, 7, $n$For corruption shall take those that belong to it, and life those that belong to it.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 26, 19, $n$Isa 26:19 — *Thy dead men shall live, together with my dead body shall they arise. Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust... and the earth shall cast out the dead* — the earth casting out its dead, the very giving-back Baruch commands of the dust.$n$, $n$Isaiah 26:19 — *Thy dead men shall live, together with my dead body shall they arise. Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust... and the earth shall cast out the dead* — the earth casting out its dead, the very giving-back Baruch commands of the dust.$n$, 14147, $n$Isa 26:19 — *Thy dead men shall live, together with my dead body shall they arise. Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust... and the earth shall cast out the dead* — the earth casting out its dead, the very giving-back Baruch commands of the dust.$n$, $n$Isaiah 26:19 — *Thy dead men shall live, together with my dead body shall they arise. Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust... and the earth shall cast out the dead* — the earth casting out its dead, the very giving-back Baruch commands of the dust.$n$),
(58036, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 42, 8, $n$And the dust shall be called, and there shall be said to it: "Give back that which is not thine, and raise up all that thou hast kept until its time".'$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 12, 2, $n$Dan 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the dust commanded to give back its dead, Baruch's word that the grave must raise up what it kept.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the dust commanded to give back its dead, Baruch's word that the grave must raise up what it kept.$n$, 14147, $n$Dan 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the dust commanded to give back its dead, Baruch's word that the grave must raise up what it kept.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the dust commanded to give back its dead, Baruch's word that the grave must raise up what it kept.$n$),
(58037, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 42, 4, $n$As for those who were before subject, and afterwards withdrew and mingled themselves with the seed of mingled peoples, the time of these was the former, and was accounted as something exalted.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 11, 23, $n$Rom 11:23 — *And they also, if they abide not still in unbelief, shall be graffed in: for Elohim (God) is able to graff them in again* — withdrawal and return both possible, the same weighing of times Baruch describes.$n$, $n$Romans 11:23 — *And they also, if they abide not still in unbelief, shall be graffed in: for Elohim (God) is able to graff them in again* — withdrawal and return both possible, the same weighing of times Baruch describes.$n$, 14146, $n$Rom 11:23 — *And they also, if they abide not still in unbelief, shall be graffed in: for Elohim (God) is able to graff them in again* — withdrawal and return both possible, the same weighing of times Baruch describes.$n$, $n$Romans 11:23 — *And they also, if they abide not still in unbelief, shall be graffed in: for Elohim (God) is able to graff them in again* — withdrawal and return both possible, the same weighing of times Baruch describes.$n$),
(58038, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 42, 4, $n$As for those who were before subject, and afterwards withdrew and mingled themselves with the seed of mingled peoples, the time of these was the former, and was accounted as something exalted.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 56, 3, $n$Isa 56:3 — *Neither let the son of the stranger, that hath joined himself to Yahuah (LORD), speak, saying, Yahuah (LORD) hath utterly separated me from his people* — the joiner not cut off and the apostate not secure, the reckoning Baruch sets out.$n$, $n$Isaiah 56:3 — *Neither let the son of the stranger, that hath joined himself to Yahuah (LORD), speak, saying, Yahuah (LORD) hath utterly separated me from his people* — the joiner not cut off and the apostate not secure, the reckoning Baruch sets out.$n$, 14146, $n$Isa 56:3 — *Neither let the son of the stranger, that hath joined himself to Yahuah (LORD), speak, saying, Yahuah (LORD) hath utterly separated me from his people* — the joiner not cut off and the apostate not secure, the reckoning Baruch sets out.$n$, $n$Isaiah 56:3 — *Neither let the son of the stranger, that hath joined himself to Yahuah (LORD), speak, saying, Yahuah (LORD) hath utterly separated me from his people* — the joiner not cut off and the apostate not secure, the reckoning Baruch sets out.$n$),
(58039, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 42, 5, $n$And as for those who before knew not but afterwards knew life, and mingled (only) with the seed of the people which had separated itself, the time of these (is) the latter, and is accounted as something exalted.$n$, 'canon', 'exodus', 12, 49, $n$Exod 12:49 — *One law shall be to him that is homeborn, and unto the stranger that sojourneth among you* — one Torah for native and joiner alike, the ground on which Baruch's withdrawn and drawn-near are weighed.$n$, $n$Exodus 12:49 — *One law shall be to him that is homeborn, and unto the stranger that sojourneth among you* — one Torah for native and joiner alike, the ground on which Baruch's withdrawn and drawn-near are weighed.$n$, 14146, $n$Exod 12:49 — *One law shall be to him that is homeborn, and unto the stranger that sojourneth among you* — one Torah for native and joiner alike, the ground on which Baruch's withdrawn and drawn-near are weighed.$n$, $n$Exodus 12:49 — *One law shall be to him that is homeborn, and unto the stranger that sojourneth among you* — one Torah for native and joiner alike, the ground on which Baruch's withdrawn and drawn-near are weighed.$n$),
(58040, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 42, 5, $n$And as for those who before knew not but afterwards knew life, and mingled (only) with the seed of the people which had separated itself, the time of these (is) the latter, and is accounted as something exalted.$n$, 'canon', 'exodus', 12, 48, $n$Exod 12:48 — *And when a stranger shall sojourn with thee, and will keep the passover... let all his males be circumcised, and then let him come near... and he shall be as one that is born in the land* — the stranger drawn near to the separated people, Baruch's proselytes joined to the covenant.$n$, $n$Exodus 12:48 — *And when a stranger shall sojourn with thee, and will keep the passover... let all his males be circumcised, and then let him come near... and he shall be as one that is born in the land* — the stranger drawn near to the separated people, Baruch's proselytes joined to the covenant.$n$, 14146, $n$Exod 12:48 — *And when a stranger shall sojourn with thee, and will keep the passover... let all his males be circumcised, and then let him come near... and he shall be as one that is born in the land* — the stranger drawn near to the separated people, Baruch's proselytes joined to the covenant.$n$, $n$Exodus 12:48 — *And when a stranger shall sojourn with thee, and will keep the passover... let all his males be circumcised, and then let him come near... and he shall be as one that is born in the land* — the stranger drawn near to the separated people, Baruch's proselytes joined to the covenant.$n$),
(58042, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 44, 13, $n$For these are they who shall inherit that time which has been spoken of, And theirs is the inheritance of the promised time.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 5, 19, $n$Matt 5:19 — *whosoever shall do and teach them, the same shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven* — those who do and teach the commandments inherit greatly, Baruch's heirs of the world to come who kept the law.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:19 — *whosoever shall do and teach them, the same shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven* — those who do and teach the commandments inherit greatly, Baruch's heirs of the world to come who kept the law.$n$, 14150, $n$Matt 5:19 — *whosoever shall do and teach them, the same shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven* — those who do and teach the commandments inherit greatly, Baruch's heirs of the world to come who kept the law.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:19 — *whosoever shall do and teach them, the same shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven* — those who do and teach the commandments inherit greatly, Baruch's heirs of the world to come who kept the law.$n$),
(58043, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 44, 14, $n$These are they who have acquired for themselves treasures of wisdom, And with them are found stores of understanding, And from mercy have they not withdrawn, And the truth of the law have they preserved.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 19, 7, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law that gives wisdom, Baruch's treasures of wisdom and the truth of the law preserved.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law that gives wisdom, Baruch's treasures of wisdom and the truth of the law preserved.$n$, 14150, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law that gives wisdom, Baruch's treasures of wisdom and the truth of the law preserved.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law that gives wisdom, Baruch's treasures of wisdom and the truth of the law preserved.$n$),
(58044, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 44, 14, $n$These are they who have acquired for themselves treasures of wisdom, And with them are found stores of understanding, And from mercy have they not withdrawn, And the truth of the law have they preserved.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 19, 11, $n$Ps 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — great reward bound to keeping the law, the inheritance Baruch gives those who preserved the truth of the law.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — great reward bound to keeping the law, the inheritance Baruch gives those who preserved the truth of the law.$n$, 14150, $n$Ps 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — great reward bound to keeping the law, the inheritance Baruch gives those who preserved the truth of the law.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — great reward bound to keeping the law, the inheritance Baruch gives those who preserved the truth of the law.$n$),
(58045, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 44, 7, $n$For if ye endure and persevere in His fear, And do not forget His law, The times shall change over you for good, And ye shall see the consolation of Zion.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 6, 2, $n$Deut 6:2 — *That thou mightest fear Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to keep all his statutes and his commandments... that thy days may be prolonged* — enduring in His fear and keeping the law that the times may turn for good, exactly Baruch's promise.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 6:2 — *That thou mightest fear Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to keep all his statutes and his commandments... that thy days may be prolonged* — enduring in His fear and keeping the law that the times may turn for good, exactly Baruch's promise.$n$, 14149, $n$Deut 6:2 — *That thou mightest fear Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to keep all his statutes and his commandments... that thy days may be prolonged* — enduring in His fear and keeping the law that the times may turn for good, exactly Baruch's promise.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 6:2 — *That thou mightest fear Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to keep all his statutes and his commandments... that thy days may be prolonged* — enduring in His fear and keeping the law that the times may turn for good, exactly Baruch's promise.$n$),
(58046, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 44, 3, $n$But withdraw ye not from the way of the law, But guard and admonish the people which remain, Lest they withdraw from the commandments of the Mighty One.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 6, 6, $n$Deut 6:6 — *And these words, which I command thee this day, shall be in thine heart* — the commandments guarded and not forgotten, Baruch's way of the law admonished to the people who remain.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 6:6 — *And these words, which I command thee this day, shall be in thine heart* — the commandments guarded and not forgotten, Baruch's way of the law admonished to the people who remain.$n$, 14149, $n$Deut 6:6 — *And these words, which I command thee this day, shall be in thine heart* — the commandments guarded and not forgotten, Baruch's way of the law admonished to the people who remain.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 6:6 — *And these words, which I command thee this day, shall be in thine heart* — the commandments guarded and not forgotten, Baruch's way of the law admonished to the people who remain.$n$),
(58048, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 45, 2, $n$'Do ye therefore so far as ye are able instruct the people, for that labour is ours. For if ye teach them, ye will quicken them.'$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 6, 7, $n$Deut 6:7 — *And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children, and shalt talk of them when thou sittest in thine house* — the law diligently taught, Baruch's labour of instructing the people.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 6:7 — *And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children, and shalt talk of them when thou sittest in thine house* — the law diligently taught, Baruch's labour of instructing the people.$n$, 14151, $n$Deut 6:7 — *And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children, and shalt talk of them when thou sittest in thine house* — the law diligently taught, Baruch's labour of instructing the people.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 6:7 — *And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children, and shalt talk of them when thou sittest in thine house* — the law diligently taught, Baruch's labour of instructing the people.$n$),
(58049, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 45, 2, $n$'Do ye therefore so far as ye are able instruct the people, for that labour is ours. For if ye teach them, ye will quicken them.'$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 19, 7, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law that quickens the soul, the very life Baruch says teaching gives the people.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law that quickens the soul, the very life Baruch says teaching gives the people.$n$, 14151, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law that quickens the soul, the very life Baruch says teaching gives the people.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law that quickens the soul, the very life Baruch says teaching gives the people.$n$),
(58050, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 46, 6, $n$For if ye do these things, Good tidings shall come unto you. [Which I before told you of; nor shall ye fall into the torment, of which I testified to you before.'$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 19, 11, $n$Ps 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — good coming to those who keep the commandments, the good tidings Baruch promises hearts prepared to obey.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — good coming to those who keep the commandments, the good tidings Baruch promises hearts prepared to obey.$n$, 14153, $n$Ps 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — good coming to those who keep the commandments, the good tidings Baruch promises hearts prepared to obey.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — good coming to those who keep the commandments, the good tidings Baruch promises hearts prepared to obey.$n$),
(58051, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 46, 5, $n$But only prepare ye your hearts, that ye may obey the law, And be subject to those who in fear are wise and understanding; And prepare your souls that ye may not depart from them.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 6, 24, $n$Deut 6:24 — *And Yahuah (LORD) commanded us to do all these statutes, to fear Yahuah Eloheinu (the LORD our God), for our good always, that he might preserve us alive* — keeping the law for good and life, Baruch's good tidings to those who obey.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 6:24 — *And Yahuah (LORD) commanded us to do all these statutes, to fear Yahuah Eloheinu (the LORD our God), for our good always, that he might preserve us alive* — keeping the law for good and life, Baruch's good tidings to those who obey.$n$, 14153, $n$Deut 6:24 — *And Yahuah (LORD) commanded us to do all these statutes, to fear Yahuah Eloheinu (the LORD our God), for our good always, that he might preserve us alive* — keeping the law for good and life, Baruch's good tidings to those who obey.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 6:24 — *And Yahuah (LORD) commanded us to do all these statutes, to fear Yahuah Eloheinu (the LORD our God), for our good always, that he might preserve us alive* — keeping the law for good and life, Baruch's good tidings to those who obey.$n$),
(58052, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 46, 4, $n$And I said unto them: 'The throne of the Mighty One I cannot resist; Nevertheless, there shall not be wanting to Yashar'el (Israel) a wise man Nor a son of the law to the race of Jacob.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 5, 17, $n$Matt 5:17 — *Think not that I am come to destroy the law, or the prophets: I am not come to destroy, but to fulfil* — the law not failing nor passing, Baruch's son of the law never wanting to Jacob.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:17 — *Think not that I am come to destroy the law, or the prophets: I am not come to destroy, but to fulfil* — the law not failing nor passing, Baruch's son of the law never wanting to Jacob.$n$, 14152, $n$Matt 5:17 — *Think not that I am come to destroy the law, or the prophets: I am not come to destroy, but to fulfil* — the law not failing nor passing, Baruch's son of the law never wanting to Jacob.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:17 — *Think not that I am come to destroy the law, or the prophets: I am not come to destroy, but to fulfil* — the law not failing nor passing, Baruch's son of the law never wanting to Jacob.$n$),
(58053, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 46, 3, $n$For where again shall we seek the law, Or who will distinguish for us between death and life?'$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 6, 7, $n$Deut 6:7 — *And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children... when thou sittest in thine house, and when thou walkest by the way* — the law to be passed on lest it be lost, the lack the elders fear and Baruch answers.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 6:7 — *And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children... when thou sittest in thine house, and when thou walkest by the way* — the law to be passed on lest it be lost, the lack the elders fear and Baruch answers.$n$, 14152, $n$Deut 6:7 — *And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children... when thou sittest in thine house, and when thou walkest by the way* — the law to be passed on lest it be lost, the lack the elders fear and Baruch answers.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 6:7 — *And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children... when thou sittest in thine house, and when thou walkest by the way* — the law to be passed on lest it be lost, the lack the elders fear and Baruch answers.$n$),
(58054, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 47, 2, $n$And I came to that place where the word had been spoken unto me, and I sat there, and fasted seven days.$n$, 'canon', 'exodus', 34, 28, $n$Exod 34:28 — *And he was there with Yahuah (LORD) forty days and forty nights; he did neither eat bread, nor drink water* — Moses fasts at the appointed place before the words of the covenant are given.$n$, $n$Exodus 34:28 — *And he was there with Yahuah (LORD) forty days and forty nights; he did neither eat bread, nor drink water* — Moses fasts at the appointed place before the words of the covenant are given.$n$, 14154, $n$Exod 34:28 — *And he was there with Yahuah (LORD) forty days and forty nights; he did neither eat bread, nor drink water* — Moses fasts at the appointed place before the words of the covenant are given.$n$, $n$Exodus 34:28 — *And he was there with Yahuah (LORD) forty days and forty nights; he did neither eat bread, nor drink water* — Moses fasts at the appointed place before the words of the covenant are given.$n$),
(58055, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 47, 2, $n$And I came to that place where the word had been spoken unto me, and I sat there, and fasted seven days.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 10, 3, $n$Dan 10:3 — *I ate no pleasant bread, neither came flesh nor wine in my mouth, neither did I anoint myself at all, till three whole weeks were fulfilled* — the seer fasts in mourning before the vision is unsealed.$n$, $n$Daniel 10:3 — *I ate no pleasant bread, neither came flesh nor wine in my mouth, neither did I anoint myself at all, till three whole weeks were fulfilled* — the seer fasts in mourning before the vision is unsealed.$n$, 14154, $n$Dan 10:3 — *I ate no pleasant bread, neither came flesh nor wine in my mouth, neither did I anoint myself at all, till three whole weeks were fulfilled* — the seer fasts in mourning before the vision is unsealed.$n$, $n$Daniel 10:3 — *I ate no pleasant bread, neither came flesh nor wine in my mouth, neither did I anoint myself at all, till three whole weeks were fulfilled* — the seer fasts in mourning before the vision is unsealed.$n$),
(58056, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 40, $n$Because each of the inhabitants of the earth knew when he was transgressing. But My Law they knew not by reason of their pride.$n$, 'canon', 'malachi', 4, 4, $n$Mal 4:4 — *Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb for all Yashar'el (Israel), with the statutes and judgments* — they perish because they remembered not the law of the Mighty One.$n$, $n$Malachi 4:4 — *Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb for all Yashar'el (Israel), with the statutes and judgments* — they perish because they remembered not the law of the Mighty One.$n$, 14159, $n$Mal 4:4 — *Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb for all Yashar'el (Israel), with the statutes and judgments* — they perish because they remembered not the law of the Mighty One.$n$, $n$Malachi 4:4 — *Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb for all Yashar'el (Israel), with the statutes and judgments* — they perish because they remembered not the law of the Mighty One.$n$),
(58058, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 39, $n$Therefore a fire shall consume their thoughts, And in flame shall the meditations of their reins be tried; For the Judge shall come and will not tarry.$n$, 'canon', 'malachi', 4, 1, $n$Mal 4:1 — *behold, the day cometh, that shall burn as an oven... and the day that cometh shall burn them up* — a fire shall consume the thoughts of the proud who knew not His law.$n$, $n$Malachi 4:1 — *behold, the day cometh, that shall burn as an oven... and the day that cometh shall burn them up* — a fire shall consume the thoughts of the proud who knew not His law.$n$, 14159, $n$Mal 4:1 — *behold, the day cometh, that shall burn as an oven... and the day that cometh shall burn them up* — a fire shall consume the thoughts of the proud who knew not His law.$n$, $n$Malachi 4:1 — *behold, the day cometh, that shall burn as an oven... and the day that cometh shall burn them up* — a fire shall consume the thoughts of the proud who knew not His law.$n$),
(58059, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 19, $n$Protect us in Thy compassions, And in Thy mercy help us.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 103, 14, $n$Ps 103:14 — *For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we are dust* — protect us in Thy compassions, for he is nothing.$n$, $n$Psalm 103:14 — *For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we are dust* — protect us in Thy compassions, for he is nothing.$n$, 14158, $n$Ps 103:14 — *For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we are dust* — protect us in Thy compassions, for he is nothing.$n$, $n$Psalm 103:14 — *For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we are dust* — protect us in Thy compassions, for he is nothing.$n$),
(58060, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 14, $n$But with Thee hours are as a time, And days as generations.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 90, 4, $n$Ps 90:4 — *For a thousand years in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past, and as a watch in the night* — with Thee hours are as a time, and days as generations.$n$, $n$Psalm 90:4 — *For a thousand years in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past, and as a watch in the night* — with Thee hours are as a time, and days as generations.$n$, 14158, $n$Ps 90:4 — *For a thousand years in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past, and as a watch in the night* — with Thee hours are as a time, and days as generations.$n$, $n$Psalm 90:4 — *For a thousand years in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past, and as a watch in the night* — with Thee hours are as a time, and days as generations.$n$),
(58061, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 13, $n$For in a little time are we born, And in a little time do we return.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 103, 15, $n$Ps 103:15 — *As for man, his days are as grass: as a flower of the field, so he flourisheth* — in a little time are we born and return.$n$, $n$Psalm 103:15 — *As for man, his days are as grass: as a flower of the field, so he flourisheth* — in a little time are we born and return.$n$, 14158, $n$Ps 103:15 — *As for man, his days are as grass: as a flower of the field, so he flourisheth* — in a little time are we born and return.$n$, $n$Psalm 103:15 — *As for man, his days are as grass: as a flower of the field, so he flourisheth* — in a little time are we born and return.$n$),
(58062, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 24, $n$For we are all one celebrated people, Who have received one law from One: And the law which is amongst us will aid us, And the surpassing wisdom which is in us will help us.'$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 119, 89, $n$Ps 119:89 — *For ever, O Yahuah (LORD), thy word is settled in heaven* — the law amongst us abides; therefore we shall not fall.$n$, $n$Psalm 119:89 — *For ever, O Yahuah (LORD), thy word is settled in heaven* — the law amongst us abides; therefore we shall not fall.$n$, 14157, $n$Ps 119:89 — *For ever, O Yahuah (LORD), thy word is settled in heaven* — the law amongst us abides; therefore we shall not fall.$n$, $n$Psalm 119:89 — *For ever, O Yahuah (LORD), thy word is settled in heaven* — the law amongst us abides; therefore we shall not fall.$n$),
(58063, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 24, $n$For we are all one celebrated people, Who have received one law from One: And the law which is amongst us will aid us, And the surpassing wisdom which is in us will help us.'$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 7, 12, $n$Rom 7:12 — *Wherefore the law is holy, and the commandment holy, and just, and good* — the one law received from One is no burden but the people's surpassing wisdom.$n$, $n$Romans 7:12 — *Wherefore the law is holy, and the commandment holy, and just, and good* — the one law received from One is no burden but the people's surpassing wisdom.$n$, 14157, $n$Rom 7:12 — *Wherefore the law is holy, and the commandment holy, and just, and good* — the one law received from One is no burden but the people's surpassing wisdom.$n$, $n$Romans 7:12 — *Wherefore the law is holy, and the commandment holy, and just, and good* — the one law received from One is no burden but the people's surpassing wisdom.$n$),
(58064, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 22, $n$But I will speak now before Thee, And I will say as my heart thinketh. In Thee do we trust, for lo! Thy law is with us, And we know that we shall not fall so long as we keep Thy statutes.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 11, $n$Deut 30:11 — *For this commandment which I command thee this day, it is not hidden from thee, neither is it far off* — the law is with us, near and able to aid us.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:11 — *For this commandment which I command thee this day, it is not hidden from thee, neither is it far off* — the law is with us, near and able to aid us.$n$, 14157, $n$Deut 30:11 — *For this commandment which I command thee this day, it is not hidden from thee, neither is it far off* — the law is with us, near and able to aid us.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:11 — *For this commandment which I command thee this day, it is not hidden from thee, neither is it far off* — the law is with us, near and able to aid us.$n$),
(58065, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 22, $n$But I will speak now before Thee, And I will say as my heart thinketh. In Thee do we trust, for lo! Thy law is with us, And we know that we shall not fall so long as we keep Thy statutes.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 20, $n$Deut 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land* — with Him is the law of life; keeping His statutes is life itself.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land* — with Him is the law of life; keeping His statutes is life itself.$n$, 14157, $n$Deut 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land* — with Him is the law of life; keeping His statutes is life itself.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land* — with Him is the law of life; keeping His statutes is life itself.$n$),
(58066, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 9, $n$With nods of fear and indignation Thou commandest the flames, And they change into spirits, And with a word Thou quickenest that which was not, And with mighty power Thou holdest that which has not yet come.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 4, 17, $n$Rom 4:17 — *even Elohim (God), who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were.* — with a word He quickens that which was not.$n$, $n$Romans 4:17 — *even Elohim (God), who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were.* — with a word He quickens that which was not.$n$, 14156, $n$Rom 4:17 — *even Elohim (God), who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were.* — with a word He quickens that which was not.$n$, $n$Romans 4:17 — *even Elohim (God), who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were.* — with a word He quickens that which was not.$n$),
(58068, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 9, $n$With nods of fear and indignation Thou commandest the flames, And they change into spirits, And with a word Thou quickenest that which was not, And with mighty power Thou holdest that which has not yet come.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 104, 4, $n$Ps 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire* — the flames change into spirits at His command.$n$, $n$Psalm 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire* — the flames change into spirits at His command.$n$, 14156, $n$Ps 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire* — the flames change into spirits at His command.$n$, $n$Psalm 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire* — the flames change into spirits at His command.$n$),
(58071, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 3, $n$Thou arrangest the method of the seasons, And they obey Thee.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 74, 16, $n$Ps 74:16 — *The day is thine, the night also is thine: thou hast prepared the light and the sun* — He arranges the method of the seasons, and they obey.$n$, $n$Psalm 74:16 — *The day is thine, the night also is thine: thou hast prepared the light and the sun* — He arranges the method of the seasons, and they obey.$n$, 14155, $n$Ps 74:16 — *The day is thine, the night also is thine: thou hast prepared the light and the sun* — He arranges the method of the seasons, and they obey.$n$, $n$Psalm 74:16 — *The day is thine, the night also is thine: thou hast prepared the light and the sun* — He arranges the method of the seasons, and they obey.$n$),
(58072, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 4, $n$Thou alone knowest the duration of the generations, And Thou revealest not Thy mysteries to many.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 7, 10, $n$Dan 7:10 — *thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened* — the duration of the generations is in His hand.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:10 — *thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened* — the duration of the generations is in His hand.$n$, 14155, $n$Dan 7:10 — *thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened* — the duration of the generations is in His hand.$n$, $n$Daniel 7:10 — *thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened* — the duration of the generations is in His hand.$n$),
(58073, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 48, 2, $n$'O my Lord, Thou summonest the advent of the times, And they stand before Thee; Thou causest the power of the ages to pass away, And they do not resist Thee;$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 2, 21, $n$Dan 2:21 — *And he changeth the times and the seasons: he removeth kings, and setteth up kings: he giveth wisdom unto the wise, and knowledge to them that know understanding* — the ages and seasons obey the Most High alone.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:21 — *And he changeth the times and the seasons: he removeth kings, and setteth up kings: he giveth wisdom unto the wise, and knowledge to them that know understanding* — the ages and seasons obey the Most High alone.$n$, 14155, $n$Dan 2:21 — *And he changeth the times and the seasons: he removeth kings, and setteth up kings: he giveth wisdom unto the wise, and knowledge to them that know understanding* — the ages and seasons obey the Most High alone.$n$, $n$Daniel 2:21 — *And he changeth the times and the seasons: he removeth kings, and setteth up kings: he giveth wisdom unto the wise, and knowledge to them that know understanding* — the ages and seasons obey the Most High alone.$n$),
(58076, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 50, 2, $n$For the earth shall then assuredly restore the dead, [Which it now receives, in order to preserve them]. It shall make no change in their form, But as it has received, so shall it restore them, And as I delivered them unto it, so also shall it raise them.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 12, 2, $n$Dan 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the dust restores both the just and the condemned for judgment.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the dust restores both the just and the condemned for judgment.$n$, 14161, $n$Dan 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the dust restores both the just and the condemned for judgment.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the dust restores both the just and the condemned for judgment.$n$),
(58080, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 51, 4, $n$For over this above all shall those who come then lament, that they rejected My law, and stopped their ears that they might not hear wisdom or receive understanding.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 2, 13, $n$Rom 2:13 — *For not the hearers of the law are just before Elohim (God), but the doers of the law shall be justified.* — the lost stopped their ears against the law and so were condemned.$n$, $n$Romans 2:13 — *For not the hearers of the law are just before Elohim (God), but the doers of the law shall be justified.* — the lost stopped their ears against the law and so were condemned.$n$, 14165, $n$Rom 2:13 — *For not the hearers of the law are just before Elohim (God), but the doers of the law shall be justified.* — the lost stopped their ears against the law and so were condemned.$n$, $n$Romans 2:13 — *For not the hearers of the law are just before Elohim (God), but the doers of the law shall be justified.* — the lost stopped their ears against the law and so were condemned.$n$),
(58081, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 51, 7, $n$But those who have been saved by their works, And to whom the law has been now a hope, And understanding an expectation, And wisdom a confidence, Shall wonders appear in their time.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 19, 7, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — to them the law has been a hope and wisdom a confidence.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — to them the law has been a hope and wisdom a confidence.$n$, 14165, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — to them the law has been a hope and wisdom a confidence.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — to them the law has been a hope and wisdom a confidence.$n$),
(58089, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 51, 10, $n$For in the heights of that world shall they dwell, And they shall be made like unto the angels, And be made equal to the stars, And they shall be changed into every form they desire, From beauty into loveliness, And from light into the splendour of glory.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 22, 30, $n$Matt 22:30 — *For in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the angels of Elohim (God) in heaven* — they shall be made like unto the angels.$n$, $n$Matthew 22:30 — *For in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the angels of Elohim (God) in heaven* — they shall be made like unto the angels.$n$, 14163, $n$Matt 22:30 — *For in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the angels of Elohim (God) in heaven* — they shall be made like unto the angels.$n$, $n$Matthew 22:30 — *For in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the angels of Elohim (God) in heaven* — they shall be made like unto the angels.$n$),
(58090, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 51, 3, $n$Also (as for) the glory of those who have now been justified in My law, who have had understanding in their life, and who have planted in their heart the root of wisdom, then their splendour shall be glorified in changes, and the form of their face shall be turned into the light of their beauty, that they may be able to acquire and receive the world which does not die, which is then promised to them.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 1, 2, $n$Ps 1:2 — *But his delight is in the law of Yahuah (LORD); and in his law doth he meditate day and night* — the root of wisdom planted in the heart is delight in the Torah.$n$, $n$Psalm 1:2 — *But his delight is in the law of Yahuah (LORD); and in his law doth he meditate day and night* — the root of wisdom planted in the heart is delight in the Torah.$n$, 14162, $n$Ps 1:2 — *But his delight is in the law of Yahuah (LORD); and in his law doth he meditate day and night* — the root of wisdom planted in the heart is delight in the Torah.$n$, $n$Psalm 1:2 — *But his delight is in the law of Yahuah (LORD); and in his law doth he meditate day and night* — the root of wisdom planted in the heart is delight in the Torah.$n$),
(58091, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 51, 3, $n$Also (as for) the glory of those who have now been justified in My law, who have had understanding in their life, and who have planted in their heart the root of wisdom, then their splendour shall be glorified in changes, and the form of their face shall be turned into the light of their beauty, that they may be able to acquire and receive the world which does not die, which is then promised to them.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 13, 43, $n$Matt 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear* — the splendour of those justified in His law, glorified.$n$, $n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear* — the splendour of those justified in His law, glorified.$n$, 14162, $n$Matt 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear* — the splendour of those justified in His law, glorified.$n$, $n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear* — the splendour of those justified in His law, glorified.$n$),
(58092, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 51, 3, $n$Also (as for) the glory of those who have now been justified in My law, who have had understanding in their life, and who have planted in their heart the root of wisdom, then their splendour shall be glorified in changes, and the form of their face shall be turned into the light of their beauty, that they may be able to acquire and receive the world which does not die, which is then promised to them.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 12, 3, $n$Dan 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever* — the form of their face turned into the light of their beauty.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever* — the form of their face turned into the light of their beauty.$n$, 14162, $n$Dan 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever* — the form of their face turned into the light of their beauty.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever* — the form of their face turned into the light of their beauty.$n$),
(58093, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 52, 6, $n$Rejoice ye in the suffering which ye now suffer: For why do ye look for the decline of your enemies?$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 5, 12, $n$Matt 5:12 — *Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for great is your reward in heaven* — make ready your soul for that which is reserved.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:12 — *Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for great is your reward in heaven* — make ready your soul for that which is reserved.$n$, 14166, $n$Matt 5:12 — *Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for great is your reward in heaven* — make ready your soul for that which is reserved.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:12 — *Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for great is your reward in heaven* — make ready your soul for that which is reserved.$n$),
(58095, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 52, 6, $n$Rejoice ye in the suffering which ye now suffer: For why do ye look for the decline of your enemies?$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 5, 3, $n$Rom 5:3 — *we glory in tribulations also: knowing that tribulation worketh patience* — rejoice ye in the suffering which ye now suffer.$n$, $n$Romans 5:3 — *we glory in tribulations also: knowing that tribulation worketh patience* — rejoice ye in the suffering which ye now suffer.$n$, 14166, $n$Rom 5:3 — *we glory in tribulations also: knowing that tribulation worketh patience* — rejoice ye in the suffering which ye now suffer.$n$, $n$Romans 5:3 — *we glory in tribulations also: knowing that tribulation worketh patience* — rejoice ye in the suffering which ye now suffer.$n$),
(58137, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 61, 6, $n$And the judgement of the rulers was then seen to be without guile, And the righteousness of the precepts of the Mighty One was accomplished with truth.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 72, 2, $n$Ps 72:2 — *He shall judge thy people with righteousness, and thy poor with judgment* — the judgement of the rulers without guile that the bright waters commend.$n$, $n$Psalm 72:2 — *He shall judge thy people with righteousness, and thy poor with judgment* — the judgement of the rulers without guile that the bright waters commend.$n$, 14184, $n$Ps 72:2 — *He shall judge thy people with righteousness, and thy poor with judgment* — the judgement of the rulers without guile that the bright waters commend.$n$, $n$Psalm 72:2 — *He shall judge thy people with righteousness, and thy poor with judgment* — the judgement of the rulers without guile that the bright waters commend.$n$),
(58138, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 61, 3, $n$And peace and tranquillity existed at that time,$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 72, 7, $n$Ps 72:7 — *In his days shall the righteous flourish; and abundance of peace so long as the moon endureth* — the peace and tranquillity of the bright waters, the prayer for the king's son.$n$, $n$Psalm 72:7 — *In his days shall the righteous flourish; and abundance of peace so long as the moon endureth* — the peace and tranquillity of the bright waters, the prayer for the king's son.$n$, 14184, $n$Ps 72:7 — *In his days shall the righteous flourish; and abundance of peace so long as the moon endureth* — the peace and tranquillity of the bright waters, the prayer for the king's son.$n$, $n$Psalm 72:7 — *In his days shall the righteous flourish; and abundance of peace so long as the moon endureth* — the peace and tranquillity of the bright waters, the prayer for the king's son.$n$),
(58144, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 62, 5, $n$And the time of their captivity which came upon the nine tribes and a half, because they were in many sins.$n$, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 22, $n$Ezek 37:22 — *I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all* — the promise over the captive houses Baruch's black waters record being torn apart.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all* — the promise over the captive houses Baruch's black waters record being torn apart.$n$, 14187, $n$Ezek 37:22 — *I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all* — the promise over the captive houses Baruch's black waters record being torn apart.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all* — the promise over the captive houses Baruch's black waters record being torn apart.$n$),
(58145, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 62, 5, $n$And the time of their captivity which came upon the nine tribes and a half, because they were in many sins.$n$, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 19, $n$Ezek 37:19 — *I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim... and will put them with him, even with the stick of Yahudah... and they shall be one in mine hand* — the healing of the very division the black waters mourn, the nine tribes and a half carried away.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:19 — *I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim... and will put them with him, even with the stick of Yahudah... and they shall be one in mine hand* — the healing of the very division the black waters mourn, the nine tribes and a half carried away.$n$, 14187, $n$Ezek 37:19 — *I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim... and will put them with him, even with the stick of Yahudah... and they shall be one in mine hand* — the healing of the very division the black waters mourn, the nine tribes and a half carried away.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:19 — *I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim... and will put them with him, even with the stick of Yahudah... and they shall be one in mine hand* — the healing of the very division the black waters mourn, the nine tribes and a half carried away.$n$),
(58151, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 63, 10, $n$And all those who were in the holy land rejoiced, and the name of the Mighty One was glorified so that it was spoken of.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 76, 1, $n$Ps 76:1 — *In Yahudah is Elohim known: his name is great in Yashar'el* — the Name glorified throughout the land of which Baruch's bright waters speak.$n$, $n$Psalm 76:1 — *In Yahudah is Elohim known: his name is great in Yashar'el* — the Name glorified throughout the land of which Baruch's bright waters speak.$n$, 14190, $n$Ps 76:1 — *In Yahudah is Elohim known: his name is great in Yashar'el* — the Name glorified throughout the land of which Baruch's bright waters speak.$n$, $n$Psalm 76:1 — *In Yahudah is Elohim known: his name is great in Yashar'el* — the Name glorified throughout the land of which Baruch's bright waters speak.$n$),
(58152, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 63, 9, $n$And Zion was saved and Jerusalem delivered: Yashar'el (Israel) also was freed from tribulation.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 76, 3, $n$Ps 76:3 — *There brake he the arrows of the bow, the shield, and the sword, and the battle* — the deliverance of Zion the bright waters celebrate, the host broken before the city.$n$, $n$Psalm 76:3 — *There brake he the arrows of the bow, the shield, and the sword, and the battle* — the deliverance of Zion the bright waters celebrate, the host broken before the city.$n$, 14190, $n$Ps 76:3 — *There brake he the arrows of the bow, the shield, and the sword, and the battle* — the deliverance of Zion the bright waters celebrate, the host broken before the city.$n$, $n$Psalm 76:3 — *There brake he the arrows of the bow, the shield, and the sword, and the battle* — the deliverance of Zion the bright waters celebrate, the host broken before the city.$n$),
(58154, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 63, 7, $n$And I went forth and destroyed their multitude, the number of whose chiefs only was a hundred and eighty-five thousand, and each one of them had an equal number (at his command).$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 37, 36, $n$Isa 37:36 — *Then the angel of Yahuah went forth, and smote in the camp of the Assyrians a hundred and fourscore and five thousand* — the destruction of the host the bright waters recount.$n$, $n$Isaiah 37:36 — *Then the angel of Yahuah went forth, and smote in the camp of the Assyrians a hundred and fourscore and five thousand* — the destruction of the host the bright waters recount.$n$, 14189, $n$Isa 37:36 — *Then the angel of Yahuah went forth, and smote in the camp of the Assyrians a hundred and fourscore and five thousand* — the destruction of the host the bright waters recount.$n$, $n$Isaiah 37:36 — *Then the angel of Yahuah went forth, and smote in the camp of the Assyrians a hundred and fourscore and five thousand* — the destruction of the host the bright waters recount.$n$),
(58160, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 64, 4, $n$And then wrath went forth from the presence of the Mighty One to the intent that Zion should be rooted out, as also it befell in your days.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 4, 25, $n$Deut 4:25 — *and shall corrupt yourselves, and make a graven image... and shall do evil in the sight of Yahuah Elohayka, to provoke him to anger* — the law's warning against the very idolatry that brought the wrath Baruch reads.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 4:25 — *and shall corrupt yourselves, and make a graven image... and shall do evil in the sight of Yahuah Elohayka, to provoke him to anger* — the law's warning against the very idolatry that brought the wrath Baruch reads.$n$, 14192, $n$Deut 4:25 — *and shall corrupt yourselves, and make a graven image... and shall do evil in the sight of Yahuah Elohayka, to provoke him to anger* — the law's warning against the very idolatry that brought the wrath Baruch reads.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 4:25 — *and shall corrupt yourselves, and make a graven image... and shall do evil in the sight of Yahuah Elohayka, to provoke him to anger* — the law's warning against the very idolatry that brought the wrath Baruch reads.$n$),
(58172, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 66, 1, $n$'And the bright tenth waters which thou hast seen: this is the purity of the generations of Josiah king of Yahudah (Judah), who was the only one at the time who submitted himself to the Mighty One with all his heart and with all his soul.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 2, $n$Deut 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka, and shalt obey his voice... with all thine heart, and with all thy soul* — the law's own call to return that Josiah, the bright waters, embodied.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka, and shalt obey his voice... with all thine heart, and with all thy soul* — the law's own call to return that Josiah, the bright waters, embodied.$n$, 14195, $n$Deut 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka, and shalt obey his voice... with all thine heart, and with all thy soul* — the law's own call to return that Josiah, the bright waters, embodied.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka, and shalt obey his voice... with all thine heart, and with all thy soul* — the law's own call to return that Josiah, the bright waters, embodied.$n$),
(58174, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 67, 8, $n$But he also shall fall at last. These are the black waters.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 137, 8, $n$Ps 137:8 — *O daughter of Babylon, who art to be destroyed; happy shall he be, that rewardeth thee as thou hast served us* — Babylon's appointed fall, the king who shall fall at last as Baruch foretells.$n$, $n$Psalm 137:8 — *O daughter of Babylon, who art to be destroyed; happy shall he be, that rewardeth thee as thou hast served us* — Babylon's appointed fall, the king who shall fall at last as Baruch foretells.$n$, 14200, $n$Ps 137:8 — *O daughter of Babylon, who art to be destroyed; happy shall he be, that rewardeth thee as thou hast served us* — Babylon's appointed fall, the king who shall fall at last as Baruch foretells.$n$, $n$Psalm 137:8 — *O daughter of Babylon, who art to be destroyed; happy shall he be, that rewardeth thee as thou hast served us* — Babylon's appointed fall, the king who shall fall at last as Baruch foretells.$n$),
(58175, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 67, 7, $n$But the king of Babylon will arise who has now destroyed Zion, And he will boast over the people, And he will speak great things in his heart in the presence of the El Elyon (Most High).$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 137, 1, $n$Ps 137:1 — *By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion* — the captivity under the king who boasts, the black waters of Zion delivered up.$n$, $n$Psalm 137:1 — *By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion* — the captivity under the king who boasts, the black waters of Zion delivered up.$n$, 14200, $n$Ps 137:1 — *By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion* — the captivity under the king who boasts, the black waters of Zion delivered up.$n$, $n$Psalm 137:1 — *By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion* — the captivity under the king who boasts, the black waters of Zion delivered up.$n$),
(58176, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 67, 6, $n$Because so far as Zion is delivered up And Jerusalem laid waste, Shall idols prosper in the cities of the Gentiles, And the vapour of the smoke of the incense of the righteousness which is by the law is extinguished in Zion, And in the region of Zion in every place lo! there is the smoke of impiety.$n$, 'canon', 'jeremiah', 52, 13, $n$Jer 52:13 — *And burned the house of Yahuah, and the king's house; and all the houses of Jerusalem... burned he with fire* — the temple's burning behind the smoke extinguished in Zion that Baruch reads.$n$, $n$Jeremiah 52:13 — *And burned the house of Yahuah, and the king's house; and all the houses of Jerusalem... burned he with fire* — the temple's burning behind the smoke extinguished in Zion that Baruch reads.$n$, 14199, $n$Jer 52:13 — *And burned the house of Yahuah, and the king's house; and all the houses of Jerusalem... burned he with fire* — the temple's burning behind the smoke extinguished in Zion that Baruch reads.$n$, $n$Jeremiah 52:13 — *And burned the house of Yahuah, and the king's house; and all the houses of Jerusalem... burned he with fire* — the temple's burning behind the smoke extinguished in Zion that Baruch reads.$n$),
(58182, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 68, 5, $n$And at that time after a little interval Zion will again be builded, and its offerings will again be restored, and the priests will return to their ministry, and also the Gentiles will come to glorify it.$n$, 'canon', 'zechariah', 4, 9, $n$Zech 4:9 — *The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it* — the restored ministry and rebuilt house of which the bright waters speak.$n$, $n$Zechariah 4:9 — *The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it* — the restored ministry and rebuilt house of which the bright waters speak.$n$, 14201, $n$Zech 4:9 — *The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it* — the restored ministry and rebuilt house of which the bright waters speak.$n$, $n$Zechariah 4:9 — *The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it* — the restored ministry and rebuilt house of which the bright waters speak.$n$),
(58183, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 68, 5, $n$And at that time after a little interval Zion will again be builded, and its offerings will again be restored, and the priests will return to their ministry, and also the Gentiles will come to glorify it.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 44, 28, $n$Isa 44:28 — *That saith of Cyrus, He is my shepherd... even saying to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be built; and to the temple, Thy foundation shall be laid* — the word over Cyrus behind the return the bright waters describe.$n$, $n$Isaiah 44:28 — *That saith of Cyrus, He is my shepherd... even saying to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be built; and to the temple, Thy foundation shall be laid* — the word over Cyrus behind the return the bright waters describe.$n$, 14201, $n$Isa 44:28 — *That saith of Cyrus, He is my shepherd... even saying to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be built; and to the temple, Thy foundation shall be laid* — the word over Cyrus behind the return the bright waters describe.$n$, $n$Isaiah 44:28 — *That saith of Cyrus, He is my shepherd... even saying to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be built; and to the temple, Thy foundation shall be laid* — the word over Cyrus behind the return the bright waters describe.$n$),
(58187, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 69, 3, $n$For as to the enormities and the impieties which should be wrought before Him, He foresaw six kinds of them.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 24, 12, $n$Matt 24:12 — *And because iniquity shall abound, the love of many shall wax cold* — the impieties of the last black waters Baruch says were foreseen.$n$, $n$Matthew 24:12 — *And because iniquity shall abound, the love of many shall wax cold* — the impieties of the last black waters Baruch says were foreseen.$n$, 14204, $n$Matt 24:12 — *And because iniquity shall abound, the love of many shall wax cold* — the impieties of the last black waters Baruch says were foreseen.$n$, $n$Matthew 24:12 — *And because iniquity shall abound, the love of many shall wax cold* — the impieties of the last black waters Baruch says were foreseen.$n$),
(58188, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 69, 1, $n$'For the last waters which thou hast seen which were darker than all that were before them, those which were after the twelfth number, which were collected together, belong to the whole world.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 24, 21, $n$Matt 24:21 — *For then shall be great tribulation, such as was not since the beginning of the world to this time, no, nor ever shall be* — the darkest waters before the end that Baruch beholds.$n$, $n$Matthew 24:21 — *For then shall be great tribulation, such as was not since the beginning of the world to this time, no, nor ever shall be* — the darkest waters before the end that Baruch beholds.$n$, 14203, $n$Matt 24:21 — *For then shall be great tribulation, such as was not since the beginning of the world to this time, no, nor ever shall be* — the darkest waters before the end that Baruch beholds.$n$, $n$Matthew 24:21 — *For then shall be great tribulation, such as was not since the beginning of the world to this time, no, nor ever shall be* — the darkest waters before the end that Baruch beholds.$n$),
(58189, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 69, 1, $n$'For the last waters which thou hast seen which were darker than all that were before them, those which were after the twelfth number, which were collected together, belong to the whole world.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 12, 1, $n$Dan 12:1 — *there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered* — the last waters darker than all before, before the consummation Baruch reads.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:1 — *there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered* — the last waters darker than all before, before the consummation Baruch reads.$n$, 14203, $n$Dan 12:1 — *there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered* — the last waters darker than all before, before the consummation Baruch reads.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:1 — *there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered* — the last waters darker than all before, before the consummation Baruch reads.$n$),
(58191, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 70, 9, $n$[And it shall come to pass that whosoever of the victors and the vanquished gets safe out of and escapes all these things aforesaid will be delivered into the hands of My servant Messiah.]$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 4, $n$Isa 11:4 — *with righteousness shall he judge the poor... and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Anointed into whose hands the survivors are delivered, the Servant Messiah of David's shoot.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:4 — *with righteousness shall he judge the poor... and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Anointed into whose hands the survivors are delivered, the Servant Messiah of David's shoot.$n$, 14208, $n$Isa 11:4 — *with righteousness shall he judge the poor... and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Anointed into whose hands the survivors are delivered, the Servant Messiah of David's shoot.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:4 — *with righteousness shall he judge the poor... and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Anointed into whose hands the survivors are delivered, the Servant Messiah of David's shoot.$n$),
(58192, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 70, 3, $n$And they shall hate one another, And provoke one another to fight, And the mean shall rule over the honourable, And those of low degree shall be extolled above the famous.$n$, 'canon', 'zechariah', 14, 13, $n$Zech 14:13 — *a great tumult from Yahuah (LORD) shall be among them; and they shall lay hold every one on the hand of his neighbour, and his hand shall rise up against the hand of his neighbour* — the mutual strife that breaks out in the last day, the hating and provoking of Baruch's vision.$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:13 — *a great tumult from Yahuah (LORD) shall be among them; and they shall lay hold every one on the hand of his neighbour, and his hand shall rise up against the hand of his neighbour* — the mutual strife that breaks out in the last day, the hating and provoking of Baruch's vision.$n$, 14207, $n$Zech 14:13 — *a great tumult from Yahuah (LORD) shall be among them; and they shall lay hold every one on the hand of his neighbour, and his hand shall rise up against the hand of his neighbour* — the mutual strife that breaks out in the last day, the hating and provoking of Baruch's vision.$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:13 — *a great tumult from Yahuah (LORD) shall be among them; and they shall lay hold every one on the hand of his neighbour, and his hand shall rise up against the hand of his neighbour* — the mutual strife that breaks out in the last day, the hating and provoking of Baruch's vision.$n$),
(58194, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 70, 2, $n$Behold! the days come, and it shall be when the time of the age has ripened, And the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, That the Mighty One will bring upon the earth and its inhabitants and upon its rulers Perturbation of spirit and stupor of heart.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 14, 16, $n$Rev 14:16 — *And he that sat on the cloud thrust in his sickle on the earth; and the earth was reaped* — the earth brought in at the end of the age, as Baruch's good and evil seeds are gathered.$n$, $n$Revelation 14:16 — *And he that sat on the cloud thrust in his sickle on the earth; and the earth was reaped* — the earth brought in at the end of the age, as Baruch's good and evil seeds are gathered.$n$, 14206, $n$Rev 14:16 — *And he that sat on the cloud thrust in his sickle on the earth; and the earth was reaped* — the earth brought in at the end of the age, as Baruch's good and evil seeds are gathered.$n$, $n$Revelation 14:16 — *And he that sat on the cloud thrust in his sickle on the earth; and the earth was reaped* — the earth brought in at the end of the age, as Baruch's good and evil seeds are gathered.$n$),
(58195, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 70, 2, $n$Behold! the days come, and it shall be when the time of the age has ripened, And the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, That the Mighty One will bring upon the earth and its inhabitants and upon its rulers Perturbation of spirit and stupor of heart.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 14, 15, $n$Rev 14:15 — *Thrust in thy sickle, and reap: for the time is come for thee to reap; for the harvest of the earth is ripe* — the harvest reaped when the time has ripened, Baruch's consummation in John's vision.$n$, $n$Revelation 14:15 — *Thrust in thy sickle, and reap: for the time is come for thee to reap; for the harvest of the earth is ripe* — the harvest reaped when the time has ripened, Baruch's consummation in John's vision.$n$, 14206, $n$Rev 14:15 — *Thrust in thy sickle, and reap: for the time is come for thee to reap; for the harvest of the earth is ripe* — the harvest reaped when the time has ripened, Baruch's consummation in John's vision.$n$, $n$Revelation 14:15 — *Thrust in thy sickle, and reap: for the time is come for thee to reap; for the harvest of the earth is ripe* — the harvest reaped when the time has ripened, Baruch's consummation in John's vision.$n$),
(58196, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 70, 2, $n$Behold! the days come, and it shall be when the time of the age has ripened, And the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, That the Mighty One will bring upon the earth and its inhabitants and upon its rulers Perturbation of spirit and stupor of heart.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 17, 5, $n$Isa 17:5 — *And it shall be as when the harvestman gathereth the corn, and reapeth the ears with his arm* — the prophet's harvest-figure for the day of reckoning, the ripened time Baruch describes.$n$, $n$Isaiah 17:5 — *And it shall be as when the harvestman gathereth the corn, and reapeth the ears with his arm* — the prophet's harvest-figure for the day of reckoning, the ripened time Baruch describes.$n$, 14205, $n$Isa 17:5 — *And it shall be as when the harvestman gathereth the corn, and reapeth the ears with his arm* — the prophet's harvest-figure for the day of reckoning, the ripened time Baruch describes.$n$, $n$Isaiah 17:5 — *And it shall be as when the harvestman gathereth the corn, and reapeth the ears with his arm* — the prophet's harvest-figure for the day of reckoning, the ripened time Baruch describes.$n$),
(58197, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 70, 2, $n$Behold! the days come, and it shall be when the time of the age has ripened, And the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, That the Mighty One will bring upon the earth and its inhabitants and upon its rulers Perturbation of spirit and stupor of heart.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 9, 38, $n$Matt 9:38 — *Pray ye therefore Yahuah (Lord) of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his harvest* — the Lord of the harvest who brings in the ripened age, the Mighty One of Baruch's vision.$n$, $n$Matthew 9:38 — *Pray ye therefore Yahuah (Lord) of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his harvest* — the Lord of the harvest who brings in the ripened age, the Mighty One of Baruch's vision.$n$, 14205, $n$Matt 9:38 — *Pray ye therefore Yahuah (Lord) of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his harvest* — the Lord of the harvest who brings in the ripened age, the Mighty One of Baruch's vision.$n$, $n$Matthew 9:38 — *Pray ye therefore Yahuah (Lord) of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his harvest* — the Lord of the harvest who brings in the ripened age, the Mighty One of Baruch's vision.$n$),
(58198, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 70, 2, $n$Behold! the days come, and it shall be when the time of the age has ripened, And the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, That the Mighty One will bring upon the earth and its inhabitants and upon its rulers Perturbation of spirit and stupor of heart.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 9, 37, $n$Matt 9:37 — *The harvest truly is plenteous, but the labourers are few* — the world named a harvest waiting to be reaped, the very image Baruch sees ripen.$n$, $n$Matthew 9:37 — *The harvest truly is plenteous, but the labourers are few* — the world named a harvest waiting to be reaped, the very image Baruch sees ripen.$n$, 14205, $n$Matt 9:37 — *The harvest truly is plenteous, but the labourers are few* — the world named a harvest waiting to be reaped, the very image Baruch sees ripen.$n$, $n$Matthew 9:37 — *The harvest truly is plenteous, but the labourers are few* — the world named a harvest waiting to be reaped, the very image Baruch sees ripen.$n$),
(58199, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 70, 2, $n$Behold! the days come, and it shall be when the time of the age has ripened, And the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, That the Mighty One will bring upon the earth and its inhabitants and upon its rulers Perturbation of spirit and stupor of heart.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 13, 39, $n$Matt 13:39 — *the harvest is the end of the world; and the reapers are the angels* — the ripening field of good and evil seed brought to its harvest, exactly Baruch's frame for the consummation.$n$, $n$Matthew 13:39 — *the harvest is the end of the world; and the reapers are the angels* — the ripening field of good and evil seed brought to its harvest, exactly Baruch's frame for the consummation.$n$, 14205, $n$Matt 13:39 — *the harvest is the end of the world; and the reapers are the angels* — the ripening field of good and evil seed brought to its harvest, exactly Baruch's frame for the consummation.$n$, $n$Matthew 13:39 — *the harvest is the end of the world; and the reapers are the angels* — the ripening field of good and evil seed brought to its harvest, exactly Baruch's frame for the consummation.$n$),
(58200, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 71, 1, $n$'And the holy land shall have mercy on its own, And it shall protect its inhabiters at that time.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 7, 3, $n$Rev 7:3 — *Hurt not the earth, neither the sea, nor the trees, till we have sealed the servants of our Elohim (God) in their foreheads* — the harm withheld until the Most High's own are secured, the sheltering Baruch promises the inhabiters of the holy land.$n$, $n$Revelation 7:3 — *Hurt not the earth, neither the sea, nor the trees, till we have sealed the servants of our Elohim (God) in their foreheads* — the harm withheld until the Most High's own are secured, the sheltering Baruch promises the inhabiters of the holy land.$n$, 14209, $n$Rev 7:3 — *Hurt not the earth, neither the sea, nor the trees, till we have sealed the servants of our Elohim (God) in their foreheads* — the harm withheld until the Most High's own are secured, the sheltering Baruch promises the inhabiters of the holy land.$n$, $n$Revelation 7:3 — *Hurt not the earth, neither the sea, nor the trees, till we have sealed the servants of our Elohim (God) in their foreheads* — the harm withheld until the Most High's own are secured, the sheltering Baruch promises the inhabiters of the holy land.$n$),
(58201, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 71, 1, $n$'And the holy land shall have mercy on its own, And it shall protect its inhabiters at that time.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 12, 1, $n$Dan 12:1 — *there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was... and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book* — the deliverance of the covenant people in the worst hour, the mercy on its own that Baruch sees.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:1 — *there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was... and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book* — the deliverance of the covenant people in the worst hour, the mercy on its own that Baruch sees.$n$, 14209, $n$Dan 12:1 — *there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was... and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book* — the deliverance of the covenant people in the worst hour, the mercy on its own that Baruch sees.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:1 — *there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was... and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book* — the deliverance of the covenant people in the worst hour, the mercy on its own that Baruch sees.$n$),
(58202, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 71, 1, $n$'And the holy land shall have mercy on its own, And it shall protect its inhabiters at that time.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 26, 20, $n$Isa 26:20 — *Come, my people, enter thou into thy chambers, and shut thy doors about thee: hide thyself as it were for a little moment, until the indignation be overpast* — the people sheltered while wrath passes, the holy land's protection Baruch names.$n$, $n$Isaiah 26:20 — *Come, my people, enter thou into thy chambers, and shut thy doors about thee: hide thyself as it were for a little moment, until the indignation be overpast* — the people sheltered while wrath passes, the holy land's protection Baruch names.$n$, 14209, $n$Isa 26:20 — *Come, my people, enter thou into thy chambers, and shut thy doors about thee: hide thyself as it were for a little moment, until the indignation be overpast* — the people sheltered while wrath passes, the holy land's protection Baruch names.$n$, $n$Isaiah 26:20 — *Come, my people, enter thou into thy chambers, and shut thy doors about thee: hide thyself as it were for a little moment, until the indignation be overpast* — the people sheltered while wrath passes, the holy land's protection Baruch names.$n$),
(58203, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 72, 4, $n$Every nation, which knows not Yashar'el (Israel) and has not trodden down the seed of Jacob, shall indeed be spared.$n$, 'canon', 'zechariah', 14, 9, $n$Zech 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth* — the kingdom established over the spared nations, the Messiah's reign Baruch's sparing prepares.$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth* — the kingdom established over the spared nations, the Messiah's reign Baruch's sparing prepares.$n$, 14211, $n$Zech 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth* — the kingdom established over the spared nations, the Messiah's reign Baruch's sparing prepares.$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth* — the kingdom established over the spared nations, the Messiah's reign Baruch's sparing prepares.$n$),
(58204, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 72, 6, $n$But all those who have ruled over you, or have known you, shall be given up to the sword.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 4, $n$Isa 11:4 — *But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth* — the just discernment of the Anointed, sparing the unoffending and giving the oppressor to the sword as Baruch tells.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:4 — *But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth* — the just discernment of the Anointed, sparing the unoffending and giving the oppressor to the sword as Baruch tells.$n$, 14211, $n$Isa 11:4 — *But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth* — the just discernment of the Anointed, sparing the unoffending and giving the oppressor to the sword as Baruch tells.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:4 — *But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth* — the just discernment of the Anointed, sparing the unoffending and giving the oppressor to the sword as Baruch tells.$n$),
(58205, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 72, 2, $n$After the signs have come, of which thou wast told before, when the nations become turbulent, and the time of My Messiah is come, he shall both summon all the nations, and some of them he shall spare, and some of them he shall slay.$n$, 'canon', 'zechariah', 14, 9, $n$Zech 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one Yahuah (LORD), and his name one* — the kingship that follows the summoning of the nations, the reign of Baruch's Anointed.$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one Yahuah (LORD), and his name one* — the kingship that follows the summoning of the nations, the reign of Baruch's Anointed.$n$, 14210, $n$Zech 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one Yahuah (LORD), and his name one* — the kingship that follows the summoning of the nations, the reign of Baruch's Anointed.$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one Yahuah (LORD), and his name one* — the kingship that follows the summoning of the nations, the reign of Baruch's Anointed.$n$),
(58206, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 72, 2, $n$After the signs have come, of which thou wast told before, when the nations become turbulent, and the time of My Messiah is come, he shall both summon all the nations, and some of them he shall spare, and some of them he shall slay.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 4, $n$Isa 11:4 — *with righteousness shall he judge the poor... and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Messiah who spares some and slays some, judging the nations by his word.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:4 — *with righteousness shall he judge the poor... and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Messiah who spares some and slays some, judging the nations by his word.$n$, 14210, $n$Isa 11:4 — *with righteousness shall he judge the poor... and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Messiah who spares some and slays some, judging the nations by his word.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:4 — *with righteousness shall he judge the poor... and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* — the Messiah who spares some and slays some, judging the nations by his word.$n$),
(58207, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 72, 2, $n$After the signs have come, of which thou wast told before, when the nations become turbulent, and the time of My Messiah is come, he shall both summon all the nations, and some of them he shall spare, and some of them he shall slay.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 10, $n$Isa 11:10 — *And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek* — the Anointed who summons all the nations, Baruch's Messiah revealed at the consummation.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:10 — *And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek* — the Anointed who summons all the nations, Baruch's Messiah revealed at the consummation.$n$, 14210, $n$Isa 11:10 — *And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek* — the Anointed who summons all the nations, Baruch's Messiah revealed at the consummation.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:10 — *And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek* — the Anointed who summons all the nations, Baruch's Messiah revealed at the consummation.$n$),
(58208, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 73, 6, $n$And wild beasts shall come from the forest and minister unto men, And asps and dragons shall come forth from their holes to submit themselves to a little child.$n$, 'canon', 'hosea', 2, 18, $n$Hos 2:18 — *in that day will I make a covenant for them with the beasts of the field, and with the fowls of heaven, and with the creeping things of the ground... and will make them to lie down safely* — the covenant with the beasts that makes them minister to men, exactly Baruch's reconciled creation.$n$, $n$Hosea 2:18 — *in that day will I make a covenant for them with the beasts of the field, and with the fowls of heaven, and with the creeping things of the ground... and will make them to lie down safely* — the covenant with the beasts that makes them minister to men, exactly Baruch's reconciled creation.$n$, 14213, $n$Hos 2:18 — *in that day will I make a covenant for them with the beasts of the field, and with the fowls of heaven, and with the creeping things of the ground... and will make them to lie down safely* — the covenant with the beasts that makes them minister to men, exactly Baruch's reconciled creation.$n$, $n$Hosea 2:18 — *in that day will I make a covenant for them with the beasts of the field, and with the fowls of heaven, and with the creeping things of the ground... and will make them to lie down safely* — the covenant with the beasts that makes them minister to men, exactly Baruch's reconciled creation.$n$),
(58209, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 73, 6, $n$And wild beasts shall come from the forest and minister unto men, And asps and dragons shall come forth from their holes to submit themselves to a little child.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 9, $n$Isa 11:9 — *They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain: for the earth shall be full of the knowledge of Yahuah (LORD)* — the creation reconciled under the Anointed, the little child to whom the serpents submit in Baruch's vision.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:9 — *They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain: for the earth shall be full of the knowledge of Yahuah (LORD)* — the creation reconciled under the Anointed, the little child to whom the serpents submit in Baruch's vision.$n$, 14213, $n$Isa 11:9 — *They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain: for the earth shall be full of the knowledge of Yahuah (LORD)* — the creation reconciled under the Anointed, the little child to whom the serpents submit in Baruch's vision.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:9 — *They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain: for the earth shall be full of the knowledge of Yahuah (LORD)* — the creation reconciled under the Anointed, the little child to whom the serpents submit in Baruch's vision.$n$),
(58210, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 73, 6, $n$And wild beasts shall come from the forest and minister unto men, And asps and dragons shall come forth from their holes to submit themselves to a little child.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 65, 25, $n$Isa 65:25 — *The wolf and the lamb shall feed together, and the lion shall eat straw like the bullock... They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain* — the beasts at peace and serving, the asp and dragon tamed in Baruch's kingdom.$n$, $n$Isaiah 65:25 — *The wolf and the lamb shall feed together, and the lion shall eat straw like the bullock... They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain* — the beasts at peace and serving, the asp and dragon tamed in Baruch's kingdom.$n$, 14213, $n$Isa 65:25 — *The wolf and the lamb shall feed together, and the lion shall eat straw like the bullock... They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain* — the beasts at peace and serving, the asp and dragon tamed in Baruch's kingdom.$n$, $n$Isaiah 65:25 — *The wolf and the lamb shall feed together, and the lion shall eat straw like the bullock... They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain* — the beasts at peace and serving, the asp and dragon tamed in Baruch's kingdom.$n$),
(58211, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 73, 2, $n$And then healing shall descend in dew, And disease shall withdraw, And anxiety and anguish and lamentation pass from amongst men, And gladness proceed through the whole earth.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 21, 4, $n$Rev 21:4 — *And Elohim (God) shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain* — anguish and lamentation passing from among men, healing descending as Baruch foretells.$n$, $n$Revelation 21:4 — *And Elohim (God) shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain* — anguish and lamentation passing from among men, healing descending as Baruch foretells.$n$, 14212, $n$Rev 21:4 — *And Elohim (God) shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain* — anguish and lamentation passing from among men, healing descending as Baruch foretells.$n$, $n$Revelation 21:4 — *And Elohim (God) shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain* — anguish and lamentation passing from among men, healing descending as Baruch foretells.$n$),
(58212, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 73, 3, $n$And no one shall again die untimely, Nor shall any adversity suddenly befall.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 65, 20, $n$Isa 65:20 — *There shall be no more thence an infant of days, nor an old man that hath not filled his days* — untimely death undone in the age of the Anointed, the very promise Baruch makes.$n$, $n$Isaiah 65:20 — *There shall be no more thence an infant of days, nor an old man that hath not filled his days* — untimely death undone in the age of the Anointed, the very promise Baruch makes.$n$, 14212, $n$Isa 65:20 — *There shall be no more thence an infant of days, nor an old man that hath not filled his days* — untimely death undone in the age of the Anointed, the very promise Baruch makes.$n$, $n$Isaiah 65:20 — *There shall be no more thence an infant of days, nor an old man that hath not filled his days* — untimely death undone in the age of the Anointed, the very promise Baruch makes.$n$),
(58213, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 73, 1, $n$'And it shall come to pass, when He has brought low everything that is in the world, And has sat down in peace for the age on the throne of His kingdom, That joy shall then be revealed, And rest shall appear.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 65, 19, $n$Isa 65:19 — *And I will rejoice in Jerusalem, and joy in my people: and the voice of weeping shall be no more heard in her, nor the voice of crying* — the joy revealed and grief banished in the kingdom, Baruch's gladness through the whole earth.$n$, $n$Isaiah 65:19 — *And I will rejoice in Jerusalem, and joy in my people: and the voice of weeping shall be no more heard in her, nor the voice of crying* — the joy revealed and grief banished in the kingdom, Baruch's gladness through the whole earth.$n$, 14212, $n$Isa 65:19 — *And I will rejoice in Jerusalem, and joy in my people: and the voice of weeping shall be no more heard in her, nor the voice of crying* — the joy revealed and grief banished in the kingdom, Baruch's gladness through the whole earth.$n$, $n$Isaiah 65:19 — *And I will rejoice in Jerusalem, and joy in my people: and the voice of weeping shall be no more heard in her, nor the voice of crying* — the joy revealed and grief banished in the kingdom, Baruch's gladness through the whole earth.$n$),
(58217, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 75, 7, $n$But if, indeed, we who exist know wherefore we have come, And submit ourselves to Him who brought us out of Egypt, We shall come again and remember those things which have passed, And shall rejoice regarding that which has been.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 20, $n$Deut 30:20 — *That thou mayest love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God)... and that thou mayest cleave unto him: for he is thy life, and the length of thy days* — to submit to and remember the Redeemer is life, the joy Baruch sets against grief.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:20 — *That thou mayest love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God)... and that thou mayest cleave unto him: for he is thy life, and the length of thy days* — to submit to and remember the Redeemer is life, the joy Baruch sets against grief.$n$, 14216, $n$Deut 30:20 — *That thou mayest love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God)... and that thou mayest cleave unto him: for he is thy life, and the length of thy days* — to submit to and remember the Redeemer is life, the joy Baruch sets against grief.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:20 — *That thou mayest love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God)... and that thou mayest cleave unto him: for he is thy life, and the length of thy days* — to submit to and remember the Redeemer is life, the joy Baruch sets against grief.$n$),
(58218, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 75, 7, $n$But if, indeed, we who exist know wherefore we have come, And submit ourselves to Him who brought us out of Egypt, We shall come again and remember those things which have passed, And shall rejoice regarding that which has been.$n$, 'canon', 'exodus', 20, 2, $n$Exod 20:2 — *I am Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), which have brought thee out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage* — the Redeemer to whom Baruch bids the people submit and so rejoice, the opening word of the law itself.$n$, $n$Exodus 20:2 — *I am Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), which have brought thee out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage* — the Redeemer to whom Baruch bids the people submit and so rejoice, the opening word of the law itself.$n$, 14216, $n$Exod 20:2 — *I am Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), which have brought thee out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage* — the Redeemer to whom Baruch bids the people submit and so rejoice, the opening word of the law itself.$n$, $n$Exodus 20:2 — *I am Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), which have brought thee out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage* — the Redeemer to whom Baruch bids the people submit and so rejoice, the opening word of the law itself.$n$),
(58219, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 75, 5, $n$Or who of those who are born can hope to come to those things, Unless he is one to whom Thou art merciful and gracious?$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 7, 8, $n$Deut 7:8 — *But because Yahuah (LORD) loved you, and because he would keep the oath which he had sworn unto your fathers* — the people come not by merit but by the mercy and grace Baruch says is the only door to the age to come.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 7:8 — *But because Yahuah (LORD) loved you, and because he would keep the oath which he had sworn unto your fathers* — the people come not by merit but by the mercy and grace Baruch says is the only door to the age to come.$n$, 14215, $n$Deut 7:8 — *But because Yahuah (LORD) loved you, and because he would keep the oath which he had sworn unto your fathers* — the people come not by merit but by the mercy and grace Baruch says is the only door to the age to come.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 7:8 — *But because Yahuah (LORD) loved you, and because he would keep the oath which he had sworn unto your fathers* — the people come not by merit but by the mercy and grace Baruch says is the only door to the age to come.$n$),
(58220, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 75, 1, $n$And I answered and said: 'Who can understand, O Yahuah (Lord), Thy goodness? For it is incomprehensible.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 11, 33, $n$Rom 11:33 — *O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of Elohim (God)! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!* — the incomprehensible goodness Baruch confesses none can search out.$n$, $n$Romans 11:33 — *O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of Elohim (God)! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!* — the incomprehensible goodness Baruch confesses none can search out.$n$, 14215, $n$Rom 11:33 — *O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of Elohim (God)! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!* — the incomprehensible goodness Baruch confesses none can search out.$n$, $n$Romans 11:33 — *O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of Elohim (God)! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!* — the incomprehensible goodness Baruch confesses none can search out.$n$),
(58221, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 76, 4, $n$Now this shall befall after forty days. Go now therefore during these days and instruct the people so far as thou art able, that they may learn so as not to die at the last time, but may learn in order that they may live at the last times.'$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 20, $n$Deut 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days* — the word learned and kept is the people's life at the last times, as Baruch is charged to teach.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days* — the word learned and kept is the people's life at the last times, as Baruch is charged to teach.$n$, 14217, $n$Deut 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days* — the word learned and kept is the people's life at the last times, as Baruch is charged to teach.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days* — the word learned and kept is the people's life at the last times, as Baruch is charged to teach.$n$),
(58222, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 76, 4, $n$Now this shall befall after forty days. Go now therefore during these days and instruct the people so far as thou art able, that they may learn so as not to die at the last time, but may learn in order that they may live at the last times.'$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 19, $n$Deut 30:19 — *I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live* — instruction given that the people may live and not die, the charge Baruch is sent to deliver.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:19 — *I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live* — instruction given that the people may live and not die, the charge Baruch is sent to deliver.$n$, 14217, $n$Deut 30:19 — *I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live* — instruction given that the people may live and not die, the charge Baruch is sent to deliver.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:19 — *I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live* — instruction given that the people may live and not die, the charge Baruch is sent to deliver.$n$),
(58223, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 77, 17, $n$Nevertheless, as ye said unto me, I will write also unto your brethren in Babylon, and I will send by means of men, and I will write in like manner to the nine tribes and a half, and send by means of a bird.'$n$, 'canon', 'jeremiah', 23, 3, $n$Jer 23:3 — *And I will gather the remnant of my flock out of all countries whither I have driven them, and will bring them again to their folds* — the scattered tribes gathered, the hope Baruch's epistle to the nine and a half tribes proclaims.$n$, $n$Jeremiah 23:3 — *And I will gather the remnant of my flock out of all countries whither I have driven them, and will bring them again to their folds* — the scattered tribes gathered, the hope Baruch's epistle to the nine and a half tribes proclaims.$n$, 14221, $n$Jer 23:3 — *And I will gather the remnant of my flock out of all countries whither I have driven them, and will bring them again to their folds* — the scattered tribes gathered, the hope Baruch's epistle to the nine and a half tribes proclaims.$n$, $n$Jeremiah 23:3 — *And I will gather the remnant of my flock out of all countries whither I have driven them, and will bring them again to their folds* — the scattered tribes gathered, the hope Baruch's epistle to the nine and a half tribes proclaims.$n$),
(58224, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 77, 13, $n$For the shepherds of Yashar'el (Israel) have perished, And the lamps which gave light are extinguished, And the fountains have withheld their stream whence we used to drink.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 12, 3, $n$Isa 12:3 — *Therefore with joy shall ye draw water out of the wells of salvation* — the fountain that does not dry up, the stream the law supplies in Baruch's answer.$n$, $n$Isaiah 12:3 — *Therefore with joy shall ye draw water out of the wells of salvation* — the fountain that does not dry up, the stream the law supplies in Baruch's answer.$n$, 14220, $n$Isa 12:3 — *Therefore with joy shall ye draw water out of the wells of salvation* — the fountain that does not dry up, the stream the law supplies in Baruch's answer.$n$, $n$Isaiah 12:3 — *Therefore with joy shall ye draw water out of the wells of salvation* — the fountain that does not dry up, the stream the law supplies in Baruch's answer.$n$),
(58225, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 77, 16, $n$If therefore ye have respect to the law, And are intent upon wisdom, A lamp will not be wanting, And a shepherd will not fail, And a fountain will not dry up.$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 6, 23, $n$Prov 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the commandment itself the lamp and the light, the law that abides though the leaders depart.$n$, $n$Proverbs 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the commandment itself the lamp and the light, the law that abides though the leaders depart.$n$, 14220, $n$Prov 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the commandment itself the lamp and the light, the law that abides though the leaders depart.$n$, $n$Proverbs 6:23 — *For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life* — the commandment itself the lamp and the light, the law that abides though the leaders depart.$n$),
(58226, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 77, 13, $n$For the shepherds of Yashar'el (Israel) have perished, And the lamps which gave light are extinguished, And the fountains have withheld their stream whence we used to drink.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 119, 105, $n$Ps 119:105 — *Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path* — the lamp that does not fail because it comes from the law, as Baruch declares to the remnant.$n$, $n$Psalm 119:105 — *Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path* — the lamp that does not fail because it comes from the law, as Baruch declares to the remnant.$n$, 14220, $n$Ps 119:105 — *Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path* — the lamp that does not fail because it comes from the law, as Baruch declares to the remnant.$n$, $n$Psalm 119:105 — *Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path* — the lamp that does not fail because it comes from the law, as Baruch declares to the remnant.$n$),
(58227, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 77, 13, $n$For the shepherds of Yashar'el (Israel) have perished, And the lamps which gave light are extinguished, And the fountains have withheld their stream whence we used to drink.$n$, 'canon', 'jeremiah', 23, 4, $n$Jer 23:4 — *And I will set up shepherds over them which shall feed them: and they shall fear no more, nor be dismayed* — the shepherds restored from Yahuah's word, the want Baruch says the law supplies.$n$, $n$Jeremiah 23:4 — *And I will set up shepherds over them which shall feed them: and they shall fear no more, nor be dismayed* — the shepherds restored from Yahuah's word, the want Baruch says the law supplies.$n$, 14220, $n$Jer 23:4 — *And I will set up shepherds over them which shall feed them: and they shall fear no more, nor be dismayed* — the shepherds restored from Yahuah's word, the want Baruch says the law supplies.$n$, $n$Jeremiah 23:4 — *And I will set up shepherds over them which shall feed them: and they shall fear no more, nor be dismayed* — the shepherds restored from Yahuah's word, the want Baruch says the law supplies.$n$),
(58228, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 77, 6, $n$If, therefore, ye direct your ways aright, Ye also shall not depart as your brethren departed, But they shall come to you.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 19, $n$Deut 30:19 — *I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live* — the choosing of the right way that the remnant may not depart, Baruch's call to direct their ways aright.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:19 — *I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live* — the choosing of the right way that the remnant may not depart, Baruch's call to direct their ways aright.$n$, 14219, $n$Deut 30:19 — *I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live* — the choosing of the right way that the remnant may not depart, Baruch's call to direct their ways aright.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:19 — *I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live* — the choosing of the right way that the remnant may not depart, Baruch's call to direct their ways aright.$n$),
(58229, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 77, 3, $n$For to you and to your fathers Yahuah (Lord) gave a law more excellent than to all peoples.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 19, 7, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the surpassing worth of the law Baruch names Israel's portion above the nations.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the surpassing worth of the law Baruch names Israel's portion above the nations.$n$, 14218, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the surpassing worth of the law Baruch names Israel's portion above the nations.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the surpassing worth of the law Baruch names Israel's portion above the nations.$n$),
(58230, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 77, 3, $n$For to you and to your fathers Yahuah (Lord) gave a law more excellent than to all peoples.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 4, 8, $n$Deut 4:8 — *And what nation is there so great, that hath statutes and judgments so righteous as all this law, which I set before you this day?* — the law more excellent than to all peoples, the gift Baruch sets before the remnant.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 4:8 — *And what nation is there so great, that hath statutes and judgments so righteous as all this law, which I set before you this day?* — the law more excellent than to all peoples, the gift Baruch sets before the remnant.$n$, 14218, $n$Deut 4:8 — *And what nation is there so great, that hath statutes and judgments so righteous as all this law, which I set before you this day?* — the law more excellent than to all peoples, the gift Baruch sets before the remnant.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 4:8 — *And what nation is there so great, that hath statutes and judgments so righteous as all this law, which I set before you this day?* — the law more excellent than to all peoples, the gift Baruch sets before the remnant.$n$),
(58231, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 78, 5, $n$that, at the last times, ye may be found worthy of your fathers.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 11, $n$Isa 11:11 — *Yahuah (Lord) shall set his hand again the second time to recover the remnant of his people, which shall be left* — the promised second gathering of the worn remnant at the last times.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:11 — *Yahuah (Lord) shall set his hand again the second time to recover the remnant of his people, which shall be left* — the promised second gathering of the worn remnant at the last times.$n$, 14224, $n$Isa 11:11 — *Yahuah (Lord) shall set his hand again the second time to recover the remnant of his people, which shall be left* — the promised second gathering of the worn remnant at the last times.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:11 — *Yahuah (Lord) shall set his hand again the second time to recover the remnant of his people, which shall be left* — the promised second gathering of the worn remnant at the last times.$n$),
(58232, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 78, 7, $n$For if ye so do these things, He will continually remember you, He who always promised on our behalf to those who were more excellent than we, that He will never forget or forsake us, but with much mercy will gather together again those who were dispersed.$n$, 'canon', 'jeremiah', 31, 10, $n$Jer 31:10 — *He that scattered Yashar'el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock* — the One who scattered is the One who gathers with much mercy.$n$, $n$Jeremiah 31:10 — *He that scattered Yashar'el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock* — the One who scattered is the One who gathers with much mercy.$n$, 14224, $n$Jer 31:10 — *He that scattered Yashar'el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock* — the One who scattered is the One who gathers with much mercy.$n$, $n$Jeremiah 31:10 — *He that scattered Yashar'el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock* — the One who scattered is the One who gathers with much mercy.$n$),
(58233, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 78, 7, $n$For if ye so do these things, He will continually remember you, He who always promised on our behalf to those who were more excellent than we, that He will never forget or forsake us, but with much mercy will gather together again those who were dispersed.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 4, $n$Deut 30:4 — *If any of thine be driven out unto the outmost parts of heaven, from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee* — no exile is too far to be regathered.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:4 — *If any of thine be driven out unto the outmost parts of heaven, from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee* — no exile is too far to be regathered.$n$, 14224, $n$Deut 30:4 — *If any of thine be driven out unto the outmost parts of heaven, from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee* — no exile is too far to be regathered.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:4 — *If any of thine be driven out unto the outmost parts of heaven, from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee* — no exile is too far to be regathered.$n$),
(58234, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 78, 7, $n$For if ye so do these things, He will continually remember you, He who always promised on our behalf to those who were more excellent than we, that He will never forget or forsake us, but with much mercy will gather together again those who were dispersed.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 3, $n$Deut 30:3 — *then Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations, whither Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath scattered thee* — the Torah's own oath to gather the dispersed with mercy.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:3 — *then Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations, whither Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath scattered thee* — the Torah's own oath to gather the dispersed with mercy.$n$, 14224, $n$Deut 30:3 — *then Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations, whither Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath scattered thee* — the Torah's own oath to gather the dispersed with mercy.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:3 — *then Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations, whither Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath scattered thee* — the Torah's own oath to gather the dispersed with mercy.$n$),
(58235, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 78, 3, $n$And truly I know that behold all we the twelve tribes are bound by one bond, inasmuch as we are born from one father.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 13, $n$Isa 11:13 — *Ephraim shall not envy Yahudah (Judah), and Yahudah (Judah) shall not vex Ephraim* — the old rivalry of the two houses healed in the one bond.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:13 — *Ephraim shall not envy Yahudah (Judah), and Yahudah (Judah) shall not vex Ephraim* — the old rivalry of the two houses healed in the one bond.$n$, 14223, $n$Isa 11:13 — *Ephraim shall not envy Yahudah (Judah), and Yahudah (Judah) shall not vex Ephraim* — the old rivalry of the two houses healed in the one bond.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:13 — *Ephraim shall not envy Yahudah (Judah), and Yahudah (Judah) shall not vex Ephraim* — the old rivalry of the two houses healed in the one bond.$n$),
(58236, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 78, 3, $n$And truly I know that behold all we the twelve tribes are bound by one bond, inasmuch as we are born from one father.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 12, $n$Isa 11:12 — *he shall... assemble the outcasts of Yashar'el (Israel), and gather together the dispersed of Yahudah (Judah) from the four corners of the earth* — both houses gathered as one from the four corners.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:12 — *he shall... assemble the outcasts of Yashar'el (Israel), and gather together the dispersed of Yahudah (Judah) from the four corners of the earth* — both houses gathered as one from the four corners.$n$, 14223, $n$Isa 11:12 — *he shall... assemble the outcasts of Yashar'el (Israel), and gather together the dispersed of Yahudah (Judah) from the four corners of the earth* — both houses gathered as one from the four corners.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:12 — *he shall... assemble the outcasts of Yashar'el (Israel), and gather together the dispersed of Yahudah (Judah) from the four corners of the earth* — both houses gathered as one from the four corners.$n$),
(58237, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 78, 3, $n$And truly I know that behold all we the twelve tribes are bound by one bond, inasmuch as we are born from one father.$n$, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 22, $n$Ezek 37:22 — *I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all* — the one bond restored, never two peoples again.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all* — the one bond restored, never two peoples again.$n$, 14223, $n$Ezek 37:22 — *I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all* — the one bond restored, never two peoples again.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all* — the one bond restored, never two peoples again.$n$),
(58238, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 78, 3, $n$And truly I know that behold all we the twelve tribes are bound by one bond, inasmuch as we are born from one father.$n$, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 19, $n$Ezek 37:19 — *Behold, I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim... and will put them with him, even with the stick of Yahudah (Judah), and make them one stick, and they shall be one in mine hand* — the two houses made one bond.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:19 — *Behold, I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim... and will put them with him, even with the stick of Yahudah (Judah), and make them one stick, and they shall be one in mine hand* — the two houses made one bond.$n$, 14223, $n$Ezek 37:19 — *Behold, I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim... and will put them with him, even with the stick of Yahudah (Judah), and make them one stick, and they shall be one in mine hand* — the two houses made one bond.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:19 — *Behold, I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim... and will put them with him, even with the stick of Yahudah (Judah), and make them one stick, and they shall be one in mine hand* — the two houses made one bond.$n$),
(58243, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 80, 4, $n$Your brethren also have they bound and led away to Babylon, and have caused them to dwell there.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 137, 1, $n$Ps 137:1 — *By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion* — the captivity to Babylon Baruch recounts to his brethren.$n$, $n$Psalm 137:1 — *By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion* — the captivity to Babylon Baruch recounts to his brethren.$n$, 14227, $n$Ps 137:1 — *By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion* — the captivity to Babylon Baruch recounts to his brethren.$n$, $n$Psalm 137:1 — *By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion* — the captivity to Babylon Baruch recounts to his brethren.$n$),
(58246, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 81, 4, $n$And the Mighty One did according to the multitude of His mercies, And the El Elyon (Most High) according to the greatness of His compassion, And He revealed unto me the word, that I might receive consolation, And He showed me visions that I should not again endure anguish, And He made known to me the mystery of the times, And the advent of the hours he showed me.$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 12, 1, $n$Dan 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up... and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book* — the mystery of the times and the deliverance shown to the seer for comfort.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up... and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book* — the mystery of the times and the deliverance shown to the seer for comfort.$n$, 14228, $n$Dan 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up... and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book* — the mystery of the times and the deliverance shown to the seer for comfort.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up... and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book* — the mystery of the times and the deliverance shown to the seer for comfort.$n$),
(58249, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 82, 7, $n$And we meditate on the beauty of their gracefulness, Though they have to do with pollutions, But as grass that withers shall they fade away.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 37, 2, $n$Ps 37:2 — *For they shall soon be cut down like the grass, and wither as the green herb* — the prosperity of the wicked fades like the grass that withers.$n$, $n$Psalm 37:2 — *For they shall soon be cut down like the grass, and wither as the green herb* — the prosperity of the wicked fades like the grass that withers.$n$, 14230, $n$Ps 37:2 — *For they shall soon be cut down like the grass, and wither as the green herb* — the prosperity of the wicked fades like the grass that withers.$n$, $n$Psalm 37:2 — *For they shall soon be cut down like the grass, and wither as the green herb* — the prosperity of the wicked fades like the grass that withers.$n$),
(58252, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 83, 22, $n$Since therefore all these things are done now, does anyone think that they will not be avenged? But the consummation of all things will come to the truth.]$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 12, 2, $n$Dan 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the consummation comes to the truth, when all things come to judgement.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the consummation comes to the truth, when all things come to judgement.$n$, 14234, $n$Dan 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the consummation comes to the truth, when all things come to judgement.$n$, $n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt* — the consummation comes to the truth, when all things come to judgement.$n$),
(58255, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 83, 4, $n$Let none therefore of these present things ascend into your hearts, but above all let us be expectant, because that which is promised to us shall come.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 40, 1, $n$Isa 40:1 — *Comfort ye, comfort ye my people, saith your Elohim (God)* — the consolation of the captives rests on the promise that surely comes.$n$, $n$Isaiah 40:1 — *Comfort ye, comfort ye my people, saith your Elohim (God)* — the consolation of the captives rests on the promise that surely comes.$n$, 14232, $n$Isa 40:1 — *Comfort ye, comfort ye my people, saith your Elohim (God)* — the consolation of the captives rests on the promise that surely comes.$n$, $n$Isaiah 40:1 — *Comfort ye, comfort ye my people, saith your Elohim (God)* — the consolation of the captives rests on the promise that surely comes.$n$),
(58259, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 84, 11, $n$For if He judge us not according to the multitude of His mercies, woe unto all us who are born.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 19, 11, $n$Ps 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — the keeping of the law that withholds the woe Baruch warns of, the law upheld as Israel's hope.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — the keeping of the law that withholds the woe Baruch warns of, the law upheld as Israel's hope.$n$, 14238, $n$Ps 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — the keeping of the law that withholds the woe Baruch warns of, the law upheld as Israel's hope.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:11 — *Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward* — the keeping of the law that withholds the woe Baruch warns of, the law upheld as Israel's hope.$n$),
(58262, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 84, 9, $n$And deliver ye this epistle and the traditions of the law to your sons after you, as also your fathers delivered (them) to you.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 4, 9, $n$Deut 4:9 — *lest they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life: but teach them thy sons, and thy sons' sons* — the law delivered to the children, the chain Baruch bids the tribes keep unbroken.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 4:9 — *lest they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life: but teach them thy sons, and thy sons' sons* — the law delivered to the children, the chain Baruch bids the tribes keep unbroken.$n$, 14237, $n$Deut 4:9 — *lest they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life: but teach them thy sons, and thy sons' sons* — the law delivered to the children, the chain Baruch bids the tribes keep unbroken.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 4:9 — *lest they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life: but teach them thy sons, and thy sons' sons* — the law delivered to the children, the chain Baruch bids the tribes keep unbroken.$n$),
(58263, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 84, 9, $n$And deliver ye this epistle and the traditions of the law to your sons after you, as also your fathers delivered (them) to you.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 32, 47, $n$Deut 32:47 — *For it is not a vain thing for you; because it is your life... ye shall prolong your days in the land* — the law handed to the sons after, as Baruch charges, because it is their very life.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:47 — *For it is not a vain thing for you; because it is your life... ye shall prolong your days in the land* — the law handed to the sons after, as Baruch charges, because it is their very life.$n$, 14236, $n$Deut 32:47 — *For it is not a vain thing for you; because it is your life... ye shall prolong your days in the land* — the law handed to the sons after, as Baruch charges, because it is their very life.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:47 — *For it is not a vain thing for you; because it is your life... ye shall prolong your days in the land* — the law handed to the sons after, as Baruch charges, because it is their very life.$n$),
(58264, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 84, 8, $n$And remember ye the law and Zion, and the holy land and your brethren, and the covenant of your fathers, and forget not the festivals and the sabbaths.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 19, 7, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law Baruch bids them remember is the perfect, abiding testimony.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law Baruch bids them remember is the perfect, abiding testimony.$n$, 14236, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law Baruch bids them remember is the perfect, abiding testimony.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple* — the law Baruch bids them remember is the perfect, abiding testimony.$n$),
(58265, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 84, 8, $n$And remember ye the law and Zion, and the holy land and your brethren, and the covenant of your fathers, and forget not the festivals and the sabbaths.$n$, 'canon', 'malachi', 4, 4, $n$Mal 4:4 — *Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb for all Yashar'el (Israel), with the statutes and judgments* — the closing charge of the prophets, the same word Baruch lays on the tribes.$n$, $n$Malachi 4:4 — *Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb for all Yashar'el (Israel), with the statutes and judgments* — the closing charge of the prophets, the same word Baruch lays on the tribes.$n$, 14236, $n$Mal 4:4 — *Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb for all Yashar'el (Israel), with the statutes and judgments* — the closing charge of the prophets, the same word Baruch lays on the tribes.$n$, $n$Malachi 4:4 — *Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb for all Yashar'el (Israel), with the statutes and judgments* — the closing charge of the prophets, the same word Baruch lays on the tribes.$n$),
(58266, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 84, 5, $n$And now Moses used to tell you before they befell you, and lo! they have befallen you: for ye have forsaken the law.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 4, 9, $n$Deut 4:9 — *take heed to thyself, and keep thy soul diligently, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes have seen... but teach them thy sons* — the forgetting of the law that Baruch says brought the predicted woe.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 4:9 — *take heed to thyself, and keep thy soul diligently, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes have seen... but teach them thy sons* — the forgetting of the law that Baruch says brought the predicted woe.$n$, 14235, $n$Deut 4:9 — *take heed to thyself, and keep thy soul diligently, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes have seen... but teach them thy sons* — the forgetting of the law that Baruch says brought the predicted woe.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 4:9 — *take heed to thyself, and keep thy soul diligently, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes have seen... but teach them thy sons* — the forgetting of the law that Baruch says brought the predicted woe.$n$),
(58267, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 84, 2, $n$Remember that formerly Moses assuredly called heaven and earth to witness against you and said: 'If ye transgress the law ye shall be dispersed, but if ye keep it ye shall be kept.'$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 20, $n$Deut 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land* — keep it and be kept, the promise Baruch repeats as the law's own terms.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land* — keep it and be kept, the promise Baruch repeats as the law's own terms.$n$, 14235, $n$Deut 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land* — keep it and be kept, the promise Baruch repeats as the law's own terms.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:20 — *for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land* — keep it and be kept, the promise Baruch repeats as the law's own terms.$n$),
(58268, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 84, 2, $n$Remember that formerly Moses assuredly called heaven and earth to witness against you and said: 'If ye transgress the law ye shall be dispersed, but if ye keep it ye shall be kept.'$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 19, $n$Deut 30:19 — *I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life* — the very witness and choice Baruch recalls Moses making.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:19 — *I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life* — the very witness and choice Baruch recalls Moses making.$n$, 14235, $n$Deut 30:19 — *I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life* — the very witness and choice Baruch recalls Moses making.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:19 — *I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life* — the very witness and choice Baruch recalls Moses making.$n$),
(58269, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 85, 10, $n$For the youth of the world is past, And the strength of the creation already exhausted, And the advent of the times is very short, Yea, they have passed by; And the pitcher is near to the cistern, And the ship to the port, And the course of the journey to the city, And life to (its) consummation.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 32, 47, $n$Deut 32:47 — *it is not a vain thing for you; because it is your life: and through this thing ye shall prolong your days* — the law set before life's consummation, the choice Baruch bids them make while the time is short.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:47 — *it is not a vain thing for you; because it is your life: and through this thing ye shall prolong your days* — the law set before life's consummation, the choice Baruch bids them make while the time is short.$n$, 14242, $n$Deut 32:47 — *it is not a vain thing for you; because it is your life: and through this thing ye shall prolong your days* — the law set before life's consummation, the choice Baruch bids them make while the time is short.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:47 — *it is not a vain thing for you; because it is your life: and through this thing ye shall prolong your days* — the law set before life's consummation, the choice Baruch bids them make while the time is short.$n$),
(58272, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 85, 11, $n$And again prepare your souls, so that when ye sail and ascend from the ship ye may have rest and not be condemned when ye depart.$n$, 'canon', 'hebrews', 9, 27, $n$Heb 9:27 — *as it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment* — the judgement after death for which Baruch bids them prepare their souls and not be condemned when they depart.$n$, $n$Hebrews 9:27 — *as it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment* — the judgement after death for which Baruch bids them prepare their souls and not be condemned when they depart.$n$, 14241, $n$Heb 9:27 — *as it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment* — the judgement after death for which Baruch bids them prepare their souls and not be condemned when they depart.$n$, $n$Hebrews 9:27 — *as it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment* — the judgement after death for which Baruch bids them prepare their souls and not be condemned when they depart.$n$),
(58276, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 85, 3, $n$But now the righteous have been gathered, And the prophets have fallen asleep, And we also have gone forth from the land, And Zion has been taken from us, And we have nothing now save the Mighty One and His law.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 119, 89, $n$Ps 119:89 — *For ever, O Yahuah (LORD), thy word is settled in heaven* — the law that abides though Zion falls, the one thing not taken away from Israel.$n$, $n$Psalm 119:89 — *For ever, O Yahuah (LORD), thy word is settled in heaven* — the law that abides though Zion falls, the one thing not taken away from Israel.$n$, 14239, $n$Ps 119:89 — *For ever, O Yahuah (LORD), thy word is settled in heaven* — the law that abides though Zion falls, the one thing not taken away from Israel.$n$, $n$Psalm 119:89 — *For ever, O Yahuah (LORD), thy word is settled in heaven* — the law that abides though Zion falls, the one thing not taken away from Israel.$n$),
(58277, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 85, 3, $n$But now the righteous have been gathered, And the prophets have fallen asleep, And we also have gone forth from the land, And Zion has been taken from us, And we have nothing now save the Mighty One and His law.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 19, 7, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure* — the law that remains to Israel when all else is taken, perfect and sure as Baruch confesses.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure* — the law that remains to Israel when all else is taken, perfect and sure as Baruch confesses.$n$, 14239, $n$Ps 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure* — the law that remains to Israel when all else is taken, perfect and sure as Baruch confesses.$n$, $n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure* — the law that remains to Israel when all else is taken, perfect and sure as Baruch confesses.$n$),
(58278, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 86, 2, $n$And meditate thereon, above all on the days of your fasts.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 1, 3, $n$Rev 1:3 — *Blessed is he that readeth, and they that hear the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written therein* — the blessing on reading, hearing, and keeping, as Baruch bids them read and meditate.$n$, $n$Revelation 1:3 — *Blessed is he that readeth, and they that hear the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written therein* — the blessing on reading, hearing, and keeping, as Baruch bids them read and meditate.$n$, 14243, $n$Rev 1:3 — *Blessed is he that readeth, and they that hear the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written therein* — the blessing on reading, hearing, and keeping, as Baruch bids them read and meditate.$n$, $n$Revelation 1:3 — *Blessed is he that readeth, and they that hear the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written therein* — the blessing on reading, hearing, and keeping, as Baruch bids them read and meditate.$n$),
(58280, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 86, 1, $n$When therefore ye receive this my epistle, read it in your congregations with care.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 31, 12, $n$Deut 31:12 — *Gather the people together, men, and women, and children... that they may hear, and that they may learn* — the law read before the gathered congregation, the pattern Baruch's epistle follows.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 31:12 — *Gather the people together, men, and women, and children... that they may hear, and that they may learn* — the law read before the gathered congregation, the pattern Baruch's epistle follows.$n$, 14243, $n$Deut 31:12 — *Gather the people together, men, and women, and children... that they may hear, and that they may learn* — the law read before the gathered congregation, the pattern Baruch's epistle follows.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 31:12 — *Gather the people together, men, and women, and children... that they may hear, and that they may learn* — the law read before the gathered congregation, the pattern Baruch's epistle follows.$n$),
(58282, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 87, 1, $n$And it came to pass when I had ended all the words of this epistle, and had written it sedulously to its close, that I folded it, and sealed it carefully, and bound it to the neck of the eagle, and dismissed and sent it.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 40, 31, $n$Isa 40:31 — *they that wait upon Yahuah (LORD) shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles* — the eagle's wings that carry the captive tribes' hope, as Baruch sends his word by the eagle.$n$, $n$Isaiah 40:31 — *they that wait upon Yahuah (LORD) shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles* — the eagle's wings that carry the captive tribes' hope, as Baruch sends his word by the eagle.$n$, 14244, $n$Isa 40:31 — *they that wait upon Yahuah (LORD) shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles* — the eagle's wings that carry the captive tribes' hope, as Baruch sends his word by the eagle.$n$, $n$Isaiah 40:31 — *they that wait upon Yahuah (LORD) shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles* — the eagle's wings that carry the captive tribes' hope, as Baruch sends his word by the eagle.$n$),
(58283, 'pseudepigrapha', '2-baruch', 87, 1, $n$And it came to pass when I had ended all the words of this epistle, and had written it sedulously to its close, that I folded it, and sealed it carefully, and bound it to the neck of the eagle, and dismissed and sent it.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 32, 11, $n$Deut 32:11 — *As an eagle stirreth up her nest, fluttereth over her young... beareth them on her wings* — the eagle of Moses' song that bears Israel, the figure Baruch's eagle-borne letter to the tribes answers to.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:11 — *As an eagle stirreth up her nest, fluttereth over her young... beareth them on her wings* — the eagle of Moses' song that bears Israel, the figure Baruch's eagle-borne letter to the tribes answers to.$n$, 14244, $n$Deut 32:11 — *As an eagle stirreth up her nest, fluttereth over her young... beareth them on her wings* — the eagle of Moses' song that bears Israel, the figure Baruch's eagle-borne letter to the tribes answers to.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 32:11 — *As an eagle stirreth up her nest, fluttereth over her young... beareth them on her wings* — the eagle of Moses' song that bears Israel, the figure Baruch's eagle-borne letter to the tribes answers to.$n$),
(59927, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 9, 13, $n$And I knew, my children, that because of Joseph this had befallen me, and I repented and wept; and I besought Yahuah Elohim (the Lord God) that my hand might be restored, and that I might hold aloof from all pollution and envy, 'and from all folly'.$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 27, 4, $n$Prov 27:4 — *Wrath is cruel, and anger is outrageous; but who is able to stand before envy?* — the unstanding-before-envy that left Simeon five months wrathful until his hand withered.$n$, $n$Proverbs 27:4 — *Wrath is cruel, and anger is outrageous; but who is able to stand before envy?* — the unstanding-before-envy that left Simeon five months wrathful until his hand withered.$n$, 14698, $n$Prov 27:4 — *Wrath is cruel, and anger is outrageous; but who is able to stand before envy?* — the unstanding-before-envy that left Simeon five months wrathful until his hand withered.$n$, $n$Proverbs 27:4 — *Wrath is cruel, and anger is outrageous; but who is able to stand before envy?* — the unstanding-before-envy that left Simeon five months wrathful until his hand withered.$n$),
(59928, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 9, 10, $n$And when Reuben heard these things he was grieved, for he wished to restore him to his father.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 37, 22, $n$Gen 37:22 — *And Reuben said unto them, Shed no blood, but cast him into this pit that is in the wilderness, and lay no hand upon him; that he might rid him out of their hands, to deliver him to his father again.* — Reuben's intent to restore Joseph, which the testament preserves: "he wished to restore him to his father."$n$, $n$Genesis 37:22 — *And Reuben said unto them, Shed no blood, but cast him into this pit that is in the wilderness, and lay no hand upon him; that he might rid him out of their hands, to deliver him to his father again.* — Reuben's intent to restore Joseph, which the testament preserves: "he wished to restore him to his father."$n$, 14698, $n$Gen 37:22 — *And Reuben said unto them, Shed no blood, but cast him into this pit that is in the wilderness, and lay no hand upon him; that he might rid him out of their hands, to deliver him to his father again.* — Reuben's intent to restore Joseph, which the testament preserves: "he wished to restore him to his father."$n$, $n$Genesis 37:22 — *And Reuben said unto them, Shed no blood, but cast him into this pit that is in the wilderness, and lay no hand upon him; that he might rid him out of their hands, to deliver him to his father again.* — Reuben's intent to restore Joseph, which the testament preserves: "he wished to restore him to his father."$n$),
(59929, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 9, 9, $n$For when I went to Shechem to bring ointment for the flocks, and Reuben to Dothan, where were our necessaries and all our stores, Yahudah (Judah) my brother sold him to the Ishmaelites.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 37, 27, $n$Gen 37:27 — *Come, and let us sell him to the Ishmeelites, and let not our hand be upon him; for he is our brother and our flesh. And his brethren were content.* — Judah's counsel that Simeon recalls, "Yahudah (Judah) my brother sold him to the Ishmaelites."$n$, $n$Genesis 37:27 — *Come, and let us sell him to the Ishmeelites, and let not our hand be upon him; for he is our brother and our flesh. And his brethren were content.* — Judah's counsel that Simeon recalls, "Yahudah (Judah) my brother sold him to the Ishmaelites."$n$, 14698, $n$Gen 37:27 — *Come, and let us sell him to the Ishmeelites, and let not our hand be upon him; for he is our brother and our flesh. And his brethren were content.* — Judah's counsel that Simeon recalls, "Yahudah (Judah) my brother sold him to the Ishmaelites."$n$, $n$Genesis 37:27 — *Come, and let us sell him to the Ishmeelites, and let not our hand be upon him; for he is our brother and our flesh. And his brethren were content.* — Judah's counsel that Simeon recalls, "Yahudah (Judah) my brother sold him to the Ishmaelites."$n$),
(59930, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 9, 14, $n$For I knew that I had devised an evil thing before Yahuah (Lord) and Jacob my father, on account of Joseph my brother, in that I envied him.$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 14, 30, $n$Prov 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* — Solomon's diagnosis of the envious heart that Simeon now repents of.$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* — Solomon's diagnosis of the envious heart that Simeon now repents of.$n$, 14697, $n$Prov 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* — Solomon's diagnosis of the envious heart that Simeon now repents of.$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* — Solomon's diagnosis of the envious heart that Simeon now repents of.$n$),
(59931, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 9, 7, $n$And I set my mind against him to destroy him, because the prince of deceit sent forth the spirit of jealousy and blinded my mind, so that I regarded him not as a brother, nor did I spare even Jacob my father.$n$, 'canon', '1-john', 3, 12, $n$1 Jn 3:12 — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* — the apostle traces brother-murder to envy, just as Simeon traces his plot to "the prince of deceit."$n$, $n$1 John 3:12 — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* — the apostle traces brother-murder to envy, just as Simeon traces his plot to "the prince of deceit."$n$, 14697, $n$1 Jn 3:12 — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* — the apostle traces brother-murder to envy, just as Simeon traces his plot to "the prince of deceit."$n$, $n$1 John 3:12 — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* — the apostle traces brother-murder to envy, just as Simeon traces his plot to "the prince of deceit."$n$),
(59932, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 9, 6, $n$For in the time of my youth I was jealous 'in many things' of Joseph, because my father loved him 'beyond all'.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 37, 11, $n$Gen 37:11 — *And his brethren envied him; but his father observed the saying.* — Moses' one word, "envied," is the seed of Simeon's whole testament.$n$, $n$Genesis 37:11 — *And his brethren envied him; but his father observed the saying.* — Moses' one word, "envied," is the seed of Simeon's whole testament.$n$, 14697, $n$Gen 37:11 — *And his brethren envied him; but his father observed the saying.* — Moses' one word, "envied," is the seed of Simeon's whole testament.$n$, $n$Genesis 37:11 — *And his brethren envied him; but his father observed the saying.* — Moses' one word, "envied," is the seed of Simeon's whole testament.$n$),
(59933, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 9, 6, $n$For in the time of my youth I was jealous 'in many things' of Joseph, because my father loved him 'beyond all'.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 37, 4, $n$Gen 37:4 — *And when his brethren saw that their father loved him more than all his brethren, they hated him, and could not speak peaceably unto him.* — the very father-love and brother-hate Simeon now confesses by name.$n$, $n$Genesis 37:4 — *And when his brethren saw that their father loved him more than all his brethren, they hated him, and could not speak peaceably unto him.* — the very father-love and brother-hate Simeon now confesses by name.$n$, 14697, $n$Gen 37:4 — *And when his brethren saw that their father loved him more than all his brethren, they hated him, and could not speak peaceably unto him.* — the very father-love and brother-hate Simeon now confesses by name.$n$, $n$Genesis 37:4 — *And when his brethren saw that their father loved him more than all his brethren, they hated him, and could not speak peaceably unto him.* — the very father-love and brother-hate Simeon now confesses by name.$n$),
(59935, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 10, 4, $n$Two years 'therefore' I afflicted my soul with fasting in the fear of Yahuah (Lord), and I learnt that deliverance from envy cometh by the fear of Elohim (God).$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 14, 27, $n$Prov 14:27 — *The fear of Yahuah (LORD) is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.* — the very deliverance Simeon found: "deliverance from envy cometh by the fear of Elohim (God)."$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:27 — *The fear of Yahuah (LORD) is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.* — the very deliverance Simeon found: "deliverance from envy cometh by the fear of Elohim (God)."$n$, 14700, $n$Prov 14:27 — *The fear of Yahuah (LORD) is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.* — the very deliverance Simeon found: "deliverance from envy cometh by the fear of Elohim (God)."$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:27 — *The fear of Yahuah (LORD) is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.* — the very deliverance Simeon found: "deliverance from envy cometh by the fear of Elohim (God)."$n$),
(59937, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 10, 2, $n$For envy ruleth over the whole mind of a man, and suffereth him 'neither to eat nor to drink', nor to do any good thing.$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 14, 30, $n$Prov 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* — the wasting Simeon describes, "he that envieth fadeth away."$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* — the wasting Simeon describes, "he that envieth fadeth away."$n$, 14699, $n$Prov 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* — the wasting Simeon describes, "he that envieth fadeth away."$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* — the wasting Simeon describes, "he that envieth fadeth away."$n$),
(59938, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 11, 8, $n$For this maketh savage the soul and destroyeth the body; it causeth anger and war in the mind, and stirreth up unto deeds of blood, and leadeth the mind into frenzy, 'and suffereth not prudence to act in men; moreover, it taketh away sleep', [and causeth tumult to the soul and trembling to the body].$n$, 'canon', 'galatians', 5, 21, $n$Gal 5:21 — *Envyings, murders, drunkenness, revellings, and such like... they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of Elohim (God).* — the savage works of the flesh, envy that "stirreth up unto deeds of blood."$n$, $n$Galatians 5:21 — *Envyings, murders, drunkenness, revellings, and such like... they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of Elohim (God).* — the savage works of the flesh, envy that "stirreth up unto deeds of blood."$n$, 14702, $n$Gal 5:21 — *Envyings, murders, drunkenness, revellings, and such like... they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of Elohim (God).* — the savage works of the flesh, envy that "stirreth up unto deeds of blood."$n$, $n$Galatians 5:21 — *Envyings, murders, drunkenness, revellings, and such like... they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of Elohim (God).* — the savage works of the flesh, envy that "stirreth up unto deeds of blood."$n$),
(59939, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 11, 7, $n$Do ye also, my children, love each one his brother with a good heart, and the spirit of envy will withdraw from you.$n$, 'canon', '1-john', 3, 14, $n$1 Jn 3:14 — *We know that we have passed from death unto life, because we love the brethren. He that loveth not his brother abideth in death.* — "love each one his brother with a good heart," the proof of life John names.$n$, $n$1 John 3:14 — *We know that we have passed from death unto life, because we love the brethren. He that loveth not his brother abideth in death.* — "love each one his brother with a good heart," the proof of life John names.$n$, 14702, $n$1 Jn 3:14 — *We know that we have passed from death unto life, because we love the brethren. He that loveth not his brother abideth in death.* — "love each one his brother with a good heart," the proof of life John names.$n$, $n$1 John 3:14 — *We know that we have passed from death unto life, because we love the brethren. He that loveth not his brother abideth in death.* — "love each one his brother with a good heart," the proof of life John names.$n$),
(59940, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 11, 7, $n$Do ye also, my children, love each one his brother with a good heart, and the spirit of envy will withdraw from you.$n$, 'canon', 'galatians', 5, 14, $n$Gal 5:14 — *For all the law is fulfilled in one word, even in this; Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.* — the brother-love Simeon commands, the law's one word.$n$, $n$Galatians 5:14 — *For all the law is fulfilled in one word, even in this; Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.* — the brother-love Simeon commands, the law's one word.$n$, 14702, $n$Gal 5:14 — *For all the law is fulfilled in one word, even in this; Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.* — the brother-love Simeon commands, the law's one word.$n$, $n$Galatians 5:14 — *For all the law is fulfilled in one word, even in this; Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.* — the brother-love Simeon commands, the law's one word.$n$),
(59941, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 11, 6, $n$All his days he reproached us not concerning this thing, but loved us as his own soul, and beyond his own sons glorified us, and gave us riches, and cattle and fruits.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 50, 21, $n$Gen 50:21 — *Now therefore fear ye not: I will nourish you, and your little ones. And he comforted them, and spake kindly unto them.* — Joseph who "gave us riches, and cattle and fruits" and reproached them not.$n$, $n$Genesis 50:21 — *Now therefore fear ye not: I will nourish you, and your little ones. And he comforted them, and spake kindly unto them.* — Joseph who "gave us riches, and cattle and fruits" and reproached them not.$n$, 14701, $n$Gen 50:21 — *Now therefore fear ye not: I will nourish you, and your little ones. And he comforted them, and spake kindly unto them.* — Joseph who "gave us riches, and cattle and fruits" and reproached them not.$n$, $n$Genesis 50:21 — *Now therefore fear ye not: I will nourish you, and your little ones. And he comforted them, and spake kindly unto them.* — Joseph who "gave us riches, and cattle and fruits" and reproached them not.$n$),
(59942, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 11, 4, $n$Now Joseph was a good man, and had the Spirit of Elohim (God) within him: being compassionate and pitiful, he bore no malice against me; but loved me even as the rest of his brethren.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 45, 5, $n$Gen 45:5 — *Now therefore be not grieved, nor angry with yourselves, that ye sold me hither: for Elohim (God) did send me before you to preserve life.* — Joseph comforting the very brothers Simeon confesses to, compassionate and pitiful.$n$, $n$Genesis 45:5 — *Now therefore be not grieved, nor angry with yourselves, that ye sold me hither: for Elohim (God) did send me before you to preserve life.* — Joseph comforting the very brothers Simeon confesses to, compassionate and pitiful.$n$, 14701, $n$Gen 45:5 — *Now therefore be not grieved, nor angry with yourselves, that ye sold me hither: for Elohim (God) did send me before you to preserve life.* — Joseph comforting the very brothers Simeon confesses to, compassionate and pitiful.$n$, $n$Genesis 45:5 — *Now therefore be not grieved, nor angry with yourselves, that ye sold me hither: for Elohim (God) did send me before you to preserve life.* — Joseph comforting the very brothers Simeon confesses to, compassionate and pitiful.$n$),
(59943, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 11, 4, $n$Now Joseph was a good man, and had the Spirit of Elohim (God) within him: being compassionate and pitiful, he bore no malice against me; but loved me even as the rest of his brethren.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 50, 20, $n$Gen 50:20 — *But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.* — Joseph's own word, the good man who "bore no malice against me."$n$, $n$Genesis 50:20 — *But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.* — Joseph's own word, the good man who "bore no malice against me."$n$, 14701, $n$Gen 50:20 — *But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.* — Joseph's own word, the good man who "bore no malice against me."$n$, $n$Genesis 50:20 — *But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.* — Joseph's own word, the good man who "bore no malice against me."$n$),
(59944, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 12, 6, $n$And they shall be few in number, divided in Levi and Yahudah (Judah), and there shall be none of you for sovereignty, even as also our father prophesied in his blessings.$n$, 'canon', 'zechariah', 6, 13, $n$Zech 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* — the division "in Levi and Yahudah (Judah)," priest and king at peace, that Simeon names.$n$, $n$Zechariah 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* — the division "in Levi and Yahudah (Judah)," priest and king at peace, that Simeon names.$n$, 14704, $n$Zech 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* — the division "in Levi and Yahudah (Judah)," priest and king at peace, that Simeon names.$n$, $n$Zechariah 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* — the division "in Levi and Yahudah (Judah)," priest and king at peace, that Simeon names.$n$),
(59945, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 12, 6, $n$And they shall be few in number, divided in Levi and Yahudah (Judah), and there shall be none of you for sovereignty, even as also our father prophesied in his blessings.$n$, 'canon', 'numbers', 24, 17, $n$Num 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)* — the sovereignty that falls not to Simeon but to the sceptre Balaam foresaw out of Judah.$n$, $n$Numbers 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)* — the sovereignty that falls not to Simeon but to the sceptre Balaam foresaw out of Judah.$n$, 14704, $n$Num 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)* — the sovereignty that falls not to Simeon but to the sceptre Balaam foresaw out of Judah.$n$, $n$Numbers 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)* — the sovereignty that falls not to Simeon but to the sceptre Balaam foresaw out of Judah.$n$),
(59946, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 12, 3, $n$Beware, therefore, of fornication, For fornication is mother of all evils, Separating from Elohim (God), and bringing near to Beliar.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 6, 11, $n$Gen 6:11 — *The earth also was corrupt before Elohim (God), and the earth was filled with violence.* — fornication "mother of all evils," filling the earth with corruption as in Noah's day.$n$, $n$Genesis 6:11 — *The earth also was corrupt before Elohim (God), and the earth was filled with violence.* — fornication "mother of all evils," filling the earth with corruption as in Noah's day.$n$, 14703, $n$Gen 6:11 — *The earth also was corrupt before Elohim (God), and the earth was filled with violence.* — fornication "mother of all evils," filling the earth with corruption as in Noah's day.$n$, $n$Genesis 6:11 — *The earth also was corrupt before Elohim (God), and the earth was filled with violence.* — fornication "mother of all evils," filling the earth with corruption as in Noah's day.$n$),
(59947, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 12, 3, $n$Beware, therefore, of fornication, For fornication is mother of all evils, Separating from Elohim (God), and bringing near to Beliar.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 6, 2, $n$Gen 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* — the fornication of the Watchers that "bringing near to Beliar," the root Enoch expounds.$n$, $n$Genesis 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* — the fornication of the Watchers that "bringing near to Beliar," the root Enoch expounds.$n$, 14703, $n$Gen 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* — the fornication of the Watchers that "bringing near to Beliar," the root Enoch expounds.$n$, $n$Genesis 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* — the fornication of the Watchers that "bringing near to Beliar," the root Enoch expounds.$n$),
(59949, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 13, 7, $n$Then shall I arise in joy, And will bless the El Elyon (Most High) because of His marvellous works, [Because Elohim (God) hath taken a body and eaten with men and saved men].$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 11, 10, $n$Isa 11:10 — *And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek: and his rest shall be glorious.* — the day Simeon shall "arise in joy," the rest of the appearing King.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:10 — *And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek: and his rest shall be glorious.* — the day Simeon shall "arise in joy," the rest of the appearing King.$n$, 14706, $n$Isa 11:10 — *And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek: and his rest shall be glorious.* — the day Simeon shall "arise in joy," the rest of the appearing King.$n$, $n$Isaiah 11:10 — *And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek: and his rest shall be glorious.* — the day Simeon shall "arise in joy," the rest of the appearing King.$n$),
(59950, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 13, 4, $n$Then shall fail the land of Ham, And all the people shall perish. Then shall all the earth rest from trouble, And all the world under heaven from war.$n$, 'canon', 'zechariah', 14, 11, $n$Zech 14:11 — *And men shall dwell in it, and there shall be no more utter destruction; but Jerusalem shall be safely inhabited.* — "all the earth rest from trouble, and all the world under heaven from war."$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:11 — *And men shall dwell in it, and there shall be no more utter destruction; but Jerusalem shall be safely inhabited.* — "all the earth rest from trouble, and all the world under heaven from war."$n$, 14706, $n$Zech 14:11 — *And men shall dwell in it, and there shall be no more utter destruction; but Jerusalem shall be safely inhabited.* — "all the earth rest from trouble, and all the world under heaven from war."$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:11 — *And men shall dwell in it, and there shall be no more utter destruction; but Jerusalem shall be safely inhabited.* — "all the earth rest from trouble, and all the world under heaven from war."$n$),
(59951, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 13, 6, $n$Then shall all the spirits of deceit be given to be trodden under foot, And men shall rule over wicked spirits.$n$, 'canon', 'zechariah', 14, 21, $n$Zech 14:21 — *in that day there shall be no more the Canaanite in the house of Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* — the spirits of deceit trodden under foot and the Canaanite removed in the day of the Lord.$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:21 — *in that day there shall be no more the Canaanite in the house of Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* — the spirits of deceit trodden under foot and the Canaanite removed in the day of the Lord.$n$, 14705, $n$Zech 14:21 — *in that day there shall be no more the Canaanite in the house of Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* — the spirits of deceit trodden under foot and the Canaanite removed in the day of the Lord.$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:21 — *in that day there shall be no more the Canaanite in the house of Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* — the spirits of deceit trodden under foot and the Canaanite removed in the day of the Lord.$n$),
(59952, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 13, 5, $n$Then the Mighty One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall glorify Shem, For Yahuah Elohim (the Lord God) shall appear on earth, And save the sons of men.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 9, 26, $n$Gen 9:26 — *Blessed be Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) of Shem; and Canaan shall be his servant.* — "the Mighty One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall glorify Shem" and Canaan perish, Noah's blessing fulfilled.$n$, $n$Genesis 9:26 — *Blessed be Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) of Shem; and Canaan shall be his servant.* — "the Mighty One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall glorify Shem" and Canaan perish, Noah's blessing fulfilled.$n$, 14705, $n$Gen 9:26 — *Blessed be Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) of Shem; and Canaan shall be his servant.* — "the Mighty One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall glorify Shem" and Canaan perish, Noah's blessing fulfilled.$n$, $n$Genesis 9:26 — *Blessed be Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) of Shem; and Canaan shall be his servant.* — "the Mighty One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall glorify Shem" and Canaan perish, Noah's blessing fulfilled.$n$),
(59953, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 13, 5, $n$Then the Mighty One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall glorify Shem, For Yahuah Elohim (the Lord God) shall appear on earth, And save the sons of men.$n$, 'canon', 'zechariah', 14, 9, $n$Zech 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one Yahuah (LORD), and his name one.* — "Yahuah Elohim shall appear on earth" when all the earth rests from war.$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one Yahuah (LORD), and his name one.* — "Yahuah Elohim shall appear on earth" when all the earth rests from war.$n$, 14705, $n$Zech 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one Yahuah (LORD), and his name one.* — "Yahuah Elohim shall appear on earth" when all the earth rests from war.$n$, $n$Zechariah 14:9 — *And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one Yahuah (LORD), and his name one.* — "Yahuah Elohim shall appear on earth" when all the earth rests from war.$n$),
(59954, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 13, 5, $n$Then the Mighty One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall glorify Shem, For Yahuah Elohim (the Lord God) shall appear on earth, And save the sons of men.$n$, 'canon', 'malachi', 3, 1, $n$Mal 3:1 — *and Yahuah (Lord), whom ye seek, shall suddenly come to his temple, even the messenger of the covenant... behold, he shall come, saith Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* — the Lord appearing on earth to save, the coming Simeon foresees.$n$, $n$Malachi 3:1 — *and Yahuah (Lord), whom ye seek, shall suddenly come to his temple, even the messenger of the covenant... behold, he shall come, saith Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* — the Lord appearing on earth to save, the coming Simeon foresees.$n$, 14705, $n$Mal 3:1 — *and Yahuah (Lord), whom ye seek, shall suddenly come to his temple, even the messenger of the covenant... behold, he shall come, saith Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* — the Lord appearing on earth to save, the coming Simeon foresees.$n$, $n$Malachi 3:1 — *and Yahuah (Lord), whom ye seek, shall suddenly come to his temple, even the messenger of the covenant... behold, he shall come, saith Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* — the Lord appearing on earth to save, the coming Simeon foresees.$n$),
(59955, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 14, 3, $n$Therefore I give you these commands that ye also may command your children, that they may observe them throughout their generations.$n$, 'canon', 'exodus', 13, 8, $n$Exod 13:8 — *And thou shalt shew thy son in that day, saying, This is done because of that which Yahuah (LORD) did unto me when I came forth out of Egypt.* — the charge to command one's children that Simeon repeats: "that ye also may command your children."$n$, $n$Exodus 13:8 — *And thou shalt shew thy son in that day, saying, This is done because of that which Yahuah (LORD) did unto me when I came forth out of Egypt.* — the charge to command one's children that Simeon repeats: "that ye also may command your children."$n$, 14708, $n$Exod 13:8 — *And thou shalt shew thy son in that day, saying, This is done because of that which Yahuah (LORD) did unto me when I came forth out of Egypt.* — the charge to command one's children that Simeon repeats: "that ye also may command your children."$n$, $n$Exodus 13:8 — *And thou shalt shew thy son in that day, saying, This is done because of that which Yahuah (LORD) did unto me when I came forth out of Egypt.* — the charge to command one's children that Simeon repeats: "that ye also may command your children."$n$),
(59956, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 14, 2, $n$For Yahuah (Lord) shall raise up from Levi as it were a High-priest, and from Yahudah (Judah) as it were a King [Elohim (God) and man], He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel).$n$, 'canon', 'hebrews', 7, 25, $n$Heb 7:25 — *Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto Elohim (God) by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* — "He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel)," the salvation arising from the two tribes.$n$, $n$Hebrews 7:25 — *Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto Elohim (God) by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* — "He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel)," the salvation arising from the two tribes.$n$, 14707, $n$Heb 7:25 — *Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto Elohim (God) by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* — "He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel)," the salvation arising from the two tribes.$n$, $n$Hebrews 7:25 — *Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto Elohim (God) by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* — "He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel)," the salvation arising from the two tribes.$n$),
(59957, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 14, 2, $n$For Yahuah (Lord) shall raise up from Levi as it were a High-priest, and from Yahudah (Judah) as it were a King [Elohim (God) and man], He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel).$n$, 'canon', 'hebrews', 7, 14, $n$Heb 7:14 — *For it is evident that our Lord sprang out of Juda; of which tribe Moses spake nothing concerning priesthood.* — the King out of Judah made a priest, the change Simeon's priest-king foretells.$n$, $n$Hebrews 7:14 — *For it is evident that our Lord sprang out of Juda; of which tribe Moses spake nothing concerning priesthood.* — the King out of Judah made a priest, the change Simeon's priest-king foretells.$n$, 14707, $n$Heb 7:14 — *For it is evident that our Lord sprang out of Juda; of which tribe Moses spake nothing concerning priesthood.* — the King out of Judah made a priest, the change Simeon's priest-king foretells.$n$, $n$Hebrews 7:14 — *For it is evident that our Lord sprang out of Juda; of which tribe Moses spake nothing concerning priesthood.* — the King out of Judah made a priest, the change Simeon's priest-king foretells.$n$),
(59958, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 14, 2, $n$For Yahuah (Lord) shall raise up from Levi as it were a High-priest, and from Yahudah (Judah) as it were a King [Elohim (God) and man], He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel).$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 110, 4, $n$Ps 110:4 — *Yahuah (LORD) hath sworn, and will not repent, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melek Tsadiq (Melchizedek).* — the High-priest from Levi who is also the King at the right hand, David's Lord.$n$, $n$Psalm 110:4 — *Yahuah (LORD) hath sworn, and will not repent, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melek Tsadiq (Melchizedek).* — the High-priest from Levi who is also the King at the right hand, David's Lord.$n$, 14707, $n$Ps 110:4 — *Yahuah (LORD) hath sworn, and will not repent, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melek Tsadiq (Melchizedek).* — the High-priest from Levi who is also the King at the right hand, David's Lord.$n$, $n$Psalm 110:4 — *Yahuah (LORD) hath sworn, and will not repent, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melek Tsadiq (Melchizedek).* — the High-priest from Levi who is also the King at the right hand, David's Lord.$n$),
(59959, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 14, 2, $n$For Yahuah (Lord) shall raise up from Levi as it were a High-priest, and from Yahudah (Judah) as it were a King [Elohim (God) and man], He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel).$n$, 'canon', 'zechariah', 6, 13, $n$Zech 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* — priest and king joined in one, the salvation from Levi and Judah.$n$, $n$Zechariah 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* — priest and king joined in one, the salvation from Levi and Judah.$n$, 14707, $n$Zech 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* — priest and king joined in one, the salvation from Levi and Judah.$n$, $n$Zechariah 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* — priest and king joined in one, the salvation from Levi and Judah.$n$),
(59960, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 14, 2, $n$For Yahuah (Lord) shall raise up from Levi as it were a High-priest, and from Yahudah (Judah) as it were a King [Elohim (God) and man], He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel).$n$, 'canon', 'numbers', 24, 17, $n$Num 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)* — the King from Judah whom Simeon bids his sons obey.$n$, $n$Numbers 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)* — the King from Judah whom Simeon bids his sons obey.$n$, 14707, $n$Num 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)* — the King from Judah whom Simeon bids his sons obey.$n$, $n$Numbers 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)* — the King from Judah whom Simeon bids his sons obey.$n$),
(59961, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 15, 4, $n$For the sorcerers told them, that on the departure of the bones of Joseph there should be throughout all the land darkness and gloom, and an exceeding great plague to the Egyptians, so that even with a lamp a man should not recognise his brother.$n$, 'canon', 'exodus', 13, 21, $n$Exod 13:21 — *And Yahuah (LORD) went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light* — light for Israel as the Egyptians sat in the darkness the sorcerers foretold at the bones' departure.$n$, $n$Exodus 13:21 — *And Yahuah (LORD) went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light* — light for Israel as the Egyptians sat in the darkness the sorcerers foretold at the bones' departure.$n$, 14709, $n$Exod 13:21 — *And Yahuah (LORD) went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light* — light for Israel as the Egyptians sat in the darkness the sorcerers foretold at the bones' departure.$n$, $n$Exodus 13:21 — *And Yahuah (LORD) went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light* — light for Israel as the Egyptians sat in the darkness the sorcerers foretold at the bones' departure.$n$),
(59963, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 15, 3, $n$For the bones of Joseph the Egyptians guarded in the tombs of the Kings.$n$, 'canon', 'exodus', 13, 19, $n$Exod 13:19 — *And Moses took the bones of Joseph with him: for he had straitly sworn the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you; and ye shall carry up my bones away hence with you.* — the very departure of Joseph's bones at the Exodus that the testament foresees.$n$, $n$Exodus 13:19 — *And Moses took the bones of Joseph with him: for he had straitly sworn the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you; and ye shall carry up my bones away hence with you.* — the very departure of Joseph's bones at the Exodus that the testament foresees.$n$, 14709, $n$Exod 13:19 — *And Moses took the bones of Joseph with him: for he had straitly sworn the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you; and ye shall carry up my bones away hence with you.* — the very departure of Joseph's bones at the Exodus that the testament foresees.$n$, $n$Exodus 13:19 — *And Moses took the bones of Joseph with him: for he had straitly sworn the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you; and ye shall carry up my bones away hence with you.* — the very departure of Joseph's bones at the Exodus that the testament foresees.$n$),
(59964, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 15, 3, $n$For the bones of Joseph the Egyptians guarded in the tombs of the Kings.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 50, 25, $n$Gen 50:25 — *And Joseph took an oath of the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.* — the oath behind the guarded bones of Joseph the testament names.$n$, $n$Genesis 50:25 — *And Joseph took an oath of the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.* — the oath behind the guarded bones of Joseph the testament names.$n$, 14709, $n$Gen 50:25 — *And Joseph took an oath of the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.* — the oath behind the guarded bones of Joseph the testament names.$n$, $n$Genesis 50:25 — *And Joseph took an oath of the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.* — the oath behind the guarded bones of Joseph the testament names.$n$),
(60167, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 79, 8, $n$Now this was the spirit of anger that persuaded me to crush Joseph as a leopard crusheth a kid.$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 14, 30, $n$Prov 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* The envy that made Dan crush at Joseph as a leopard at a kid.$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* The envy that made Dan crush at Joseph as a leopard at a kid.$n$, 14788, $n$Prov 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* The envy that made Dan crush at Joseph as a leopard at a kid.$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:30 — *A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.* The envy that made Dan crush at Joseph as a leopard at a kid.$n$),
(60173, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 80, 5, $n$And wherewith encompasseth it his eyes? With hatred of heart, so as to be envious of his brother.$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 14, 30, $n$Prov 14:30 — *but envy the rottenness of the bones.* The hatred of heart and envy of a brother that anger ends in, by Dan's own reckoning.$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:30 — *but envy the rottenness of the bones.* The hatred of heart and envy of a brother that anger ends in, by Dan's own reckoning.$n$, 14789, $n$Prov 14:30 — *but envy the rottenness of the bones.* The hatred of heart and envy of a brother that anger ends in, by Dan's own reckoning.$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:30 — *but envy the rottenness of the bones.* The hatred of heart and envy of a brother that anger ends in, by Dan's own reckoning.$n$),
(60174, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 80, 2, $n$For anger is blindness, and does not suffer one to see the face of any man with truth.$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 14, 29, $n$Prov 14:29 — *He that is slow to wrath is of great understanding: but he that is hasty of spirit exalteth folly.* The blindness of anger that Dan says cannot see a man's face with truth.$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:29 — *He that is slow to wrath is of great understanding: but he that is hasty of spirit exalteth folly.* The blindness of anger that Dan says cannot see a man's face with truth.$n$, 14789, $n$Prov 14:29 — *He that is slow to wrath is of great understanding: but he that is hasty of spirit exalteth folly.* The blindness of anger that Dan says cannot see a man's face with truth.$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:29 — *He that is slow to wrath is of great understanding: but he that is hasty of spirit exalteth folly.* The blindness of anger that Dan says cannot see a man's face with truth.$n$),
(60179, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 13, $n$And no longer shall Jerusalem endure desolation, Nor Yashar'el (Israel) be led captive; For Yahuah (Lord) shall be in the midst of it [living amongst men], And the Holy One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall reign over it [in humility and in poverty; and he who believeth on Him shall reign amongst men in truth].$n$, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 27, $n$Ezek 37:27 — *My tabernacle also shall be with them: yea, I will be their Elohim (God), and they shall be my people.* The Lord in the midst of His restored city, exactly as Dan promises Jerusalem.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:27 — *My tabernacle also shall be with them: yea, I will be their Elohim (God), and they shall be my people.* The Lord in the midst of His restored city, exactly as Dan promises Jerusalem.$n$, 14794, $n$Ezek 37:27 — *My tabernacle also shall be with them: yea, I will be their Elohim (God), and they shall be my people.* The Lord in the midst of His restored city, exactly as Dan promises Jerusalem.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:27 — *My tabernacle also shall be with them: yea, I will be their Elohim (God), and they shall be my people.* The Lord in the midst of His restored city, exactly as Dan promises Jerusalem.$n$),
(60180, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 13, $n$And no longer shall Jerusalem endure desolation, Nor Yashar'el (Israel) be led captive; For Yahuah (Lord) shall be in the midst of it [living amongst men], And the Holy One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall reign over it [in humility and in poverty; and he who believeth on Him shall reign amongst men in truth].$n$, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 22, $n$Ezek 37:22 — *and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* The end of captivity and division Dan foresees when the Lord dwells in the midst of Jerusalem.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* The end of captivity and division Dan foresees when the Lord dwells in the midst of Jerusalem.$n$, 14794, $n$Ezek 37:22 — *and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* The end of captivity and division Dan foresees when the Lord dwells in the midst of Jerusalem.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* The end of captivity and division Dan foresees when the Lord dwells in the midst of Jerusalem.$n$),
(60181, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 9, $n$And so when ye return to Yahuah (Lord) ye shall obtain mercy, And He shall bring you into His sanctuary, And He shall give you peace.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 3, $n$Deut 30:3 — *will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations.* The very return-and-mercy Dan promises when Israel turns back to the Lord.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:3 — *will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations.* The very return-and-mercy Dan promises when Israel turns back to the Lord.$n$, 14794, $n$Deut 30:3 — *will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations.* The very return-and-mercy Dan promises when Israel turns back to the Lord.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:3 — *will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations.* The very return-and-mercy Dan promises when Israel turns back to the Lord.$n$),
(60182, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 12, $n$And the saints shall rest in Eden, And in the New Jerusalem will the righteous rejoice, And it shall be unto the glory of Elohim (God) for ever.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 65, 18, $n$Isa 65:18 — *for, behold, I create Jerusalem a rejoicing, and her people a joy.* The rejoicing of the righteous in the New Jerusalem that Dan foresees.$n$, $n$Isaiah 65:18 — *for, behold, I create Jerusalem a rejoicing, and her people a joy.* The rejoicing of the righteous in the New Jerusalem that Dan foresees.$n$, 14793, $n$Isa 65:18 — *for, behold, I create Jerusalem a rejoicing, and her people a joy.* The rejoicing of the righteous in the New Jerusalem that Dan foresees.$n$, $n$Isaiah 65:18 — *for, behold, I create Jerusalem a rejoicing, and her people a joy.* The rejoicing of the righteous in the New Jerusalem that Dan foresees.$n$),
(60183, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 12, $n$And the saints shall rest in Eden, And in the New Jerusalem will the righteous rejoice, And it shall be unto the glory of Elohim (God) for ever.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 2, 9, $n$Gen 2:9 — *the tree of life also in the midst of the garden.* The Eden in which Dan's saints shall rest, the garden the New Jerusalem brings back.$n$, $n$Genesis 2:9 — *the tree of life also in the midst of the garden.* The Eden in which Dan's saints shall rest, the garden the New Jerusalem brings back.$n$, 14793, $n$Gen 2:9 — *the tree of life also in the midst of the garden.* The Eden in which Dan's saints shall rest, the garden the New Jerusalem brings back.$n$, $n$Genesis 2:9 — *the tree of life also in the midst of the garden.* The Eden in which Dan's saints shall rest, the garden the New Jerusalem brings back.$n$),
(60184, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 12, $n$And the saints shall rest in Eden, And in the New Jerusalem will the righteous rejoice, And it shall be unto the glory of Elohim (God) for ever.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 22, 2, $n$Rev 22:2 — *was there the tree of life... and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.* Eden's tree restored within the city — the rest Dan promises the saints.$n$, $n$Revelation 22:2 — *was there the tree of life... and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.* Eden's tree restored within the city — the rest Dan promises the saints.$n$, 14793, $n$Rev 22:2 — *was there the tree of life... and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.* Eden's tree restored within the city — the rest Dan promises the saints.$n$, $n$Revelation 22:2 — *was there the tree of life... and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.* Eden's tree restored within the city — the rest Dan promises the saints.$n$),
(60185, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 12, $n$And the saints shall rest in Eden, And in the New Jerusalem will the righteous rejoice, And it shall be unto the glory of Elohim (God) for ever.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 21, 2, $n$Rev 21:2 — *And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven*. The very New Jerusalem in which Dan says the righteous shall rejoice.$n$, $n$Revelation 21:2 — *And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven*. The very New Jerusalem in which Dan says the righteous shall rejoice.$n$, 14793, $n$Rev 21:2 — *And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven*. The very New Jerusalem in which Dan says the righteous shall rejoice.$n$, $n$Revelation 21:2 — *And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven*. The very New Jerusalem in which Dan says the righteous shall rejoice.$n$),
(60186, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 11, $n$And the captivity shall he take from Beliar [the souls of the saints], And turn disobedient hearts unto Yahuah (Lord), And give to them that call upon him eternal peace.$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 20, 6, $n$Rev 20:6 — *but they shall be priests of Elohim (God) and of Messiah (Christ), and shall reign with him a thousand years.* The saints whose captivity is taken from Beliar, reigning in the peace Dan promises them.$n$, $n$Revelation 20:6 — *but they shall be priests of Elohim (God) and of Messiah (Christ), and shall reign with him a thousand years.* The saints whose captivity is taken from Beliar, reigning in the peace Dan promises them.$n$, 14792, $n$Rev 20:6 — *but they shall be priests of Elohim (God) and of Messiah (Christ), and shall reign with him a thousand years.* The saints whose captivity is taken from Beliar, reigning in the peace Dan promises them.$n$, $n$Revelation 20:6 — *but they shall be priests of Elohim (God) and of Messiah (Christ), and shall reign with him a thousand years.* The saints whose captivity is taken from Beliar, reigning in the peace Dan promises them.$n$),
(60187, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 10, $n$And there shall arise unto you from the tribe of [Yahudah (Judah) and of] Levi the salvation of Yahuah (Lord); And he shall make war against Beliar, And execute an everlasting vengeance on our enemies;$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 20, 2, $n$Rev 20:2 — *And he laid hold on the dragon, that old serpent, which is the Devil, and Satan, and bound him a thousand years.* The binding of Beliar that Dan calls the war the Lord's salvation makes against him.$n$, $n$Revelation 20:2 — *And he laid hold on the dragon, that old serpent, which is the Devil, and Satan, and bound him a thousand years.* The binding of Beliar that Dan calls the war the Lord's salvation makes against him.$n$, 14792, $n$Rev 20:2 — *And he laid hold on the dragon, that old serpent, which is the Devil, and Satan, and bound him a thousand years.* The binding of Beliar that Dan calls the war the Lord's salvation makes against him.$n$, $n$Revelation 20:2 — *And he laid hold on the dragon, that old serpent, which is the Devil, and Satan, and bound him a thousand years.* The binding of Beliar that Dan calls the war the Lord's salvation makes against him.$n$),
(60189, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 10, $n$And there shall arise unto you from the tribe of [Yahudah (Judah) and of] Levi the salvation of Yahuah (Lord); And he shall make war against Beliar, And execute an everlasting vengeance on our enemies;$n$, 'canon', 'hebrews', 7, 14, $n$Heb 7:14 — *For it is evident that our Lord sprang out of Juda; of which tribe Moses spake nothing concerning priesthood.* The very fusion Dan foretells — the King out of Judah made also the priest, after the order of Melchizedek.$n$, $n$Hebrews 7:14 — *For it is evident that our Lord sprang out of Juda; of which tribe Moses spake nothing concerning priesthood.* The very fusion Dan foretells — the King out of Judah made also the priest, after the order of Melchizedek.$n$, 14791, $n$Heb 7:14 — *For it is evident that our Lord sprang out of Juda; of which tribe Moses spake nothing concerning priesthood.* The very fusion Dan foretells — the King out of Judah made also the priest, after the order of Melchizedek.$n$, $n$Hebrews 7:14 — *For it is evident that our Lord sprang out of Juda; of which tribe Moses spake nothing concerning priesthood.* The very fusion Dan foretells — the King out of Judah made also the priest, after the order of Melchizedek.$n$),
(60190, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 10, $n$And there shall arise unto you from the tribe of [Yahudah (Judah) and of] Levi the salvation of Yahuah (Lord); And he shall make war against Beliar, And execute an everlasting vengeance on our enemies;$n$, 'canon', 'numbers', 24, 17, $n$Num 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)*. Balaam's Sceptre, the king from Judah whom Dan joins with Levi as the salvation of the Lord.$n$, $n$Numbers 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)*. Balaam's Sceptre, the king from Judah whom Dan joins with Levi as the salvation of the Lord.$n$, 14791, $n$Num 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)*. Balaam's Sceptre, the king from Judah whom Dan joins with Levi as the salvation of the Lord.$n$, $n$Numbers 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)*. Balaam's Sceptre, the king from Judah whom Dan joins with Levi as the salvation of the Lord.$n$),
(60191, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 83, 10, $n$And there shall arise unto you from the tribe of [Yahudah (Judah) and of] Levi the salvation of Yahuah (Lord); And he shall make war against Beliar, And execute an everlasting vengeance on our enemies;$n$, 'canon', 'zechariah', 6, 13, $n$Zech 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* The joined priesthood and kingship — Levi and Judah — from which Dan says salvation arises.$n$, $n$Zechariah 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* The joined priesthood and kingship — Levi and Judah — from which Dan says salvation arises.$n$, 14791, $n$Zech 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* The joined priesthood and kingship — Levi and Judah — from which Dan says salvation arises.$n$, $n$Zechariah 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* The joined priesthood and kingship — Levi and Judah — from which Dan says salvation arises.$n$),
(60192, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 84, 7, $n$And His name shall be in every place of Yashar'el (Israel), 'and among the Gentiles'.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 4, $n$Deut 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee:* The Lord's name in every place of Israel and among the Gentiles — the gathering of the scattered Dan foresees.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee:* The Lord's name in every place of Israel and among the Gentiles — the gathering of the scattered Dan foresees.$n$, 14796, $n$Deut 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee:* The Lord's name in every place of Israel and among the Gentiles — the gathering of the scattered Dan foresees.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee:* The Lord's name in every place of Israel and among the Gentiles — the gathering of the scattered Dan foresees.$n$),
(60193, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 84, 6, $n$And it shall be in the time of the lawlessness of Yashar'el (Israel), that Yahuah (Lord) will (not) depart from them, but will transform them into a nation that doeth His will, for none of the angels will be equal unto him.$n$, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 23, $n$Ezek 37:23 — *but I will save them out of all their dwellingplaces, wherein they have sinned, and will cleanse them: so shall they be my people.* The transforming into a nation that does His will, which Dan promises the repentant.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:23 — *but I will save them out of all their dwellingplaces, wherein they have sinned, and will cleanse them: so shall they be my people.* The transforming into a nation that does His will, which Dan promises the repentant.$n$, 14796, $n$Ezek 37:23 — *but I will save them out of all their dwellingplaces, wherein they have sinned, and will cleanse them: so shall they be my people.* The transforming into a nation that does His will, which Dan promises the repentant.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:23 — *but I will save them out of all their dwellingplaces, wherein they have sinned, and will cleanse them: so shall they be my people.* The transforming into a nation that does His will, which Dan promises the repentant.$n$),
(60194, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 84, 4, $n$For he knoweth that on the day on which Yashar'el (Israel) shall repent, the kingdom of the enemy shall be brought to an end.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 2, $n$Deut 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), and shalt obey his voice according to all that I command thee this day, thou and thy children, with all thine heart*. The day of Israel's repentance on which Dan says the enemy's kingdom ends.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), and shalt obey his voice according to all that I command thee this day, thou and thy children, with all thine heart*. The day of Israel's repentance on which Dan says the enemy's kingdom ends.$n$, 14796, $n$Deut 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), and shalt obey his voice according to all that I command thee this day, thou and thy children, with all thine heart*. The day of Israel's repentance on which Dan says the enemy's kingdom ends.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), and shalt obey his voice according to all that I command thee this day, thou and thy children, with all thine heart*. The day of Israel's repentance on which Dan says the enemy's kingdom ends.$n$),
(60195, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 84, 2, $n$Draw near unto Elohim (God) and to the angel that intercedeth for you, for he is a mediator between Elohim (God) and man, and for the peace of Yashar'el (Israel) he shall stand up against the kingdom of the enemy.$n$, 'canon', 'hebrews', 7, 25, $n$Heb 7:25 — *seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* The intercession of the priest-king, exactly the office Dan ascribes to the one who pleads Israel's peace.$n$, $n$Hebrews 7:25 — *seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* The intercession of the priest-king, exactly the office Dan ascribes to the one who pleads Israel's peace.$n$, 14795, $n$Heb 7:25 — *seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* The intercession of the priest-king, exactly the office Dan ascribes to the one who pleads Israel's peace.$n$, $n$Hebrews 7:25 — *seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* The intercession of the priest-king, exactly the office Dan ascribes to the one who pleads Israel's peace.$n$),
(60357, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 131, 6, $n$Therefore was I called Benjamin, that is, a son of days.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 35, 24, $n$Gen 35:24 — *The sons of Rachel; Joseph, and Benjamin.* — the two sons of Rachel set side by side, the brotherhood that drives the whole testament.$n$, $n$Genesis 35:24 — *The sons of Rachel; Joseph, and Benjamin.* — the two sons of Rachel set side by side, the brotherhood that drives the whole testament.$n$, 14850, $n$Gen 35:24 — *The sons of Rachel; Joseph, and Benjamin.* — the two sons of Rachel set side by side, the brotherhood that drives the whole testament.$n$, $n$Genesis 35:24 — *The sons of Rachel; Joseph, and Benjamin.* — the two sons of Rachel set side by side, the brotherhood that drives the whole testament.$n$),
(60358, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 131, 3, $n$And since Rachel my mother died in giving me birth, I had no milk; therefore I was suckled by Bilhah her handmaid.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 35, 18, $n$Gen 35:18 — *And it came to pass, as her soul was in departing, (for she died) that she called his name Ben-oni: but his father called him Benjamin.* — Rachel's death in birth that Benjamin mourns, "since Rachel my mother died in giving me birth."$n$, $n$Genesis 35:18 — *And it came to pass, as her soul was in departing, (for she died) that she called his name Ben-oni: but his father called him Benjamin.* — Rachel's death in birth that Benjamin mourns, "since Rachel my mother died in giving me birth."$n$, 14850, $n$Gen 35:18 — *And it came to pass, as her soul was in departing, (for she died) that she called his name Ben-oni: but his father called him Benjamin.* — Rachel's death in birth that Benjamin mourns, "since Rachel my mother died in giving me birth."$n$, $n$Genesis 35:18 — *And it came to pass, as her soul was in departing, (for she died) that she called his name Ben-oni: but his father called him Benjamin.* — Rachel's death in birth that Benjamin mourns, "since Rachel my mother died in giving me birth."$n$),
(60359, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 131, 4, $n$For Rachel remained barren for twelve years 'after she had borne Joseph'; and she prayed Yahuah (Lord) with fasting twelve days, and she conceived and bare me.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 30, 24, $n$Gen 30:24 — *And she called his name Joseph; and said, Yahuah (LORD) shall add to me another son.* — Rachel's own prayer for a second son, which the testament says Jacob also prayed, "that he might see two sons born from her."$n$, $n$Genesis 30:24 — *And she called his name Joseph; and said, Yahuah (LORD) shall add to me another son.* — Rachel's own prayer for a second son, which the testament says Jacob also prayed, "that he might see two sons born from her."$n$, 14850, $n$Gen 30:24 — *And she called his name Joseph; and said, Yahuah (LORD) shall add to me another son.* — Rachel's own prayer for a second son, which the testament says Jacob also prayed, "that he might see two sons born from her."$n$, $n$Genesis 30:24 — *And she called his name Joseph; and said, Yahuah (LORD) shall add to me another son.* — Rachel's own prayer for a second son, which the testament says Jacob also prayed, "that he might see two sons born from her."$n$),
(60360, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 131, 4, $n$For Rachel remained barren for twelve years 'after she had borne Joseph'; and she prayed Yahuah (Lord) with fasting twelve days, and she conceived and bare me.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 30, 22, $n$Gen 30:22 — *And Elohim (God) remembered Rachel, and Elohim (God) hearkened to her, and opened her womb.* — the hearkened-to prayer Benjamin recalls, that his mother "prayed Yahuah with fasting twelve days, and she conceived."$n$, $n$Genesis 30:22 — *And Elohim (God) remembered Rachel, and Elohim (God) hearkened to her, and opened her womb.* — the hearkened-to prayer Benjamin recalls, that his mother "prayed Yahuah with fasting twelve days, and she conceived."$n$, 14850, $n$Gen 30:22 — *And Elohim (God) remembered Rachel, and Elohim (God) hearkened to her, and opened her womb.* — the hearkened-to prayer Benjamin recalls, that his mother "prayed Yahuah with fasting twelve days, and she conceived."$n$, $n$Genesis 30:22 — *And Elohim (God) remembered Rachel, and Elohim (God) hearkened to her, and opened her womb.* — the hearkened-to prayer Benjamin recalls, that his mother "prayed Yahuah with fasting twelve days, and she conceived."$n$),
(60361, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 132, 3, $n$And he said unto me: Even so, brother, when they had stripped me of my coat they gave me to the Ishmaelites, and they gave me a loin cloth, and scourged me, and bade me run.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 37, 28, $n$Gen 37:28 — *and sold Joseph to the Ishmeelites for twenty pieces of silver: and they brought Joseph into Egypt.* — the very sale Joseph names, "they gave me to the Ishmaelites."$n$, $n$Genesis 37:28 — *and sold Joseph to the Ishmeelites for twenty pieces of silver: and they brought Joseph into Egypt.* — the very sale Joseph names, "they gave me to the Ishmaelites."$n$, 14851, $n$Gen 37:28 — *and sold Joseph to the Ishmeelites for twenty pieces of silver: and they brought Joseph into Egypt.* — the very sale Joseph names, "they gave me to the Ishmaelites."$n$, $n$Genesis 37:28 — *and sold Joseph to the Ishmeelites for twenty pieces of silver: and they brought Joseph into Egypt.* — the very sale Joseph names, "they gave me to the Ishmaelites."$n$),
(60362, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 132, 3, $n$And he said unto me: Even so, brother, when they had stripped me of my coat they gave me to the Ishmaelites, and they gave me a loin cloth, and scourged me, and bade me run.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 37, 23, $n$Gen 37:23 — *they stript Joseph out of his coat, his coat of many colours that was on him.* — the stripping Joseph recalls, "when they had stripped me of my coat."$n$, $n$Genesis 37:23 — *they stript Joseph out of his coat, his coat of many colours that was on him.* — the stripping Joseph recalls, "when they had stripped me of my coat."$n$, 14851, $n$Gen 37:23 — *they stript Joseph out of his coat, his coat of many colours that was on him.* — the stripping Joseph recalls, "when they had stripped me of my coat."$n$, $n$Genesis 37:23 — *they stript Joseph out of his coat, his coat of many colours that was on him.* — the stripping Joseph recalls, "when they had stripped me of my coat."$n$),
(60363, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 132, 2, $n$And I said 'unto him', They dabbled thy coat with blood and sent it, and said: Know whether this be thy son's coat.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 37, 31, $n$Gen 37:31 — *And they took Joseph's coat, and killed a kid of the goats, and dipped the coat in the blood.* — the bloodied coat Benjamin describes, "they dabbled thy coat with blood and sent it."$n$, $n$Genesis 37:31 — *And they took Joseph's coat, and killed a kid of the goats, and dipped the coat in the blood.* — the bloodied coat Benjamin describes, "they dabbled thy coat with blood and sent it."$n$, 14851, $n$Gen 37:31 — *And they took Joseph's coat, and killed a kid of the goats, and dipped the coat in the blood.* — the bloodied coat Benjamin describes, "they dabbled thy coat with blood and sent it."$n$, $n$Genesis 37:31 — *And they took Joseph's coat, and killed a kid of the goats, and dipped the coat in the blood.* — the bloodied coat Benjamin describes, "they dabbled thy coat with blood and sent it."$n$),
(60365, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 133, 8, $n$In thee shall be fulfilled the prophecy of heaven [concerning the Lamb of Elohim (God), and Saviour of the world], that a blameless one shall be delivered up for lawless men, and a sinless shall die for ungodly men [in the blood of the covenant, for the salvation of the Gentiles and 'of Israel', and shall destroy Beliar and his servants].$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 49, 6, $n$Isa 49:6 — *I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.* — the salvation reaching to the Gentiles that the prophecy names, "for the salvation of the Gentiles and of Israel."$n$, $n$Isaiah 49:6 — *I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.* — the salvation reaching to the Gentiles that the prophecy names, "for the salvation of the Gentiles and of Israel."$n$, 14854, $n$Isa 49:6 — *I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.* — the salvation reaching to the Gentiles that the prophecy names, "for the salvation of the Gentiles and of Israel."$n$, $n$Isaiah 49:6 — *I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.* — the salvation reaching to the Gentiles that the prophecy names, "for the salvation of the Gentiles and of Israel."$n$),
(60367, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 133, 6, $n$For Joseph also besought our father 'that he would pray for his brethren', that 'the Lord' would not impute to them as sin whatever evil they had done unto him.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 50, 20, $n$Gen 50:20 — *But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.* — the good-man's word turning his brothers' evil to salvation, the keystone of Joseph's mercy.$n$, $n$Genesis 50:20 — *But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.* — the good-man's word turning his brothers' evil to salvation, the keystone of Joseph's mercy.$n$, 14853, $n$Gen 50:20 — *But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.* — the good-man's word turning his brothers' evil to salvation, the keystone of Joseph's mercy.$n$, $n$Genesis 50:20 — *But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.* — the good-man's word turning his brothers' evil to salvation, the keystone of Joseph's mercy.$n$),
(60368, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 133, 6, $n$For Joseph also besought our father 'that he would pray for his brethren', that 'the Lord' would not impute to them as sin whatever evil they had done unto him.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 50, 17, $n$Gen 50:17 — *Forgive, I pray thee now, the trespass of thy brethren, and their sin; for they did unto thee evil... And Joseph wept when they spake unto him.* — the forgiveness Benjamin recalls, that Joseph asked the sin not be imputed to them.$n$, $n$Genesis 50:17 — *Forgive, I pray thee now, the trespass of thy brethren, and their sin; for they did unto thee evil... And Joseph wept when they spake unto him.* — the forgiveness Benjamin recalls, that Joseph asked the sin not be imputed to them.$n$, 14853, $n$Gen 50:17 — *Forgive, I pray thee now, the trespass of thy brethren, and their sin; for they did unto thee evil... And Joseph wept when they spake unto him.* — the forgiveness Benjamin recalls, that Joseph asked the sin not be imputed to them.$n$, $n$Genesis 50:17 — *Forgive, I pray thee now, the trespass of thy brethren, and their sin; for they did unto thee evil... And Joseph wept when they spake unto him.* — the forgiveness Benjamin recalls, that Joseph asked the sin not be imputed to them.$n$),
(60369, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 133, 4, $n$How many men wished to slay him, and Elohim (God) shielded him! For he that feareth Elohim (God) and loveth his neighbour cannot be smitten by the spirit of Beliar, being shielded by the fear of Elohim (God).$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 5, 8, $n$Matt 5:8 — *Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see Elohim (God).* — the pure mind that "seeth all things rightly," shielded by the fear of God.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:8 — *Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see Elohim (God).* — the pure mind that "seeth all things rightly," shielded by the fear of God.$n$, 14852, $n$Matt 5:8 — *Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see Elohim (God).* — the pure mind that "seeth all things rightly," shielded by the fear of God.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:8 — *Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see Elohim (God).* — the pure mind that "seeth all things rightly," shielded by the fear of God.$n$),
(60370, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 133, 3, $n$Fear ye Yahuah (Lord), and love your neighbour; and even though the spirits of Beliar claim you to afflict you with every evil, yet shall they not have dominion over you, even as they had not over Joseph my brother.$n$, 'canon', 'leviticus', 19, 18, $n$Lev 19:18 — *thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* — the neighbour-love Benjamin couples to the fear of God as the shield against Beliar.$n$, $n$Leviticus 19:18 — *thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* — the neighbour-love Benjamin couples to the fear of God as the shield against Beliar.$n$, 14852, $n$Lev 19:18 — *thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* — the neighbour-love Benjamin couples to the fear of God as the shield against Beliar.$n$, $n$Leviticus 19:18 — *thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* — the neighbour-love Benjamin couples to the fear of God as the shield against Beliar.$n$),
(60371, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 133, 1, $n$Do ye also, therefore, my children, love Yahuah Elohim (the Lord God) of heaven and earth, and keep His commandments, following the example of the good and holy man 'Joseph'.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 16, $n$Deut 30:16 — *to love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to walk in his ways, and to keep his commandments and his statutes and his judgments, that thou mayest live.* — the love-and-keep Moses set before Israel, which Benjamin repeats to his sons.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:16 — *to love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to walk in his ways, and to keep his commandments and his statutes and his judgments, that thou mayest live.* — the love-and-keep Moses set before Israel, which Benjamin repeats to his sons.$n$, 14852, $n$Deut 30:16 — *to love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to walk in his ways, and to keep his commandments and his statutes and his judgments, that thou mayest live.* — the love-and-keep Moses set before Israel, which Benjamin repeats to his sons.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:16 — *to love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to walk in his ways, and to keep his commandments and his statutes and his judgments, that thou mayest live.* — the love-and-keep Moses set before Israel, which Benjamin repeats to his sons.$n$),
(60372, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 134, 4, $n$If any one is glorified, he envieth him not; if any one is enriched, he is not jealous; if any one is valiant, he praiseth him; the virtuous man he laudeth; 'on the poor man he hath mercy; on the weak he hath compassion; unto Elohim (God) he singeth praises'.$n$, 'canon', 'proverbs', 14, 31, $n$Prov 14:31 — *He that oppresseth the poor reproacheth his Maker: but he that honoureth him hath mercy on the poor.* — the mercy on the poor and compassion on the weak that marks the good man.$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:31 — *He that oppresseth the poor reproacheth his Maker: but he that honoureth him hath mercy on the poor.* — the mercy on the poor and compassion on the weak that marks the good man.$n$, 14856, $n$Prov 14:31 — *He that oppresseth the poor reproacheth his Maker: but he that honoureth him hath mercy on the poor.* — the mercy on the poor and compassion on the weak that marks the good man.$n$, $n$Proverbs 14:31 — *He that oppresseth the poor reproacheth his Maker: but he that honoureth him hath mercy on the poor.* — the mercy on the poor and compassion on the weak that marks the good man.$n$),
(60373, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 134, 4, $n$If any one is glorified, he envieth him not; if any one is enriched, he is not jealous; if any one is valiant, he praiseth him; the virtuous man he laudeth; 'on the poor man he hath mercy; on the weak he hath compassion; unto Elohim (God) he singeth praises'.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 12, 15, $n$Rom 12:15 — *Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep.* — the un-envying heart that praises the valiant and laughs not at another's good.$n$, $n$Romans 12:15 — *Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep.* — the un-envying heart that praises the valiant and laughs not at another's good.$n$, 14856, $n$Rom 12:15 — *Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep.* — the un-envying heart that praises the valiant and laughs not at another's good.$n$, $n$Romans 12:15 — *Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep.* — the un-envying heart that praises the valiant and laughs not at another's good.$n$),
(60374, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 134, 3, $n$'And though they devise with evil intent concerning him, by doing good he overcometh evil, being shielded by God'; and he loveth the righteous as his own soul.$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 12, 21, $n$Rom 12:21 — *Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.* — the very overcoming Benjamin names, "by doing good he overcometh evil."$n$, $n$Romans 12:21 — *Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.* — the very overcoming Benjamin names, "by doing good he overcometh evil."$n$, 14856, $n$Rom 12:21 — *Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.* — the very overcoming Benjamin names, "by doing good he overcometh evil."$n$, $n$Romans 12:21 — *Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.* — the very overcoming Benjamin names, "by doing good he overcometh evil."$n$),
(60375, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 134, 4, $n$If any one is glorified, he envieth him not; if any one is enriched, he is not jealous; if any one is valiant, he praiseth him; the virtuous man he laudeth; 'on the poor man he hath mercy; on the weak he hath compassion; unto Elohim (God) he singeth praises'.$n$, 'canon', 'leviticus', 19, 18, $n$Lev 19:18 — *thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* — the love of the righteous "as his own soul" that crowns the good man's mercy.$n$, $n$Leviticus 19:18 — *thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* — the love of the righteous "as his own soul" that crowns the good man's mercy.$n$, 14855, $n$Lev 19:18 — *thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* — the love of the righteous "as his own soul" that crowns the good man's mercy.$n$, $n$Leviticus 19:18 — *thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* — the love of the righteous "as his own soul" that crowns the good man's mercy.$n$),
(60376, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 134, 2, $n$For the good man hath not a 'dark eye'; for he showeth mercy to all men, even though they be sinners.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 5, 7, $n$Matt 5:7 — *Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.* — the mercy to all, even to sinners, that the good man shows.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:7 — *Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.* — the mercy to all, even to sinners, that the good man shows.$n$, 14855, $n$Matt 5:7 — *Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.* — the mercy to all, even to sinners, that the good man shows.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:7 — *Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.* — the mercy to all, even to sinners, that the good man shows.$n$),
(60377, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 134, 2, $n$For the good man hath not a 'dark eye'; for he showeth mercy to all men, even though they be sinners.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 6, 22, $n$Matt 6:22 — *The light of the body is the eye: if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall be full of light.* — the single eye against the "dark eye" Benjamin names as the mark of the good man.$n$, $n$Matthew 6:22 — *The light of the body is the eye: if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall be full of light.* — the single eye against the "dark eye" Benjamin names as the mark of the good man.$n$, 14855, $n$Matt 6:22 — *The light of the body is the eye: if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall be full of light.* — the single eye against the "dark eye" Benjamin names as the mark of the good man.$n$, $n$Matthew 6:22 — *The light of the body is the eye: if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall be full of light.* — the single eye against the "dark eye" Benjamin names as the mark of the good man.$n$),
(60378, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 135, 5, $n$And if any one betrayeth a righteous man, the righteous man prayeth: though for a little he be humbled, yet not long after he appeareth far more glorious, as was Joseph my brother.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 49, 7, $n$Isa 49:7 — *to him whom man despiseth, to him whom the nation abhorreth... Kings shall see and arise.* — the despised one lifted to honour, the Servant-pattern of humbled-then-glorious.$n$, $n$Isaiah 49:7 — *to him whom man despiseth, to him whom the nation abhorreth... Kings shall see and arise.* — the despised one lifted to honour, the Servant-pattern of humbled-then-glorious.$n$, 14857, $n$Isa 49:7 — *to him whom man despiseth, to him whom the nation abhorreth... Kings shall see and arise.* — the despised one lifted to honour, the Servant-pattern of humbled-then-glorious.$n$, $n$Isaiah 49:7 — *to him whom man despiseth, to him whom the nation abhorreth... Kings shall see and arise.* — the despised one lifted to honour, the Servant-pattern of humbled-then-glorious.$n$),
(60379, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 135, 5, $n$And if any one betrayeth a righteous man, the righteous man prayeth: though for a little he be humbled, yet not long after he appeareth far more glorious, as was Joseph my brother.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 50, 20, $n$Gen 50:20 — *ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good... to save much people alive.* — Joseph humbled by betrayal yet raised to save, the example Benjamin names, "as was Joseph my brother."$n$, $n$Genesis 50:20 — *ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good... to save much people alive.* — Joseph humbled by betrayal yet raised to save, the example Benjamin names, "as was Joseph my brother."$n$, 14857, $n$Gen 50:20 — *ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good... to save much people alive.* — Joseph humbled by betrayal yet raised to save, the example Benjamin names, "as was Joseph my brother."$n$, $n$Genesis 50:20 — *ye thought evil against me; but Elohim (God) meant it unto good... to save much people alive.* — Joseph humbled by betrayal yet raised to save, the example Benjamin names, "as was Joseph my brother."$n$),
(60381, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 136, 5, $n$The good mind hath not two tongues, of blessing and of cursing, of contumely and 'of honour', of sorrow and of joy, of quietness and of confusion, of hypocrisy and of truth, [of poverty and of wealth]; but it hath one 'disposition', uncorrupt and pure, concerning all men.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 5, 37, $n$Matt 5:37 — *But let your communication be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more than these cometh of evil.* — the single, guileless speech of the uncorrupt mind.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:37 — *But let your communication be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more than these cometh of evil.* — the single, guileless speech of the uncorrupt mind.$n$, 14858, $n$Matt 5:37 — *But let your communication be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more than these cometh of evil.* — the single, guileless speech of the uncorrupt mind.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:37 — *But let your communication be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more than these cometh of evil.* — the single, guileless speech of the uncorrupt mind.$n$),
(60382, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 136, 3, $n$He delighteth not in pleasure, '[he grieveth not his neighbour], he sateth not himself with luxuries, he erreth not in the uplifting of the eyes', for Yahuah (Lord) is his portion.$n$, 'canon', 'psalms', 73, 26, $n$Ps 73:26 — *My flesh and my heart faileth: but Elohim (God) is the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.* — the Lord as the good man's portion, that he covets no corruptible thing.$n$, $n$Psalm 73:26 — *My flesh and my heart faileth: but Elohim (God) is the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.* — the Lord as the good man's portion, that he covets no corruptible thing.$n$, 14858, $n$Ps 73:26 — *My flesh and my heart faileth: but Elohim (God) is the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.* — the Lord as the good man's portion, that he covets no corruptible thing.$n$, $n$Psalm 73:26 — *My flesh and my heart faileth: but Elohim (God) is the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.* — the Lord as the good man's portion, that he covets no corruptible thing.$n$),
(60385, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 137, 5, $n$Because for ever those who are like unto Cain 'in envy and hatred of brethren', shall be punished with the same judgment'.$n$, 'canon', '1-john', 3, 15, $n$1 Jn 3:15 — *Whosoever hateth his brother is a murderer: and ye know that no murderer hath eternal life abiding in him.* — the judgment on "those who are like unto Cain in envy and hatred of brethren."$n$, $n$1 John 3:15 — *Whosoever hateth his brother is a murderer: and ye know that no murderer hath eternal life abiding in him.* — the judgment on "those who are like unto Cain in envy and hatred of brethren."$n$, 14859, $n$1 Jn 3:15 — *Whosoever hateth his brother is a murderer: and ye know that no murderer hath eternal life abiding in him.* — the judgment on "those who are like unto Cain in envy and hatred of brethren."$n$, $n$1 John 3:15 — *Whosoever hateth his brother is a murderer: and ye know that no murderer hath eternal life abiding in him.* — the judgment on "those who are like unto Cain in envy and hatred of brethren."$n$),
(60386, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 137, 5, $n$Because for ever those who are like unto Cain 'in envy and hatred of brethren', shall be punished with the same judgment'.$n$, 'canon', '1-john', 3, 12, $n$1 Jn 3:12 — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* — the Cain-pattern of envy and brother-hatred the testament warns against.$n$, $n$1 John 3:12 — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* — the Cain-pattern of envy and brother-hatred the testament warns against.$n$, 14859, $n$1 Jn 3:12 — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* — the Cain-pattern of envy and brother-hatred the testament warns against.$n$, $n$1 John 3:12 — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* — the Cain-pattern of envy and brother-hatred the testament warns against.$n$),
(60387, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 137, 4, $n$And when he was two hundred years old he began to suffer, and in the nine-hundredth year he was destroyed. For on account of Abel, his brother, with all the evils was he judged, but Lamech with seventy times seven.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 4, 24, $n$Gen 4:24 — *If Cain shall be avenged sevenfold, truly Lamech seventy and sevenfold.* — the very measure the testament names, "but Lamech with seventy times seven."$n$, $n$Genesis 4:24 — *If Cain shall be avenged sevenfold, truly Lamech seventy and sevenfold.* — the very measure the testament names, "but Lamech with seventy times seven."$n$, 14859, $n$Gen 4:24 — *If Cain shall be avenged sevenfold, truly Lamech seventy and sevenfold.* — the very measure the testament names, "but Lamech with seventy times seven."$n$, $n$Genesis 4:24 — *If Cain shall be avenged sevenfold, truly Lamech seventy and sevenfold.* — the very measure the testament names, "but Lamech with seventy times seven."$n$),
(60388, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 137, 3, $n$Therefore was Cain also delivered over to seven vengeances by Elohim (God), for in every hundred years Yahuah (Lord) brought one plague upon him.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 4, 15, $n$Gen 4:15 — *whosoever slayeth Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him sevenfold.* — the sevenfold vengeance Benjamin recalls, "Cain also delivered over to seven vengeances."$n$, $n$Genesis 4:15 — *whosoever slayeth Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him sevenfold.* — the sevenfold vengeance Benjamin recalls, "Cain also delivered over to seven vengeances."$n$, 14859, $n$Gen 4:15 — *whosoever slayeth Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him sevenfold.* — the sevenfold vengeance Benjamin recalls, "Cain also delivered over to seven vengeances."$n$, $n$Genesis 4:15 — *whosoever slayeth Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him sevenfold.* — the sevenfold vengeance Benjamin recalls, "Cain also delivered over to seven vengeances."$n$),
(60389, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 138, 2, $n$He that hath a pure mind in love, looketh not after a woman with a view to fornication; for he hath no defilement in his heart, because the Spirit of Elohim (God) resteth upon him.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 5, 8, $n$Matt 5:8 — *Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see Elohim (God).* — the purity of heart on which the Spirit of God rests.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:8 — *Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see Elohim (God).* — the purity of heart on which the Spirit of God rests.$n$, 14860, $n$Matt 5:8 — *Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see Elohim (God).* — the purity of heart on which the Spirit of God rests.$n$, $n$Matthew 5:8 — *Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see Elohim (God).* — the purity of heart on which the Spirit of God rests.$n$),
(60390, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 138, 2, $n$He that hath a pure mind in love, looketh not after a woman with a view to fornication; for he hath no defilement in his heart, because the Spirit of Elohim (God) resteth upon him.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 5, 28, $n$Matt 5:28 — *whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her hath committed adultery with her already in his heart.* — the very looking the pure mind refuses, "looketh not after a woman with a view to fornication."$n$, $n$Matthew 5:28 — *whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her hath committed adultery with her already in his heart.* — the very looking the pure mind refuses, "looketh not after a woman with a view to fornication."$n$, 14860, $n$Matt 5:28 — *whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her hath committed adultery with her already in his heart.* — the very looking the pure mind refuses, "looketh not after a woman with a view to fornication."$n$, $n$Matthew 5:28 — *whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her hath committed adultery with her already in his heart.* — the very looking the pure mind refuses, "looketh not after a woman with a view to fornication."$n$),
(60395, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 139, 4, $n$And the veil of the temple shall be rent, and the Spirit of Elohim (God) shall pass on to the Gentiles as fire poured forth.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 27, 51, $n$Matt 27:51 — *And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom.* — the very rending of the veil Benjamin prophesies, "the veil of the temple shall be rent."$n$, $n$Matthew 27:51 — *And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom.* — the very rending of the veil Benjamin prophesies, "the veil of the temple shall be rent."$n$, 14863, $n$Matt 27:51 — *And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom.* — the very rending of the veil Benjamin prophesies, "the veil of the temple shall be rent."$n$, $n$Matthew 27:51 — *And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom.* — the very rending of the veil Benjamin prophesies, "the veil of the temple shall be rent."$n$),
(60396, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 139, 3, $n$[And He shall enter into the [first] temple, and there shall Yahuah (Lord) be treated with outrage, and He shall be lifted up upon a tree.$n$, 'canon', 'galatians', 3, 13, $n$Gal 3:13 — *Messiah (Christ) hath redeemed us from the curse of the law, being made a curse for us: for it is written, Cursed is every one that hangeth on a tree.* — the Anointed lifted up upon a tree, bearing the curse for the salvation Benjamin foresees.$n$, $n$Galatians 3:13 — *Messiah (Christ) hath redeemed us from the curse of the law, being made a curse for us: for it is written, Cursed is every one that hangeth on a tree.* — the Anointed lifted up upon a tree, bearing the curse for the salvation Benjamin foresees.$n$, 14863, $n$Gal 3:13 — *Messiah (Christ) hath redeemed us from the curse of the law, being made a curse for us: for it is written, Cursed is every one that hangeth on a tree.* — the Anointed lifted up upon a tree, bearing the curse for the salvation Benjamin foresees.$n$, $n$Galatians 3:13 — *Messiah (Christ) hath redeemed us from the curse of the law, being made a curse for us: for it is written, Cursed is every one that hangeth on a tree.* — the Anointed lifted up upon a tree, bearing the curse for the salvation Benjamin foresees.$n$),
(60397, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 139, 3, $n$[And He shall enter into the [first] temple, and there shall Yahuah (Lord) be treated with outrage, and He shall be lifted up upon a tree.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 21, 23, $n$Deut 21:23 — *for he that is hanged is accursed of Elohim (God)* — the Torah's word on the one hanged on a tree, the curse the lifted-up Lord bears.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 21:23 — *for he that is hanged is accursed of Elohim (God)* — the Torah's word on the one hanged on a tree, the curse the lifted-up Lord bears.$n$, 14863, $n$Deut 21:23 — *for he that is hanged is accursed of Elohim (God)* — the Torah's word on the one hanged on a tree, the curse the lifted-up Lord bears.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 21:23 — *for he that is hanged is accursed of Elohim (God)* — the Torah's word on the one hanged on a tree, the curse the lifted-up Lord bears.$n$),
(60398, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 139, 2, $n$Nevertheless the temple of Elohim (God) shall be in your portion, and the last (temple) shall be more glorious than the first. And the twelve tribes shall be gathered together there, and all the Gentiles, until the El Elyon (Most High) shall send forth His salvation in the visitation of an 'only-begotten prophet'.$n$, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 22, $n$Ezek 37:22 — *And I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* — the twelve tribes gathered together as one, the two-house reunion.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *And I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* — the twelve tribes gathered together as one, the two-house reunion.$n$, 14862, $n$Ezek 37:22 — *And I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* — the twelve tribes gathered together as one, the two-house reunion.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *And I will make them one nation in the land... and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* — the twelve tribes gathered together as one, the two-house reunion.$n$),
(60399, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 139, 2, $n$Nevertheless the temple of Elohim (God) shall be in your portion, and the last (temple) shall be more glorious than the first. And the twelve tribes shall be gathered together there, and all the Gentiles, until the El Elyon (Most High) shall send forth His salvation in the visitation of an 'only-begotten prophet'.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 2, 2, $n$Isa 2:2 — *And it shall come to pass in the last days, that the mountain of the LORD'S house shall be established in the top of the mountains... and all nations shall flow unto it.* — the gathering of the tribes and all the Gentiles to the house of God.$n$, $n$Isaiah 2:2 — *And it shall come to pass in the last days, that the mountain of the LORD'S house shall be established in the top of the mountains... and all nations shall flow unto it.* — the gathering of the tribes and all the Gentiles to the house of God.$n$, 14862, $n$Isa 2:2 — *And it shall come to pass in the last days, that the mountain of the LORD'S house shall be established in the top of the mountains... and all nations shall flow unto it.* — the gathering of the tribes and all the Gentiles to the house of God.$n$, $n$Isaiah 2:2 — *And it shall come to pass in the last days, that the mountain of the LORD'S house shall be established in the top of the mountains... and all nations shall flow unto it.* — the gathering of the tribes and all the Gentiles to the house of God.$n$),
(60404, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 140, 10, $n$And He shall convict Yashar'el (Israel) through the chosen ones of the Gentiles, even as he reproved Esau through the Madianites, who deceived their brethren, [so that they fell into fornication, and idolatry; and they were alienated from Elohim (God),] becoming therefore children in the portion of them that fear Yahuah (Lord).$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 11, 25, $n$Rom 11:25 — *blindness in part is happened to Yashar'el (Israel), until the fulness of the Gentiles be come in.* — the chosen Gentiles brought in to convict and gather Israel.$n$, $n$Romans 11:25 — *blindness in part is happened to Yashar'el (Israel), until the fulness of the Gentiles be come in.* — the chosen Gentiles brought in to convict and gather Israel.$n$, 14868, $n$Rom 11:25 — *blindness in part is happened to Yashar'el (Israel), until the fulness of the Gentiles be come in.* — the chosen Gentiles brought in to convict and gather Israel.$n$, $n$Romans 11:25 — *blindness in part is happened to Yashar'el (Israel), until the fulness of the Gentiles be come in.* — the chosen Gentiles brought in to convict and gather Israel.$n$),
(60406, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 140, 10, $n$And He shall convict Yashar'el (Israel) through the chosen ones of the Gentiles, even as he reproved Esau through the Madianites, who deceived their brethren, [so that they fell into fornication, and idolatry; and they were alienated from Elohim (God),] becoming therefore children in the portion of them that fear Yahuah (Lord).$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 11, 11, $n$Rom 11:11 — *through their fall salvation is come unto the Gentiles, for to provoke them to jealousy.* — Israel convicted and provoked through the believing Gentiles, exactly as Benjamin foresees.$n$, $n$Romans 11:11 — *through their fall salvation is come unto the Gentiles, for to provoke them to jealousy.* — Israel convicted and provoked through the believing Gentiles, exactly as Benjamin foresees.$n$, 14868, $n$Rom 11:11 — *through their fall salvation is come unto the Gentiles, for to provoke them to jealousy.* — Israel convicted and provoked through the believing Gentiles, exactly as Benjamin foresees.$n$, $n$Romans 11:11 — *through their fall salvation is come unto the Gentiles, for to provoke them to jealousy.* — Israel convicted and provoked through the believing Gentiles, exactly as Benjamin foresees.$n$),
(60407, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 140, 8, $n$Then also all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame. And Yahuah (Lord) shall judge Yashar'el (Israel) first, for their unrighteousness; [for when He appeared as Elohim (God) in the flesh to deliver them they believed Him not].$n$, 'canon', 'revelation', 20, 12, $n$Rev 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God)... and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* — all men risen and judged, as Benjamin foresees.$n$, $n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God)... and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* — all men risen and judged, as Benjamin foresees.$n$, 14867, $n$Rev 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God)... and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* — all men risen and judged, as Benjamin foresees.$n$, $n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God)... and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* — all men risen and judged, as Benjamin foresees.$n$),
(60409, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 140, 8, $n$Then also all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame. And Yahuah (Lord) shall judge Yashar'el (Israel) first, for their unrighteousness; [for when He appeared as Elohim (God) in the flesh to deliver them they believed Him not].$n$, 'canon', 'daniel', 12, 2, $n$Dan 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* — the very words behind "all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame."$n$, $n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* — the very words behind "all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame."$n$, 14867, $n$Dan 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* — the very words behind "all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame."$n$, $n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* — the very words behind "all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame."$n$),
(60410, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 140, 6, $n$'And' then shall ye see Enoch, Noah, and Shem, and Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, rising on the right hand in gladness.$n$, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 12, $n$Ezek 37:12 — *Behold, O my people, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves.* — the raising of Israel and her fathers from the grave.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:12 — *Behold, O my people, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves.* — the raising of Israel and her fathers from the grave.$n$, 14866, $n$Ezek 37:12 — *Behold, O my people, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves.* — the raising of Israel and her fathers from the grave.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:12 — *Behold, O my people, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves.* — the raising of Israel and her fathers from the grave.$n$),
(60411, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 140, 7, $n$Then shall we also rise, each one over our tribe, worshipping the King of heaven, [who appeared upon earth in the form of a man in humility. And as many as believe on Him on the earth shall rejoice with Him].$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 19, 28, $n$Matt 19:28 — *ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel).* — the twelve set "each one over our tribe," as Benjamin foresees.$n$, $n$Matthew 19:28 — *ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel).* — the twelve set "each one over our tribe," as Benjamin foresees.$n$, 14866, $n$Matt 19:28 — *ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel).* — the twelve set "each one over our tribe," as Benjamin foresees.$n$, $n$Matthew 19:28 — *ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel).* — the twelve set "each one over our tribe," as Benjamin foresees.$n$),
(60412, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 140, 6, $n$'And' then shall ye see Enoch, Noah, and Shem, and Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, rising on the right hand in gladness.$n$, 'canon', 'matthew', 22, 32, $n$Matt 22:32 — *I am the Elohim (God) of Abraham, and the Elohim (God) of Isaac, and the Elohim (God) of Jacob? Elohim (God) is not the Elohim (God) of the dead, but of the living.* — the fathers who live to God, who Benjamin sees "rising on the right hand in gladness."$n$, $n$Matthew 22:32 — *I am the Elohim (God) of Abraham, and the Elohim (God) of Isaac, and the Elohim (God) of Jacob? Elohim (God) is not the Elohim (God) of the dead, but of the living.* — the fathers who live to God, who Benjamin sees "rising on the right hand in gladness."$n$, 14866, $n$Matt 22:32 — *I am the Elohim (God) of Abraham, and the Elohim (God) of Isaac, and the Elohim (God) of Jacob? Elohim (God) is not the Elohim (God) of the dead, but of the living.* — the fathers who live to God, who Benjamin sees "rising on the right hand in gladness."$n$, $n$Matthew 22:32 — *I am the Elohim (God) of Abraham, and the Elohim (God) of Isaac, and the Elohim (God) of Jacob? Elohim (God) is not the Elohim (God) of the dead, but of the living.* — the fathers who live to God, who Benjamin sees "rising on the right hand in gladness."$n$),
(60414, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 140, 5, $n$For all these things they gave us for an inheritance, saying: Keep the commandments of Elohim (God), until Yahuah (Lord) shall reveal His salvation to all Gentiles.$n$, 'canon', 'isaiah', 49, 6, $n$Isa 49:6 — *I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.* — the salvation revealed "to all Gentiles" that the fathers' charge waits for.$n$, $n$Isaiah 49:6 — *I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.* — the salvation revealed "to all Gentiles" that the fathers' charge waits for.$n$, 14865, $n$Isa 49:6 — *I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.* — the salvation revealed "to all Gentiles" that the fathers' charge waits for.$n$, $n$Isaiah 49:6 — *I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.* — the salvation revealed "to all Gentiles" that the fathers' charge waits for.$n$),
(60415, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 140, 3, $n$Do ye, therefore, truth each one to his neighbour, and keep the law of Yahuah (Lord) and His commandments.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 16, $n$Deut 30:16 — *to love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to walk in his ways, and to keep his commandments and his statutes and his judgments, that thou mayest live.* — the very keeping Benjamin leaves "instead of inheritance."$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:16 — *to love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to walk in his ways, and to keep his commandments and his statutes and his judgments, that thou mayest live.* — the very keeping Benjamin leaves "instead of inheritance."$n$, 14865, $n$Deut 30:16 — *to love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to walk in his ways, and to keep his commandments and his statutes and his judgments, that thou mayest live.* — the very keeping Benjamin leaves "instead of inheritance."$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:16 — *to love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), to walk in his ways, and to keep his commandments and his statutes and his judgments, that thou mayest live.* — the very keeping Benjamin leaves "instead of inheritance."$n$),
(60417, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 141, 2, $n$And there shall arise in the latter days] one beloved of Yahuah (Lord), [of the tribe of Yahudah (Judah) and Levi], a doer of His good pleasure in his mouth, [with new knowledge enlightening the Gentiles].$n$, 'canon', 'romans', 11, 1, $n$Rom 11:1 — *For I also am an Israelite, of the seed of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin.* — the apostle naming his own tribe, the beloved arisen in the latter days.$n$, $n$Romans 11:1 — *For I also am an Israelite, of the seed of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin.* — the apostle naming his own tribe, the beloved arisen in the latter days.$n$, 14870, $n$Rom 11:1 — *For I also am an Israelite, of the seed of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin.* — the apostle naming his own tribe, the beloved arisen in the latter days.$n$, $n$Romans 11:1 — *For I also am an Israelite, of the seed of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin.* — the apostle naming his own tribe, the beloved arisen in the latter days.$n$),
(60419, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 141, 2, $n$And there shall arise in the latter days] one beloved of Yahuah (Lord), [of the tribe of Yahudah (Judah) and Levi], a doer of His good pleasure in his mouth, [with new knowledge enlightening the Gentiles].$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 33, 12, $n$Deut 33:12 — *The beloved of Yahuah (LORD) shall dwell in safety by him; and Yahuah (LORD) shall cover him all the day long.* — the "one beloved of Yahuah" of Benjamin's tribe, Moses' own blessing on Benjamin.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 33:12 — *The beloved of Yahuah (LORD) shall dwell in safety by him; and Yahuah (LORD) shall cover him all the day long.* — the "one beloved of Yahuah" of Benjamin's tribe, Moses' own blessing on Benjamin.$n$, 14870, $n$Deut 33:12 — *The beloved of Yahuah (LORD) shall dwell in safety by him; and Yahuah (LORD) shall cover him all the day long.* — the "one beloved of Yahuah" of Benjamin's tribe, Moses' own blessing on Benjamin.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 33:12 — *The beloved of Yahuah (LORD) shall dwell in safety by him; and Yahuah (LORD) shall cover him all the day long.* — the "one beloved of Yahuah" of Benjamin's tribe, Moses' own blessing on Benjamin.$n$),
(60420, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 141, 1, $n$If ye 'therefore, my children', walk in holiness 'according to the commandments of the Lord', ye shall again dwell securely with me, and all Yashar'el (Israel) shall be gathered unto Yahuah (Lord). And I shall no longer be called a ravening wolf on account of your ravages, but [a worker of Yahuah (Lord) distributing food to them that work what is good.$n$, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 21, $n$Ezek 37:21 — *Behold, I will take the children of Yashar'el (Israel) from among the heathen... and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land.* — the ingathering that makes the dispersed dwell securely again.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:21 — *Behold, I will take the children of Yashar'el (Israel) from among the heathen... and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land.* — the ingathering that makes the dispersed dwell securely again.$n$, 14869, $n$Ezek 37:21 — *Behold, I will take the children of Yashar'el (Israel) from among the heathen... and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land.* — the ingathering that makes the dispersed dwell securely again.$n$, $n$Ezekiel 37:21 — *Behold, I will take the children of Yashar'el (Israel) from among the heathen... and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land.* — the ingathering that makes the dispersed dwell securely again.$n$),
(60421, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 141, 1, $n$If ye 'therefore, my children', walk in holiness 'according to the commandments of the Lord', ye shall again dwell securely with me, and all Yashar'el (Israel) shall be gathered unto Yahuah (Lord). And I shall no longer be called a ravening wolf on account of your ravages, but [a worker of Yahuah (Lord) distributing food to them that work what is good.$n$, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 4, $n$Deut 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee.* — the gathering of "all Yashar'el (Israel) shall be gathered unto Yahuah (Lord)" Benjamin foresees.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee.* — the gathering of "all Yashar'el (Israel) shall be gathered unto Yahuah (Lord)" Benjamin foresees.$n$, 14869, $n$Deut 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee.* — the gathering of "all Yashar'el (Israel) shall be gathered unto Yahuah (Lord)" Benjamin foresees.$n$, $n$Deuteronomy 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee.* — the gathering of "all Yashar'el (Israel) shall be gathered unto Yahuah (Lord)" Benjamin foresees.$n$),
(60422, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 141, 1, $n$If ye 'therefore, my children', walk in holiness 'according to the commandments of the Lord', ye shall again dwell securely with me, and all Yashar'el (Israel) shall be gathered unto Yahuah (Lord). And I shall no longer be called a ravening wolf on account of your ravages, but [a worker of Yahuah (Lord) distributing food to them that work what is good.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 49, 27, $n$Gen 49:27 — *Benjamin shall ravin as a wolf: in the morning he shall devour the prey, and at night he shall divide the spoil.* — the very wolf Benjamin says he shall "no longer be called."$n$, $n$Genesis 49:27 — *Benjamin shall ravin as a wolf: in the morning he shall devour the prey, and at night he shall divide the spoil.* — the very wolf Benjamin says he shall "no longer be called."$n$, 14869, $n$Gen 49:27 — *Benjamin shall ravin as a wolf: in the morning he shall devour the prey, and at night he shall divide the spoil.* — the very wolf Benjamin says he shall "no longer be called."$n$, $n$Genesis 49:27 — *Benjamin shall ravin as a wolf: in the morning he shall devour the prey, and at night he shall divide the spoil.* — the very wolf Benjamin says he shall "no longer be called."$n$),
(60424, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 142, 3, $n$And in the ninety-first year from the entrance of the children of Yashar'el (Israel) into Egypt, they and their brethren brought up the bones of their fathers secretly during the Canaanitish war; and they buried them in Hebron, by the feet of their fathers.$n$, 'canon', 'exodus', 13, 19, $n$Exod 13:19 — *And Moses took the bones of Joseph with him.* — the keeping of the fathers' oath, the bones carried up out of Egypt as Benjamin commands.$n$, $n$Exodus 13:19 — *And Moses took the bones of Joseph with him.* — the keeping of the fathers' oath, the bones carried up out of Egypt as Benjamin commands.$n$, 14871, $n$Exod 13:19 — *And Moses took the bones of Joseph with him.* — the keeping of the fathers' oath, the bones carried up out of Egypt as Benjamin commands.$n$, $n$Exodus 13:19 — *And Moses took the bones of Joseph with him.* — the keeping of the fathers' oath, the bones carried up out of Egypt as Benjamin commands.$n$),
(60425, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 142, 1, $n$And when he finished his words, he said: I command you, my children, carry up my bones out of Egypt, and bury me at Hebron, near my fathers.$n$, 'canon', 'genesis', 50, 25, $n$Gen 50:25 — *And Joseph took an oath of the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.* — the same oath Benjamin lays on his sons, "carry up my bones out of Egypt."$n$, $n$Genesis 50:25 — *And Joseph took an oath of the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.* — the same oath Benjamin lays on his sons, "carry up my bones out of Egypt."$n$, 14871, $n$Gen 50:25 — *And Joseph took an oath of the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.* — the same oath Benjamin lays on his sons, "carry up my bones out of Egypt."$n$, $n$Genesis 50:25 — *And Joseph took an oath of the children of Yashar'el (Israel), saying, Elohim (God) will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.* — the same oath Benjamin lays on his sons, "carry up my bones out of Egypt."$n$);
